\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BOOKSTORE WITH A PURPOSE OFFERING VOCATIONAL TRAINING PROGRAM\b0\par\par\uc2 1,461 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECRETARY OF STATE IN UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 BLINKEN, UKRAINE, AID, KULEBA, ZELENSKYY\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, ESCAPE, BIVENS, CAVALCANTE, SIGHTINGS, COMMUNITY\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE, ALERTS, TEMPERATURES, SCHOOLS\par \par \uc2 RAINFALL, FLOODING, EUROPE, STIVERSON\par \par \uc2 TARRIO, SENTENCED, RIOT, CAPITOL, KELLY\par \par \uc2 MCCONNELL, HEALTH, PHYSICIAN, CONGRESS, TRANSPARENCY\par \par \uc2 PAXTON, IMPEACHMENT, TRIAL, TEXAS, MURR, DONOR, JENKINS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, COVID, HEALTH, WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 US OPEN, SEMIFINALS, SHELTON, DJOKOVIC, GAUFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, CONVICTED, TRIAL, HILL, JURY, WILSON, BOOK\par \par \uc2 GRIFFIN, HARPOOTLIAN, MURDER, JURORS, TRIAL, EVIDENCE\par \par \uc2 JONAS, TURNER, DIVORCE, CHILDREN, TRACY\par \par \uc2 MANNING, "MANNINGCAST", WITHERSPOON, BRADY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE THREAT\par \par \uc2 CAVALCANTE, FUGITIVE, MURDER, ESCAPE, PRISON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT MANHUNT FOR ESCAPED KILLER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTHORITIES STEP UP THEIR EFFORTS\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, HEAT WAVE, RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD HEAT WAVE SPREADING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 88 MILLION ON ALERT FROM CA TO MA\par \par \uc2 MODERNA, BOOSTER, COVID, RESULTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MODERNA REPORTS RESULTS OF UPDATED COVID BOOSTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DATA SHOWS STRONG IMMUNE RESPONSE\par \par \uc2 FRANKE, ARRESTED, CHILD ABUSE, INFLUENCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARENTING INFLUENCER ARRESTED FOR CHILD ABUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUSBAND'S ATTORNEY TELLS HIS CLIENT'S SIDE\par \par \uc2 STALKERWARE, PHONE, TRACKING, ALERT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE RISE OF STALKERWARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROGRAMS THAT COULD BE TRACKING YOUR PHONE\par \par \uc2 CREDIT CARD, DEBT, ADVICE, FINANCES, STREAKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE AMERICANS DEFAULTING ON CREDIT CARDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPERT ADVICE ON WHAT TO KNOW & DO\par \par \uc2 STUBBS, TENNIS, COACH, KING, AMBUSH TENNIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RENNAE STUBBS' COURTSIDE AMBUSH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SURPRISING YOUNG PLAYERS WITH BILLIE JEAN KING\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM "A HAUNTING IN VENICE"\par \par \uc2 "TAMRON HALL", TALK SHOW, HOST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAMRON HALL LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\par \par \uc2 BOOKSTORE, VOCATIONAL TRAINING, YOUTH, GIBSON, ZIMILES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOOKSTORE WITH A PURPOSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFERING VOCATIONAL TRAINING PROGRAM\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to take a look now at a small, independent bookstore that doesn't expand minds and imagination, it expands the world for people with unique abilities. Our friends, Kate and Charlie Gibson, explore their mission.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 On our must-listen podcast, "The Bookcase with Kate and Charlie," in addition to speaking with some of the finest authors of the day, most weeks we also speak with an independent bookseller somewhere around the country.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 Because independent bookstores are important. So, that brought us to Maplewood, New Jersey and a store called Words, where the story behind the store is just as compelling as the stories that are in the bookstore shelves. Jonah and Ellen Zimiles started this store not just to sell books but with a larger purpose in mind. So, I say you started the bookstore with a purpose. Why?\par \par \uc2 ELLEN ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 So we had, at that time, a 12-year-old with autism, and we wanted to come up with some sort of vocational program, something to do for people to sort of both give him something and give others in the community something.\par \par \uc2 JONAH ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 The idea we came up with was to run this vocational training program with the idea of hoping that they could then branch out and get jobs, which some people have done, and, or at least get exposure to working.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 To date they have implied more than 150 young people with autism. Why do you think bookselling lends itself so well to vocational training of this kind?\par \par \uc2 ELLEN ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 A bookstore is like any other store, right, there are things to do that have nothing to do with books, some things that have everything to do with books. We had down here, earlier today, two young men who were putting stickers on the bags so that they say our name, and you need that for any kind of store, whether it's a bookstore or otherwise. They were putting out the chairs, because we have events. They have profound autism and still be able to do that and feel confidence and feel like you're doing something that's of value.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 But Jonah and Ellen didn't stop there. They became the first tenants of Lifetown, 20 minutes away, in Livingston, New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE LIFETOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIMULATED SMALL TOWN TEACHING LIFE SKILLS TO PEOPLE FACING DIFFERENT CHALLENGES\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 Lifetown is a 50,000-square-foot warehouse where people with autism and other challenges can come to learn how to deal with activities that most of us would take for granted.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 Inside, there is a simulated small town, a main street teaching Lifetown visitors how to deal with traffic lights and crosswalks, as well as 15 working small stores, where visitors learn to deal with volunteer shopkeepers.\par \par \uc2 JONAH ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 Well, first, they often they come in, and they've given some money out, and then they can use these dollars in all the shops around Lifetown.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 Among the stores, a movie theater, complete with popcorn for sale, a grocery. I can't help but notice that it is well stocked with snacks.\par \par \uc2 ELLEN ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 A health center.\par \par \uc2 JONAH ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 They have the opportunity to go up and down, to sit, see what it is to play with things.\par \par \uc2 ELLEN ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 Play with teeth.\par \par \uc2 JONAH ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 Play with teeth and say, "Gee, this isn't that scary."\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 A beauty salon and, of course, a satellite Words bookstore.\par \par \uc2 JONAH ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 They get to go in the stores and learn about each of the different stores and their functions and to practice reading skills and math skills and things like that, and get to learn how to shop and buy things in stores. Lifetown supports people with all kinds of disabilities so that there are people with physical disabilities, where they have very different challenges than people with autism or other intellectual disabilities.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 In Lifetown, there's also a gym, an aquatic center, a sand room, a sensory room where, if overstimulated, kids can come to calm down. Those with autism are very sensitive to loud noises, so each of these rooms, even the movie theater, is adapted to keep sound levels down. So, it makes kids comfortable with the sensory experience of going to the movie.\par \par \uc2 JONAH ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 Exactly and what the behavior is and what the expectations are, how you go in, you pick your seat.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 Twenty-seven hundred donors contributed more than $18 million to create this Lifetown building four years ago. How many kids have experienced Lifetown?\par \par \uc2 RABBI ZALMAN GROSSBAUM (LIFETOWN INC.)\par \par \uc2 To date, we've had over 30,000 individuals participate in programs here. Next year, we'll probably have 30,000, 40,000 individuals here, both from the schools and from the community at large. It's really something unique, an incredible experience. We want to make it possible for everybody.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 The important thing is for those who come to Lifetown, there are no outsiders here. There's no behavior unexpected or unaccepted, and small victories, learning how to make a doctor's appointment, how to buy groceries, how to navigate a stop light, how to handle money, are all to be celebrated. While many school groups come through for an introductory visit, anyone can come back again and again, and they do. What is the ultimate goal?\par \par \uc2 JONAH ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 I think it's to normalize them in the community, to make them feel fully integrated and fully part of the community.\par \par \uc2 ELLEN ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 This is a place where everyone, as you're younger and grow, and as you're older, that you are accepted, that you feel comfortable, that you know how to do things. You feel competent in your own abilities. But that's what this is trying to teach people.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 So, there's a dual purpose. It gets them more comfortable with the world, and it gets the world more comfortable to them.\par \par \uc2 ELLEN ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 A hundred percent.\par \par \uc2 JONAH ZIMILES (WORDS)\par \par \uc2 Beautifully said.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 We are so grateful for the Zimiles for introducing us to Lifetown, wonderful life lessons learned in a totally welcoming environment.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON ("THE BOOK CASE")\par \par \uc2 Society has a lot to learn about those who come to Lifetown, and those who come to Lifetown do learn a lot about how to deal with society.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So great to see that from Charlie and Kate. We love their podcast. The latest episode of "The Book Case" drops tomorrow. Kate and Charlie chat with "The River We Remember" author, William Kent Krueger. And you can check out the QR code on your screen. It takes you right to the page.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230914ej960000t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AUTO WORKERS THREATEN WALKOUT NEARLY 150,000 WORKERS DEMANDING PAY RAISE, PENSIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 592 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEPTEMBER SCORCHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEAR RECORD HIGH TEMPERATURES THIS WEEK FOR MILLIONS\par \par \uc2 BURNING MAN, FLOODING, STRANDED, DIPLO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ESCAPE FROM "BURNING MAN"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS FINALLY LEAVE MUD-SWAMPED FESTIVAL GROUNDS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, COVID-19\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST LADY TESTS POSITIVE FOR COVID-19\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHITE HOUSE: JILL BIDEN "EXPERIENCING ONLY MILD SYMPTOMS"\par \par \uc2 CAVALCANTE, SEARCH, BIVINS, DOMAL, RYAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT MANHUNT FOR ESCAPED MURDERER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE CONFIRM AT LEAST FOUR SIGHTINGS OF KILLER ON THE LOOSE\par \par \uc2 MARTIN, FAIN, BIDEN, PROTEST, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , PENSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTO WORKERS THREATEN WALKOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEARLY 150,000 WORKERS DEMANDING PAY RAISE, PENSIONS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to get the latest now on the looming strike in the auto industry. 150,000 workers poised to walkout. That could cost the big three automakers billions, send shockwaves through the broader economy. Chief business correspondent Rebecca Jarvis tracking it all. Good morning, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Good morning, George. And a potential large impact here. The hard deadline is 11:59 PM on September 14th. The head of \uc2 UAW\uc2  says, if the automakers, including GM, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and Ford, do not meet their demands, they will strike shutting down production across the country.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, a strike deadline looming as the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  clash with the big three automakers. The union demanding a 46% pay raise, a 32-hour work week and a return of traditional pensions. Automakers Ford, GM and \uc2 Jeep\uc2  maker \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  say those demands are unrealistic. But newly elected union president, Shawn Fain, has vowed to keep pushing with the current contract expiring in just nine days.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT UNITED AUTO WORKERS)\par \par \uc2 When workers get fair and equitable justice, and fair and equitable wages and benefits, they move the economy. A CEO making $29 million doesn't move this economy.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fain calling out corporate greed as strikes and threats of strikes are growing in other industries, too. From Hollywood...\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Hey, hey. Ho, ho. Corporate greed has got to go.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \u8230\'20\'26to companies like UPS.\par \par \uc2 STANFORD MARTIN (\uc2 STELLANTIS\uc2  EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 Everything is not going to be the way it was. Ain't going to be a status quo.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) All this as car manufacturers compete with \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and transition to producing more electric vehicles, which require fewer workers to assemble. President Biden, who bills himself as a pro-union president, downplaying the threat.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 No, I'm not worried about a strike until it happens.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fain's response?\par \par \uc2 SHAWN FAIN (PRESIDENT UNITED AUTO WORKERS)\par \par \uc2 Well, I'm shocked by that reaction. You know, he must know something we don't know. Our intent is not to strike, our intent is to get a fair agreement.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The last time the \uc2 UAW\uc2  went on strike, it was 2019. It lasted 42 days, and it was specifically against \uc2 General Motors\uc2 . That cost the automaker $3.6 billion. This time, economists estimate that a strike lasting just ten days would cost the US economy at least $5 billion. And it would have ripple effects, everything from the manufacturers to dealerships, like this one behind me, to consumers who would pay a higher price for their cars because supplies are already constrained. George?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRIKE COULD SEND ALREADY HIGH CAR PRICES EVEN HIGHER\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Rebecca, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230913ej9500006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAJOR AUTO WORKERS STRIKE LOOMS NEARLY 150,000 COULD WALK OFF JOB IN LESS THAN TWO WEEKS\b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 September 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRAPPED IN THE MUD\par \par \uc2 BURNING MAN, MUD, RAINS, SHELTER, TRAPPED, DESERT\par \par \uc2 TRAPPED, RAINS, MUD, BURNING MAN\par \par \uc2 LABOR DAY, TRAVEL, AIRPORTS, ROADS, TSA, SMITH\par \par \uc2 RIP CURRENTS, BEACHES, SAFETY\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SEARCH, RYAN, CAVALCANTE, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 CAMPAIGN, REPUBLICANS, RAMASWAMY, POLL, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 AUTO WORKERS, STRIKE, NEGOTIATIONS, AUTOMAKERS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, George thank you. We turn now to the looming possibility of a major auto industry strike. Nearly 150,000 workers could walk off the job in less than two weeks, and there's no sign of a deal in sight. Phil Lipof has more. Good morning, Phil.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR AUTO WORKERS STRIKE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEARLY 150,000 COULD WALK OFF JOB IN LESS THAN TWO WEEKS\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Rebecca. This morning the clock is ticking and that strike is looming as the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  and Detroit's three automakers still seem pretty far from contract agreements. Hundreds of thousands of autoworker ready to strike. Two of the big sticking points, higher wages and improved benefits.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Detroit's big three auto makers Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , will take a huge financial hit if this strike happens. Also having a ripple effect on the broader US economy. Only adding to a summer of strikes, most notably the writers guild and actors in Hollywood.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Those strikes are affecting fall lineups and the box office. Tens of thousands of writers and actors have been out of work now for months. The auto workers deadline for a strike, by the way, is September 14th. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230908ej9400030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 JEROME POWELL\uc2  SAYS THE FED WILL "PROCEED CAREFULLY" ON INTEREST RATES LEAVES DOOR OPEN FOR MORE HIKES\b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEATHER ALERT: SOUTHERN WILDFIRES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DANGEROUS HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TROUBLE IN THE TROPICS\par \par \uc2 LOUISIANA, WILDFIRE, EVACUATIONS, HAVENS, EDWARDS\par \par \uc2 OKLAHOMA, SHOOTING, HIGH SCHOOL, BERGER, MARSHALL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, 2024, CANDIDATES, GOP, DEBATE, DESANTIS, SCOTT, RAMASWAMY\par \par \uc2 F-18, CRASH, PILOT, SAN DIEGO, TRAINING, FAULKNER\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, WAR, RUSSIA, PROGRESS, TROOPS\par \par \uc2 POWELL, JACKSON HOLE, INTEREST RATES, FED, HIKES\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to the Federal Reserve Chairman, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 's newest assessment on the economy and what the central bank is ready to do to fight inflation. It could mean another boost to interest rates and ABC's Morgan Norwood is following it all. Good morning, Morgan.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, Gio. Look, we've seen signs that inflation is cooling, right, but the Fed Chair says that there's still more work to do and that additional rate hikes are still on the table in the coming months. Now, he pointed out that the economy has been doing better than expected and that consumer spending has been robust. That is great, but the economic indicator that Fed officials are really worried about is the cpi, that's the consumer price index, which signals how much Americans are spending on everyday goods.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS CONCERNED ABOUT CONSUMER SPENDING. AS SOME AMERICANS STRUGGLE TO GET LOANS WITH INTEREST RATE HIKES\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So for July, let's take this for example, we were down to just over three percent, that's from nine percent last year, but it's still above that targeted two percent rate that the Fed really wants to see. And the Fed's rate hikes to lower inflation have been wallet busters for Americans who are struggling to get approved for car loans, let alone a 30-year mortgage with rates there roughly 7.5 percent. That is a 22-year high, by the way. But, support is coming soon for some home buyers. Ahead on "Gma," I will tell you about a new one percent down payment program and the caution from experts. Gio.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNITED AUTO WORKERS UNION AUTHORIZING A STRIKE. FORD, GM, AND \uc2 STELLANTIS\uc2  WORKERS MAY BE HITTING THE PICKET LINES SOON\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Morgan, as you mentioned here, of course, there's word now that the \uc2 United Auto Workers Union\uc2 , they've authorized a strike. What are they asking for, and how might that strike impact Americans?\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, good question there. \uc2 UAW\uc2 's big three members, you've got Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , they authorized a strike and thousands of autoworkers could be hitting the picket lines soon. So, look, they want higher wages, cost of living allowances, better benefits, and more paid time off, right, all the things. But, they're demanding an offer by September 14th and with no deal, we could see car production lines come to a halt, which, of course, could drive up car prices. Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely, Morgan, all right. And as you said, coming up in our next half hour here, how \uc2 Zillow\uc2  is trying to make home buying more affordable to some with a one percent down payment program. All right, Will.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230901ej8q00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUMMER OF THE STRIKE IN LOS ANGELES CITY WORKERS STAGE ONE DAY WALKOUT AS WRITERS' STRIKE HITS 100 DAYS\b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WE HAVE A WINNER\par \par \uc2 MEGA MILLIONS, WINNER, JACKPOT, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 JACKPOT, TICKET, MEGA MILLIONS, PUBLIX\par \par \uc2 FIRES, MAUI, EVACUATIONS, DESTRUCTION, TEXAS, MALLINGER\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, OHIO, GOP, REJECT, ABORTION, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, INDICTMENT, GEORGIA, WITNESSES, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 GOP, CAMPAIGN, DESANTIS, PENCE, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ASSAULT, CHARGES, RIVERFRONT, ALBERT, WARRANTS\par \par \uc2 STRIKES, LOS ANGELES, WRITERS, ACTORS, CITY WORKERS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, DeMarco, thank you. We do turn now to the Hollywood writers' strike marking 100 days after thousands of city workers joined them and actors on the picket lines yesterday. Will Reeve is in Los Angeles with the latest, the shows already being affected, and where do negotiations stand now. Will, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUMMER OF THE STRIKE IN LOS ANGELES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CITY WORKERS STAGE ONE DAY WALKOUT AS WRITERS' STRIKE HITS 100 DAYS\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Whit. Right now LA is a struck town. The unions that make the city go financially and operationally are demanding changes. And there's no real movement in Hollywood as the WGA hits the century mark.\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Studios negotiate.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning the Hollywood writers' strike hitting the 100 day mark, joined by actors at the beginning of July, neither union budging from their demands for higher pay, better staffing and increased benefits.\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Corporate greed has got to go.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Los Angeles city workers also picketing, for 24 hours Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 DION CORNELIOUS (BUS OPERATOR)\par \par \uc2 They're overworking me, overworking others, and it's affecting our family lives.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The union representing sanitation workers, airport custodians, lifeguards and others, claim the city is not negotiating in good faith. City employees marching in front of city hall and \uc2 Los Angeles International Airport\uc2 . The protest disrupting shuttle buses, trash pickup and airport operations.\par \par \uc2 CITY WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 There's a lot of people coming through LAX every day, seven days a week. So it's very hard to do that shorthanded.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The two sides have a meeting set for next week, though the Mayor Karen Bass says the city has been available to discuss negotiations since the start of the year. With no apparent end to the Hollywood strike imminent, the work stoppage is affecting all types of programs, including "Jeopardy!" whose showrunner conceded Monday, the long running quiz show will resort to using a combination of material that their WGA writers wrote before the strike, which is still in the database, and material that has been redeployed from multiple seasons of the show.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yesterday the Writers Guild said that the 100th day of their strike marked only a milestone of shame for the studios who have not yet issued a response. As far as the city workers strike, LA Mayor Karen Bass said the city will not shut down. Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230818ej8900031\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LOS ANGELES CITY WORKERS SET TO STRIKE ONE-DAY WALKOUT OVER WHAT UNION CALLS UNFAIR LABOR PRACTICES\b0\par\par\uc2 372 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLIGHTS, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER CAUSES AIR TRAVEL CHAOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 10,000 FLIGHTS CANCELED OR DELAYED\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDWEST AT RISK FOR LARGE HAIL & POSSIBLE TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 WALKOUT, STRIKE, LOS ANGELES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES CITY WORKERS SET TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-DAY WALKOUT OVER WHAT UNION CALLS UNFAIR LABOR PRACTICES\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to thousands of city workers in Los Angeles joining Hollywood writers and performers on the picket line, walking out for one day. Our chief national correspondent Matt Gutman is there in LA with the latest for us. Good morning, Matt.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Robin. Twenty-four hours of picketing begins here at LAX. You can see dozens of city workers behind me. Now, of course, LAX, the gateway to Los Angeles, one of the busiest airports in the world. And travellers already told to expect delays here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES STRIKE\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is the first time in about 40 years that LA City workers have gone on strike. There are 11,000 sanitation workers and shuttle drivers and engineers and mechanics. And what they're asking for are better wages in the city with a skyrocketing cost of living. Now, labor leaders say there will be continuing rolling strikes throughout the city all day long. They also say that this is part of the hot labor summer with the city workers joining some 15,000 hotel workers who've been on intermittent strikes, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers and, of course, the 170,000 strong members of the actors and writers' guild. The writers have been on strike for 100 days now. No end in sight to that strike, which has crippled Hollywood over the past several months.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And while it may seem to the contrary, there are actually fewer labor actions now than in, say, the '90s or the past 20 years. Union membership is actually down. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, that's some demonstration there. Okay, Matt, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230818ej8800005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STRIKING HOLLYWOOD WRITERS MEET WITH STUDIOS WRITERS GUILD WALKOUT IS APPROACHING ITS 100TH DAY\b0\par\par\uc2 457 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROAD TO 2024: TRUMP ON THE TRAIL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CAMPAIGN, ARRAIGNMENT, ALABAMA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, HEAT, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 IDAHO, SCHOOL BUS, CAMPERS, INJURED\par \par \uc2 CHARGED, SOCIAL MEDIA, GIVEAWAY, VIDEO GAME, CENAT\par \par \uc2 US, IRAN, MARINES, CARGO, SHIPPING\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, PORT, DRONES, WARSHIP\par \par \uc2 GILGO, MURDERS, VERGATA, TIERNEY, BONN\par \par \uc2 TEEN, SIBLEY, STABBING, NYC, GAS STATION\par \par \uc2 HOLLYWOOD, WRITERS, STUDIOS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the new development in the Hollywood writers' strike. Union members and studios holding their first meeting as the walkout approaches day 100. ABC's Will Ganss is here with the details. Good morning, Will.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Janai. We've been out, we've been without new episodes of "Jimmy Kimmel Live," "Snl," and "The Daily Show" for nearly 100 days, but for the first time since Hollywood writers went on strike May 1st, a small glimmer of hope perhaps. Negotiators for the writers' union meeting yesterday with reps for the major studios. For first time in three months, this meeting was essentially a talk to see if talks can resume, if there's enough common ground to even try to negotiate a new deal, but after that meeting yesterday, it doesn't feel that that deal is much closer at all.\par \par \uc2 WILL GANSS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In an email obtained by ABC News to the members of the writers' union from its own negotiating committee, it seems no real progress was made. The wga committee accusing the studios of leaking things to the press and also saying that studio reps indicated in this confidential meeting that they were, quote, "not willing to engage on the preservation of the writer's room or success-based residuals," those being two of the major sticking points in why the writers struck in the first place. Even still, the wga email indicates that both sides agree that the goal here is to get people back to work, though it looks like that might still be a ways away. Major productions like "Dead Pool 3," "Beetlejuice 2," and the "Dirty Dancing" sequel are all halted right now. Turns out, a writers strike can put Baby in a corner, you guys.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. All right, well, I guess we're going to have to watch Will Ganss TikTok videos to keep us busy in the meantime.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He's got it covered.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He does have some good entertainment.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, right.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, it's, when you are in a push. All right, thank you, Will. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230815ej8500032\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ALL EYES ON JOBS REPORT STRONG JOB CREATION EXPECTED, BUT LABOR MARKET TO COOL\b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 August 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP PLEADS NOT GUILTY\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, JAN 6TH, ELECTION, CHARGES, PLEA, DOJ, DUNN\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, ARRAIGNMENT, COURT, COMMUNICATING\par \par \uc2 POLL, TRUMP, INDICTMENT, CHARGES, CAMPAIGN\par \par \uc2 DRONES, ATTACKS, SHIP, RUSSIA, UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 HEAT, DEATHS, CRYOTHERAPY, HORSES, CALDER\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE, ALERTS, RECORD, LOWS\par \par \uc2 GILGO BEACH, MURDERS, VICTIMS, HEUERMANN, REMAINS, DNA\par \par \uc2 SPYING, CHINA, \uc2 US NAVY\uc2 , WEI, ZHAO, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 JOBS REPORT, ECONOMY, LABOR\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Whit. We turn now to this morning's jobs report. Elizabeth Schulze is at the Department of Labor with what the numbers means for the economy and inflation. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRONG JOB CREATION EXPECTED, BUT LABOR MARKET EXPECTED TO COOL\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Good morning, Rebecca. The Labor Department's report this morning will reveal if American employers are scaling back their fast pace of hiring. Economists expect that 200,000 jobs were added to the work force in July. That would confirm a cooling pace of job growth in recent months.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But the labor market is still remarkably strong. Every month industries like health care, local government and hospitality, are adding tens of thousands of workers to their payrolls.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For now, strength in the economy, including the jobs market, is offsetting long term concerns about the finances of the federal government after ratings agency \uc2 Fitch\uc2  downgraded the nation's credit rating this week. And a growing number of economists are now hopeful that the US will avoid a recession altogether this year. Guys.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Something hopeful. All right, Elizabeth, thank you. Eva.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACCUSED IDAHO KILLER OFFERS ALIBI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRYAN KOHBERGER SAYS HE WAS DRIVING ALONE ON NIGHT OF KILLINGS\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up, the man accused of the Idaho college murders offers an alibi. Will it help his defense? But first, back to Ginger.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230815ej840000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UPS & WORKERS TO RESUME TALKS WITH STRIKE LOOMING LARGEST SINGLE COMPANY WALKOUT EVER COULD COST US ECONOMY BILLIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 438 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HEAT, MERGELL, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, LAWSUIT, ABBOTT, BIDEN, PIERRE, FUENTES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPT SUES TEXAS OVER RIO GRANDE BARRIER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR ABBOTT REFUSES TO REMOVE BUOYS & RAZOR WIRE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL IN TURMOIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE PROTESTS AS NETANYAHU'S COURT REFORM PLAN PASSES\par \par \uc2 TURBULENCE, \uc2 DELTA AIRLINES\uc2 , HAIL, COURY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR SCARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DELTA FLIGHT MAKES EMERGENCY LANDING AFTER HITTING TURBULENCE & SEVERE HAIL\par \par \uc2 CAMPBELL, OBAMA, PADDLEBOARD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRAGEDY AT THE OBAMA ESTATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EMPLOYEE OF FORMER FIRST FAMILY APPARENTLY DIES WHILE PADDLEBOARDING\par \par \uc2 UPS, NEGOTIATIONS, TEAMSTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UPS & WORKERS TO RESUME TALKS WITH STRIKE LOOMING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LARGEST SINGLE COMPANY WALKOUT EVER COULD COST U.S. ECONOMY BILLIONS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We have the potential UPS strike that could upend shipping and cause the economy billions. It could come as soon as next week if an agreement is not reached. Our senior national correspondent Steve Osunsami is tracking the latest. Good morning, Steve.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Robin. One good sign is that the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  and UPS resume negotiations today. But if they cannot come to agreement within a week, there could be a strike and the results could be catastrophic. UPS stores like this one directly behind me would have a tough time promising deliveries.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE UPS STRIKE\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) UPS delivers everyday here in the United States, 18.6 million packages. Companies big and small rely on UPS to do their business. And about 340,000 workers could walk out if this happens, which would make this the largest strike against a single employer in US history. UPS is already talking about having managers and people who aren't covered by the contract driving trucks. But UPS pilots, who are under a different agreement, already said that they would respect this possible strike.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UPS STRIKE IMPACT\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The last time UPS had a strike was in 1997. It lasted 15 days, and the company lost hundreds of millions of dollars. Experts say that if a strike happens next week and if it lasted just ten days, it could cost the US economy more than $7 billion.\par \par \uc2 STEVE OSUNSAMI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're hearing the issue is mostly about money. Both the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  and UPS agree that their workers need a raise. Sources tell us, though, the question is over how much. Robin?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And hopefully a resolution can be reached. All right, Steve, thank you. Linsey?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230809ej7p00030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUMMER OF THE STRIKE FIRST THE WRITERS THEN THE ACTORS, IS UPS NEXT?\b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP, JANUARY 6TH, INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, STORM, CAMERON, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DANGEROUS STORMS ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION AFTER TORNADO RIPS THROUGH PARTS OF NORTH CAROLINA\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE, WEATHER, TRACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MARINE HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IMPACT OF SOARING OCEAN TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE, WILDFIRES, PERKINS, GREECE\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, ABUSE, BORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TROUBLE AT RIO GRANDE BORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS OFFICIALS DRAW CRITICISM OVER RAZOR WIRE BARRIER AS INHUMANE\par \par \uc2 NORTH KOREA, GATES, KING, FIKE, CAVANAUGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. SERVICEMAN DETAINED IN NORTH KOREA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS ON 23-YEAR-OLD WHO BOLTED ACROSS BORDER WITH SOUTH KOREA\par \par \uc2 BROADWAY, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUMMER OF THE STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST THE WRITERS THEN THE ACTORS, IS UPS NEXT NEXT?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Here at home, Broadway is now facing a potential strike. They would join the writers and actors on the picket line. Our chief national correspondent Matt Gutman is tracking it from Los Angeles. Good morning, Matt.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Michael. This would be the third entertainment union in the industry to strike.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The International Alliance of Theatrical Stage employees will call a vote to authorize a strike. And it could go into effect as early as Friday. It would affect dozens of Broadway shows and tours, crew members like stage managers, makeup artists, wardrobe personnel looking for better wages and for benefits.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BROADWAY WORKERS CALL STRIKE AUTHORIZATION VOTE\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And those stage employees would join the 170,000 actors and writers now picketing. They're asking for better pay and for protections against artificial intelligence. Now, things getting a little bit heated out in LA. The city said it's now investigating tree trimming of city trees outside Universal Studios, where picketers have been grabbing shade in recent days against the heat. Now, LA actors and writers joining UPS workers picketing on Wednesday, 340,000 UPS workers, the biggest delivery company in the world. They have been threatening to strike. But a sliver of hope. Both sides say they are going to get back to the negotiating table. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We sure hope that sliver of hope, you know, actually all this hopefully works out. Matt, thank you so much for that. Robin?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230807ej7k00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUMMER OF THE STRIKE? UPS, AUTOWORKERS COULD JOIN WRITERS & ACTORS ON THE PICKET LINE\b0\par\par\uc2 575 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRUTAL WEEKEND\par \par \uc2 RAINFALL, FLOODING, RIVERS, HEAT, TEMPS\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TRAVEL, AIRLINES, CANCELATIONS, DELAYS\par \par \uc2 RAIN, FLOODING, HEAT DOME, TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 SERIAL KILLER, ARREST, HEUERMANN, VICTIMS, DNA, BELLONE, TIERNEY\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, BRIDGE, ATTACK, DRONE, CRIMEA\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, CAMPAIGN, SHAKE-UP, REPUBLICANS, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 WIMBLEDON, UPSETS, ALCARAZ, DJOKOVIC, VONDROUSOVA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILDFIRE SMOKE FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MISSING, ABDUCTION, RUSSELL, HOME, TODDLER, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 ESCAPED, CAUGHT, BURHAM, POLICE, HOMEOWNER\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, WRITERS, ACTORS, STREAMING, AI, UPS, AUTOWORKERS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, thanks very much. We're turning now to what is turning to be the summer of the strike. Hollywood is shut down. Writers and actors are walking the picket lines right now. And other potential strikes are looming. Kayna Whitworth is tracking it all from Los Angeles. Good morning, Kayna.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUMMER OF THE STRIKE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UPS, AUTOWORKERS COULD JOIN HOLLYWOOD WRITERS & ACTORS ON THE PICKET LINE\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) yeah, George, good morning. This is certainly a consequential summer for organized labor unions across this country. But here in Los Angeles, this is actually the first time since the '60s that both actors and writers will be joining that picket lines together. Now the biggest issues here outside of the earnings, are concerns over streaming residuals and the impact of AI technology.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Two things the studios say they addressed in their recent offer of what they called historic pay and the highest residuals in 35 years. Actors joining writers who've been on strike since May. George Clooney calling this an inflection point in the industry, and Fran Drescher, who is also President of \uc2 SAG\uc2 /\uc2 AFTRA\uc2 , says what's happening to us is what's happening across all fields of labor, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Kayna, two other big strikes looming.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Certainly, George. So we're looking first at UPS here. There - one of two possible strikes happening this summer. UPS workers could be striking as early as August 1st in what some analysts say could be the costliest work stoppage in US history, hitting the US economy for over $7 billion.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Negotiations are also under way with the United Autoworkers Union as they attempt to secure their futures in a dramatically changing industry. They don't want to be left behind as automakers make the shift to EV. And those contracts are set to expire in early September.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, George, certainly all of these strikes have long lasting ripple effects. Lawmakers are taking note. Democratic Congressman Adam Schiff says he will be here in LA on the picket lines later today, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They are consequential. Okay, Kayna, thanks very much. Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up, the massive passport back log. Trevor Ault has what's being done to speed it up. Hey, Trevor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE PASSPORT BACKLOG\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael, yeah. You've heard of job fairs. Well how about passport fairs? That's just one way the State Department is trying to cut into that massive back log of passports. But a lot of people have had to cancel their trips. We'll tell you what you need to know before you go abroad. That's coming up just ahead.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230802ej7h0005x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HISTORIC STRIKE ACTORS & WRITERS WALKING THE PICKET LINES TOGETHER\b0\par\par\uc2 1,695 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 MURDERS, HEUERMANN, VICTIMS, TIERNEY, PERTEL, ZEMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, ACTORS, WRITERS, DRESCHER, DAVIS, IGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Three years after the pandemic brought Hollywood to a standstill, the industry is once again facing a crisis. This time it's an historic strike. Actors and writers now walking the picket lines together, shutting down Hollywood. Here's ABC's Matt Gutman.\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Actors on strike. We're in it to win it.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) From New York to LA, some of Hollywood's biggest stars trading in props for picket signs.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We are here supporting the union.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why are people out here?\par \par \uc2 KENDRICK SAMPSON (ACTOR "INSECURE")\par \par \uc2 We're out here because \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  has made it very hard to come to a deal that makes sense.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Stars like Jason Sudeikis and Susan Sarandon joining the protests. Matt Damon speaking out from the red carpet.\par \par \uc2 MATT DAMON (ACTOR "OPPENHEIMER")\par \par \uc2 We got to protect the people who are kind of on the margins. We've got to figure out something that is fair.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The strike impacting everyone from background actors to A-listers. The actors say they want higher wages, residual pay, better access to health care, and artificial intelligence regulation.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You've experienced being knocked off of health insurance?\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, one year I was $50 short. We're working class. You know, not everybody can do this full time and make a living, you know. So for them to pinch pennies, for them to not want to share the wealth is really problematic.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After failing to reach an agreement with major studios, the union is standing firm.\par \par \uc2 CLAYTON DAVIS (SENIOR AWARDS EDITOR "VARIETY")\par \par \uc2 People just feel like the man is on their neck, and that is a way to breathe again.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The industry now facing a crisis as 160,000 actors join the 10,000 members of the Writers Guild, striking since May 2nd, on the picket lines. Over the weekend, the cast of "Oppenheimer" walking out of their own premiere, and \uc2 SAG\uc2  President Fran Drescher speaking out and fired up for the cause.\par \par \uc2 FRAN DRESCHER (PRESIDENT \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 At some point you have to say no, we're not going to take this anymore. The entire business model has been changed by streaming, digital, AI. This is a moment of history that is a moment of truth.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , Hollywood's largest union, has been in contract talks since June 7th with the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2 . The bargaining rep for studios and streamers like \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , \uc2 Sony Pictures\uc2 , \uc2 Warner Brothers\uc2 , and the \uc2 Walt Disney Company\uc2 , the parent company of ABC News.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They were unable to reach an agreement by the deadline, and their contract expired. The industry has already been reeling for months from the domino effect of the writers' strike.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM :\uc2 JIMMY KIMMEL\uc2  LIVE"\par \par \uc2 JIMMY KIMMEL\uc2  ("\uc2 JIMMY KIMMEL\uc2  LIVE")\par \par \uc2 Thank you for being here. It is a big night for us.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Late night television airing reruns. Production suspended for hit shows like \uc2 Netflix\uc2 's "Stranger Things," FX's "American Horror Story" and ABC's "Abbott Elementary," and the impact is bringing most of Hollywood to a standstill.\par \par \uc2 CLAYTON DAVIS (SENIOR AWARDS EDITOR "VARIETY")\par \par \uc2 We're not gonna have fall TV. Writers rooms have been shut down since May. So your favorite shows are not coming back.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One of the biggest issues plaguing many actors right now is what they see as unfair residual payments.\par \par \uc2 CLAYTON DAVIS (SENIOR AWARDS EDITOR "VARIETY")\par \par \uc2 So residuals, the way they work, you know, you get paid for the day that you give your services to the said TV show or film, but they get paid every time that show airs in syndication or anywhere in the world.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In the world of streaming, shows don't go to reruns. Content perpetually lives on the platforms and can be viewed at any time. That accessibility has drastically affected payments. Performers receiving what they say are paltry amounts.\par \par \uc2 KENDRICK SAMPSON (ACTOR "INSECURE")\par \par \uc2 There are no excuses. Right now you're being greedy and inhumane.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Actor Kendrick Sampson of \uc2 HBO\uc2 's "Insecure," was on the LA picket lines last week.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You are a successful actor.\par \par \uc2 KENDRICK SAMPSON (ACTOR "INSECURE")\par \par \uc2 I'm a successful.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And tell me the residual checks that you got, five of them, was it last week?\par \par \uc2 KENDRICK SAMPSON (ACTOR "INSECURE")\par \par \uc2 Oh, five? 56.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You got 56.\par \par \uc2 KENDRICK SAMPSON (ACTOR "INSECURE")\par \par \uc2 I got an envelope of 56 checks. And out of 50 of them, I would even say, I would even venture to say 10 of them didn't equal a dollar.\par \par \uc2 KIMIKO GLENN (ACTOR "ORANGE IS THE NEW BLACK")\par \par \uc2 What's going on?\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kimiko Glenn was a cast member on one of the shows that put \uc2 Netflix\uc2  on the map, "Orange Is The New Black."\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "ORANGE IS THE NEW BLACK"\par \par \uc2 KIMIKO GLENN (ACTOR "ORANGE IS THE NEW BLACK")\par \par \uc2 Is this some kind of game? I don't get it.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Recently a TikTok of hers resurfaced where she shows off her paltry residual checks from her recurring role.\par \par \uc2 KIMIKO GLENN (ACTOR "ORANGE IS THE NEW BLACK")\par \par \uc2 My God, I'm about to be so rich. What? The sad reality is for the past 10 years, my residual checks have looked like this.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She concedes that the explosion of streaming brought new opportunities, just ones that don't pay a livable wage.\par \par \uc2 KIMIKO GLENN (ACTOR "ORANGE IS THE NEW BLACK")\par \par \uc2 At this point you have to get like a side hustle. You have to sort of have several different income streams in order to make this life work. And it didn't used to be that way.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Last week, the \uc2 Walt Disney Company\uc2  CEO \uc2 Bob Iger\uc2 , shared his view on the strike with CNBC.\par \par \uc2 BOB IGER (CEO THE \uc2 WALT DISNEY COMPANY\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 This is very disturbing to me. We've talked about disruptive forces on this business and all the challenges that we're facing and the recovery from COVID, which is ongoing. It's not completely back. This is the worst time in the world to add to that disruption.\par \par \uc2 BOB IGER (CEO THE \uc2 WALT DISNEY COMPANY\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 I understand any labor organizations' desire to work on the behalf, behalf of its members to get the most compensation and the be compensated fairly based on the value that they deliver. There's a level of expectation that they have that is just not realistic.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What's your biggest concern right now?\par \par \uc2 FRAN DRESCHER (PRESIDENT \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 I hope that the opposition will come back to the table to talk to us, and I hope that they realize that too little too late.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Another central issue in negotiations is the rise of artificial intelligence in productions.\par \par \uc2 VINCENT AMAYA (BACKGROUND ACTOR & SAG-AFTRA MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 One of my friends was promised four months of work, and that's huge, but day one, they scammed him, and he never heard from production, never heard from casting or that project ever again.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For Vincent Amaya and Elizabeth Mihalek, career background actors, or extras, their likeness is their livelihood.\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Hey, hey, ho, ho, this corporate greed has got to go.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But they say the current proposal that offers just one day's pay in exchange for the rights to use their AI-generated likenesses for an entire project is unfair.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH MIHALEK (BACKGROUND ACTOR & SAG-AFTRA MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 If you're going to continue to make money for the next 30, 40 years off of work I do, I feel like I should be compensated for that.\par \par \uc2 VINCENT AMAYA (BACKGROUND ACTOR & SAG-AFTRA MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 This thing is so new, and people think it's a condition of employment, but it's not. It's not in our contract.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They're part of the majority of actors who audience may never know by name, but who make the Hollywood machine run, for now.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH MIHALEK (BACKGROUND ACTOR & SAG-AFTRA MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 We're kind of support in a scene. We are all the people that you see that make it feel very real.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 AMPTP\uc2  said in a statement that they "Presented a deal that offered historic pay and residual increases," and that it has offered protections for "Actors' digital likenesses" from AI, but that their offer was rejected.\par \par \uc2 WRITER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 To increase their profits at the expense of our livelihoods.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With writers and actors now firmly entrenched together, the disruption in Hollywood has no end in sight.\par \par \uc2 CLAYTON DAVIS (SENIOR AWARDS EDITOR "VARIETY")\par \par \uc2 This is going to be a game where we're going to see who flinches first. It could be some time before we see Hollywood working again.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Their future on the line. They say they're prepared to keep fighting for as long as it takes.\par \par \uc2 VINCENT AMAYA (BACKGROUND ACTOR & SAG-AFTRA MEMBER)\par \par \uc2 I definitely want to still be able to earn a living. I still want to get health insurance through work. I just want us to go back to be able to paying my bills.\par \par \uc2 STRIKER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 What do we want?\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Contracts.\par \par \uc2 STRIKER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 When do we want it?\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Now.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STYLE ICON\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Matt. Coming up, remembering a style icon. Jane Birkin, the inspiration for the Birkin bag.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020230719ej7h00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE LOOMING UPS STRIKE THAT COULD HURT SMALL BUSINESSES COULD DELAY MILLIONS OF DELIVERIES AND SLOW SUPPLY CHAINS\b0\par\par\uc2 831 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAT ALERTS, FLOODING AND SMOKY SKIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEATHER EXTREMES\par \par \uc2 HEAT, WILDFIRES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEAT RECORDS LIKELY FROM COAST-TO-COAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT ALSO FOR 50+ MILLION IN NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, CANADA, SMOKE, AIR QUALITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILDFIRE SMOKE NOW CHOKING MIDWEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LATEST ROUND OF HAZE FROM CANADIAN WILDFIRES MOVING IN\par \par \uc2 ARREST, HEUERMANN, BALLONE, TIERNEY, GILBERT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE HUNT FOR EVIDENCE AFTER GILGO BEACH ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW POLICE CRACKED THE CASE MORE THAN A DECADE AFTER THE MURDERS\par \par \uc2 HARRISON, HEUERMANN\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, LONGMORE, SCANDRETT, TURNER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT MANHUNT FOR MASS SHOOTING SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALLEGED GUNMAN ACCUSED KILLING FOUR IN AN ATLANTA SUBURB\par \par \uc2 BURHAM, ARREST\par \par \uc2 2024 ELECTION, PENCE, FUNDRAISING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FUNDRAISING FIGURES AHEAD OF IOWA CAUCUSES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT THE NUMBERS SAY ABOUT GOP CONTENDERS\par \par \uc2 AAA, INSURANCE, FLORIDA, COVERAGE\par \par \uc2 GUSAKOV, NOTRE DAME CATHEDRAL, RESTORATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RUSSELL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR MISSING WOMAN COMES TO AN END\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CARLEE RUSSELL FOUND SAFE AFTER ALLEGEDLY BEING KIDNAPPED DAYS AGO\par \par \uc2 CRIME TOURISM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT WARNING ABOUT "CRIME TOURISTS"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECTS SAID TO TRAVEL FROM STATE-TO-STATE TARGETING HOMES\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2 , STRIKE, CALPIN, HADELY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE LOOMING \uc2 UPS\uc2  STRIKE THAT COULD HURT SMALL BUSINESSES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COULD DELAY MILLIONS OF DELIVERIES AND SLOW SUPPLY CHAINS AS CONTRACT EXPIRES JULY 31\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "GMA" as we look at the potential effects of a walkout by \uc2 UPS\uc2  workers in what would be the largest single employer strike in US history. Especially hard hit would be small businesses. And ABC's Jay O'Brien is in Washington with more on what it would mean for them. Jay, good morning.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, good morning. Union delivery drivers are key to \uc2 UPS\uc2  and to \uc2 UPS\uc2  stores like this one behind me. And with each passing day and no deal, small business owners who rely on \uc2 UPS\uc2  say they're getting uneasy.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, with contract negotiations stalled between shipping giant \uc2 UPS\uc2  and the \uc2 Teamsters Union\uc2 , fears a potential strike could hit small businesses hard.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE CALPIN (NIBBLES AND BITS)\par \par \uc2 We ship. We ship a lot.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Maggie Calpin, owner of gourmet gift basket store Nibbles and Bits, says the strike would throw the thousands of packages she ships through her local \uc2 UPS\uc2  store into upheaval.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE CALPIN (NIBBLES AND BITS)\par \par \uc2 I'm nervous. A lot of time we're locked in for free shipping because we order in such bulk. That might stop now.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A ten-day UPS strike could be the costliest in US history, totaling an estimated $7 billion according to a research firm that studies labor disputes.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Who are we?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , which represents roughly 350,000 \uc2 UPS\uc2  workers, already marching in what are called practice picket lines. Last month, union workers voted overwhelmingly to authorize a strike starting August 1st if there's no agreement. \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  demands include better pay, an increase in full-time jobs, and for the company to address health and safety concerns, including the sweltering heat inside delivery vehicles. The union accusing \uc2 UPS\uc2  of walking away from the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 JIM HADELY (\uc2 UPS\uc2  DRIVER AND UNION SHOP STEWARD)\par \par \uc2 We work long hours. We work strenuous hours out in the crazy heat, the cold, you know, all conditions. We made the company a lot of money over the last five years. I would just ask them to come to the table.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UPS\uc2  STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But in a statement to ABC News, \uc2 UPS\uc2  says they've already made historic proposals and blame the union for refusing to negotiate, adding, "We have not walked away and the union has a responsibility to remain at the table." Margaret Barrow, owner of New York city-based snack maker, It's Nola now racing to find other delivery options if the \uc2 UPS\uc2  union deal falls through.\par \par \uc2 MARGARET BARROW (OWNER IT'S NOLA)\par \par \uc2 It's going to significantly impact how much money I'm going to have to spend in looking for alternative shipping prices. I've already started looking at that and it doesn't look very good.\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 UPS\uc2  added it still expects a deal can be reached by that July 31st deadline, but the company is also training non-union employees to step in if there is a strike. A Teamster spokesperson telling me that is a, quote, "insult." Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, something to watch closely. Jay O'Brien, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOOTING STARS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up here on "Good Morning America," the big moments overnight at the \uc2 WNBA\uc2  all-star game. The shooting stars that made the difference.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230802ej7g00039\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD HALTED POTENTIAL ECONOMIC IMPACT AS ACTORS JOIN WRITERS ON STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 90 MILLION AMERICANS UNDER HEAT ALERTS: DANGEROUS WEEKEND WEATHER\par \par \uc2 HEAT, RECORD, CALIFORNIA, FLORIDA, BJORLO\par \par \uc2 GILGO BEACH, MURDERS, HEUERMANN, HARRISON, TIERNEY, MUSTO, PERTEL\par \par \uc2 GILGO, MURDERS, SUFFOLK, DA, EVIDENCE, TIERNEY\par \par \uc2 HOLLYWOOD, STRIKE, DRESCHER, DEWEY, OLBILOM, WAGMEISTER\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, to Hollywood on strike, actors joining the pickets lines with the Writers Guild as they fight for more compensation and protections from major industry changes. ABC's Zohreen Shah is in LA with more on the impact and where things stand now. Zohreen, good morning.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, you just have to drive by any studio in LA to see where things stand. The actors have joined the picket line, and they tell me the Hollywood dream is a far, far reach. For most working actors, many are barely scraping by, and so for the first time in six decades they are joining the writers in strike.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Sag-Aftra strong. \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  strong.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, day two of Hollywood actors joining writers on strike, bringing the entertainment industry to a halt.\par \par \uc2 FRAN DRESCHER (PRESIDENT \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 We are speaking on behalf of workers all across the nation and around the world, the eyes of workers are upon us.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Picketers yesterday stretched across the entrances of major studios from Hollywood and LA to New York City. Many movie and TV productions from "Wednesday" to upcoming Marvel films like "Dead Pool 3" indefinitely delayed while "House of the Dragon," whose cast is mostly British and not part of \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , may continue filming. Actors are looking for better residual pay and higher wages for streaming shows, and protection of their likeness from the use of AI. These issues largely affecting actors barely making living wages.\par \par \uc2 GERALD DEWEY (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 You are typically having to work a second job in order to subsidize your income.\par \par \uc2 JESSICA OBILOM (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I was living check to check, let's just be honest. I had a friend who lived in his car for a year.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And the strike potentially crippling the Los Angeles economy that relies so heavily on Hollywood. \uc2 Forbes\uc2  estimating the cost could top three billion and thousands of jobs.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH WAGMEISTER (CHIEF ESPONDENT "VARIETY")\par \par \uc2 A Hollywood production brings a lot of money to a lot of different businesses. We're talking hotels, we're talking restaurants, so there's going to be a huge economic impact from this strike.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A far reaching impact. As for the association representing the studios and streamers, they say they offered actors historic pay and residual increases and ai protection for actors' digital likeness, but that offer was not accepted. Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So many workers and industries affected by this. Zohreen, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230802ej7f00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD STRIKES' RIPPLE EFFECT GROWING ECONOMIC CONCERNS AS ACTORS HIT PICKET LINES\b0\par\par\uc2 528 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTING, LONGMORE, TARPLEY, SCANDRETT\par \par \uc2 HEUERMAN, MURDER, ARREST, TIERNEY, PERTEL, KAFKA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GILGO BEACH MURDER INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD BREAKING HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 HARTMAN, LEVELLE, PROTESTS, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , WRITERS GUILD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD STRIKES' RIPPLE EFFECT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We move now to the historic Hollywood strike upending the industry.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's the first time in nearly 60 years that both actors and writers have been on strike at the same time, and the financial and human toll could be devastating.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Related industries from catering services to makeup now reeling as well. And this could go on for months. Here's ABC's Zohreen Shah.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING ECONOMIC CONCERNS AS ACTORS HIT PICKET LINES\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 What do we want?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Contracts.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, day two of the Hollywood shutdown and growing concerns over the spreading economic impact.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Our picket lines are more full than ever.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) 160,000 actors in the \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  union joining The Writers Guild on strike Friday, the first time since 1960 both have been on strike simultaneously.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 There's just a general work stoppage. There's a lot of crew out of work right now.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And not just actors and writers feeling the effects. Tens of thousands in adjacent industries depend on TV and movie productions for their livelihood. Mark Hartman owns a cafe near a major studio, and he says the last writers' strike was difficult to recover from.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You lost 40% of your business last time?\par \par \uc2 MARK HARTMAN (OWNER PRISCILLA'S COFFEE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Yeah, for a long time. And we also lost half our staff, too. They lost their jobs, too.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Corri Levelle, whose business provides flower-related props for studio productions, says she had to lay off half her staff even before the actors joined the writers on strike.\par \par \uc2 I LEVELLE (OWNER SANDY ROSE FLORAL PROP HOUSE)\par \par \uc2 I'm looking at losing about $100,000 a month. I'm a small company. That's a lot of money.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAG-AFTRA UNION DEMANDS\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The striking \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  members demanding regulations for artificial intelligence in productions, higher wages, and increased residual pay.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 ALLIANCE OF MOTION PICTURE AND TELEVISION PRODUCERS\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For its part, the association representing the studios says it offered actors historic pay and residual increases and protections for actors' digital likenesses from AI, but that their offer was rejected.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Whit, there is no sign of a deal being reached any time soon. Fifteen years ago, when just the writers picketed for three months, it cost California alone $2 billion according to a study by the \uc2 Milken Institute\uc2 . Experts warn of a potentially bigger impact this time around. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Major concerns about what this could mean going forward. Zohreen, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230718ej7f00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD SHUTS DOWN ACTORS JOIN WRITERS ON STRIKE AFTER FAILING TO REACH DEAL WITH STUDIOS\b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUMMER STORMS & EXTREME HEAT\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, HEAT, TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAINFALL, WINDS, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE, PHOENIX, TEMPERATURES, RECORD, OCEAN\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , DRESCHER, HOLLYWOOD, IGER, WAGMEISTER\par \par \uc2 MORTGAGE, RATES, RISE, HOMEBUYERS\par \par \uc2 SECRET SERVICE, COCAINE, WHITE HOUSE, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 FDA, OPILL, BIRTH CONTROL, PRESCRIPTION, AUGUSTE\par \par \uc2 ASPARTAME, WHO, CARCINOGEN, FDA, MODERATION\par \par \uc2 POWERBALL, MEGA MILLIONS, JACKPOTS, THOMPSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNBEARABLE NIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 NILO, SEXUAL ASSAULT, CHARGES, BAIL, PINKHAM, CATALDO, HAYDEN\par \par \uc2 MANATEES, SWIMMERS, HARASSING, ENDANGERED, GARRETT, ILLEGAL\par \par \uc2 CREDIT CARD, SKIMMING, THIEVES, \uc2 WALMART\uc2 , CRANE, LEONARD\par \par \uc2 "BARBIE", CENA, MERMAID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OPPRESSIVE HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MARINE HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE STORMS ON THE MOVE: MAJOR WEEKEND HEATWAVE\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 HOLLYWOOD, WRITERS, ACTORS, STRIKE, DEAL, STUDIOS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to Hollywood shut down where the biggest entertainment industry strike in decades is under way. Actors are now on the picket lines with writers who walked out in May. And Chief National Correspondent, Matt Gutman is in Los Angeles with the very latest. Good morning, Matt.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Rebecca. This is the first Hollywood actors walkout in 43 years, effectively paralyzing the $100 billion plus a year industry. I spoke with Fran Drescher, a very fired up union president, who said this is their moment of truth. Now, negotiations between the studios and streamers and the actors broke down early Thursday morning with the studio saying that they're disappointed that the actors walked away from historic increases in pay and residuals.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The strike became official this morning, and we are already starting to see the effects of it. The entire cast of the film "Oppenheimer" walking away from their uk premiere. Now, the actors say they are fighting for better pay and residuals, which are critical for them receiving health insurance. Also hard to underscore the importance of ai for the actors. They are concerned someone will take their likeness and use it in perpetuity. And it is worth noting that this is the first time that all 170,000 members of the Actors and Writers Guilds are striking at the same time since 1960. Juju.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Matt, massive ripe effects. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230801ej7e0008w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD SHUTS DOWN ACTORS JOIN WRITERS ON STRIKE AFTER FAILING TO REACH DEAL WITH STUDIOS\b0\par\par\uc2 849 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUMMER STORMS & EXTREME HEAT\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, HEAT, TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAINFALL, WINDS, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE, PHOENIX, TEMPERATURES, RECORD, OCEAN\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , DRESCHER, HOLLYWOOD, IGER, WAGMEISTER\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It sure is. Okay, Matt, thank you very much. Now to the Hollywood shut down. The biggest entertainment industry strike in decade. Actors have now joined the picket lines with the writers who walked out in May. Chief national correspondent Matt Gutman is in Los Angeles with the latest. Good morning, Matt.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD SHUTS DOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTORS JOIN WRITERS ON STRIKE AFTER FAILING TO REACH DEAL WITH STUDIOS\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, George. This is the first Hollywood actors walkout in 43 years, and it effectively paralyzes the $100 billion plus industry. And in a media landscape being transformed by streaming and AI, a very fired up Fran Drescher, the union president, telling me this is their moment of truth.\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Pay your actors.\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Pay your actors.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning no lights, camera or action in Hollywood. \uc2 SAG\uc2 /\uc2 AFTRA\uc2 , the union representing some of the biggest names in film and television, is officially on strike. Overnight the cast of "Oppenheimer" leaving before the screening at the UK premiere to support the strike.\par \par \uc2 MATT DAMON (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 We've got to protect the people who are kind of on the margins. We've got to figure out something that is fair.\par \par \uc2 FRAN DRESCHER (PRESIDENT \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 It came with great sadness that we came to this crossroads, but we had no choice.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Weeks of intense negotiations with major studios broke down with the actors' existing contract expiring early Thursday morning.\par \par \uc2 FRAN DRESCHER (PRESIDENT \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 In the long run, if we don't draw the line in the sand now, they're going to be squeezed out of a livelihood anyway. They already are. So what are we doing making incremental changes on a contract that's no longer relevant? It's like rearranged furniture on the "Titanic."\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The actors say they're fighting for higher wages and protections in a streaming era, including residual pay, critical to them keeping their health care, and the regulated use of AI.\par \par \uc2 MARK ROMAN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 If we don't have clear rules that say only human actors can be used as background acting talent, not AI, I don't get a job.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The group representing studios and streamers saying it's "Disappointed the actors union decided to walk away from negotiations," adding that the strike will "Deepen the financial hardship for thousands who depend on the industry for their livelihoods." \uc2 Bob Iger\uc2 , the CEO of the \uc2 Walt Disney Company\uc2 , the parent company of ABC News, warned of the strike's economic impact.\par \par \uc2 BOB IGER (CEO THE \uc2 WALT DISNEY COMPANY\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 It is very disturbing to me. We've talked about disruptive forces on this business and all the challenges we're facing and the recovery from COVID, which is ongoing. It's not completely back. This is the worst time in the world to add to that disruption.\par \par \uc2 BOB IGER (CEO THE \uc2 WALT DISNEY COMPANY\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 I understand any labor organization's desire to work on the behalf, behalf of its members to get the most compensation and to be compensated fairly based on the value that they deliver. There's a level of expectation that they have that is just not realistic.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A-listers, including Meryl Streep, Quinta Brunson and Mark Ruffalo, urging leadership to hold the line, according to a signed letter obtained by "\uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2 " late last month. Several highly anticipated productions like \uc2 Netflix\uc2  "Stranger Things," already shut down due to the writers' strike.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH WAGMEISTER (CHIEF ESPONDENT "VARIETY")\par \par \uc2 There's really no model for how this works especially in this current media landscape. So when the actors are on strike, along with the writers being on strike, essentially no work can be done in Hollywood.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to the guidelines of the strike, \uc2 SAG\uc2 /\uc2 AFTRA\uc2  members will not be able to attend premieres, award shows, or festivals. They can't do interviews for completed work, promote events on social media or attend conventions like Comic-Con.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're already starting to see some of the ripple effects. Festivals are being impacted. The Emmys, which just announced their nominees, could be postponed. Broadcast networks are hinting that their fall lineups might include more reruns and reality shows.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And just to give you a sense of how rare it is for both the writers and actors guilds to strike simultaneously, George is gonna like this one, it was 1960 and Dwight Eisenhower was president. Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We appreciate that history.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I wasn't born in 1960, Matt.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230801ej7e0008h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD SHUTS DOWN BOTH SIDES DIG IN AS ACTORS JOIN WRITERS ON STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 514 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ARREST, HEUERMAN, TIERNEY, HARRISON, PERTEL\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE STORMS & SCORCHING HEAT\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, BURHAM BIVENS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , SUDEIKIS, IRELAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD SHUTS DOWN\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, Hollywood grinding to a halt. The actors now on strike, joining writers already on the picket lines. The first time both groups have been on strike at the same time in more than 60 years. What they're asking for. Here's Matt Gutman.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOTH SIDES DIG IN AS ACTORS JOIN WRITERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 On strike.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Shut it down.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, both sides digging in on day one of that historic shutdown that threatens to paralyze Hollywood.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 There are no excuses. Right now, you're being greedy and inhumane, and that's that.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Union power.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Early this morning, the 160,000 members of the \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  union joining the already striking Writers' Guild. The last time Hollywood actors and writers on strike at the same time was 1960.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 What do we want?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Contract.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Actors picketing on both coasts, including Ted Lasso's Jason Sudeikis and Susan Sarandon who joined the protests in New York, supporting the majority actors who do not make a living wage from acting.\par \par \uc2 DUNCAN CRABTREE-IRELAND (CHIEF NEGOTIATOR \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 I think our message is really resonating. There's a lot of people, even beyond our membership, who are kind of fed up with big corporations trying to just run roughshod over everybody.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  members demanding regulations for artificial intelligence in productions, higher wages, and increased residual pay, which is essential to many of them keeping health insurance.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You've experienced being knocked off of health insurance?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I have, yes. One year, I was $50 short. We're working class, not everybody can do this full-time and make a living. So, for them to pinch pennies, for them to not want to share the wealth is really problematic.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 ALLIANCE OF MOTION PICTURE AND TELEVISION PRODUCERS\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The association representing studios and streamers saying they offered the actors historic pay and residual increases and protections for actors' digital likenesses from AI, but that their offer was rejected.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, the last time the actors went on strike, it was 1980 and it lasted for more than three months. And we are already starting to see some of ripple effects. Actors walking out on their own premieres. Networks saying, they will run more reruns and reality shows in the fall. And just moments ago, LA's Mayor Karen Bass urging both sides to get back to the negotiating table. She's concerned about the economic impact of the strike. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Matt Gutman on this again tonight. Thank you, Matt.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230718ej7e00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD ACTORS' STRIKE IMMINENT \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  CONTRACT DEADLINE EXPIRES WITHOUT A DEAL\b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES, TRUJILLO, CARR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADOES TEAR THROUGH THE HEARTLAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TWISTER TOUCHES IN CHICAGO AREA AS SEVERE STORMS WREAK HAVOC\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS FROM COAST TO COAST ON ALERT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, PAY, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD ACTORS' TRIKE IMMINENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  CONTRACT DEADLINE EXPIRES WITHOUT A DEAL\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to the breaking news overnight. And Hollywood on the brink of shutting down. Actors failed to reach a deal with the major studios. Trevor Ault joins us for what it means for the TV shows and movies that you've been waiting for. Good morning, Trevor.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. Yes, so the overnight deadline for a deal has come and gone. And that means, this morning, the national board for the \uc2 Screen Actors Guild\uc2  is expected to vote to authorize a strike. And this, of course, has gigantic implications for Hollywood. And the sticking points are, of course, over pay but also on the potential use in the future of artificial intelligence to replace actors and writers.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible)\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 LA is a union town?\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, Hollywood is poised to strike. Overnight, the contract deadline expiring without agreement after more than four weeks of intense negotiations between \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  and the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH WAGMEISTER (CHIEF ESPONDENT "VARIETY")\par \par \uc2 In this streaming era, everything is different. Nothing is the same from where it was in the broadcast TV era, where there was a model for residuals and a model for pay. Now, all of that's changing, and the actors and the union are essentially saying, pay us more and give us our residuals. And a big component of these negotiations and what \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  is fighting for is also protections from AI.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a statement, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  says they voted unanimously to recommend to the national board a strike. The president, actress Fran Drescher, saying the union "negotiated in good faith and was eager to reach a deal but the \uc2 AMPTP\uc2 's response to the union's most important proposals had been insulting and disrespectful of our massive contributions to this industry." If the board formally votes to strike, film and TV sets would be near total shut down. Even promotional tours or appearances at big events like Comicon would likely be put on hold. And this potential strike begins as The Writers Guild strike has already stretched more than 70 days fighting for similar victories with no end in sight.\par \par \uc2 TREVOR AULT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, in a statement, the producers say this was the \uc2 Screen Actors Guild\uc2 's decision to walk away from the negotiating table in what the producers call historic pay and residual increases. And they say this strike is going to deepen the financial hardships for thousands of people who depend on the industry for their livelihoods, though it's clear the actors authorizing the strike believe the future of their livelihoods is what's at stake, and they think in the long run they will win. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Huge impact there. Okay, Trevor, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230801ej7d0005p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD FACING SHUTDOWN ACTORS GUILD VOTES UNANIMOUSLY TO JOIN WRITERS ON STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 577 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, FLOODING, SCOTT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 HEAT, SLIFKA, EUROPE, CLIMATE CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCORCHING HEAT COAST TO COAST\par \par \uc2 PROTEST, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , DRESCHER, DAMON, IGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD FACING SHUTDOWN\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the developing story from California. Hollywood coming to a halt. The actors' union now set to strike at midnight. The Writers Guild already on strike. This is the first time in more than 60 years this has happened. ABC's chief national correspondent Matt Gutman from Los Angeles tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTORS GUILD VOTES UNANIMOUSLY TO JOIN WRITERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Strike.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, for the first time in 63 years, both actors and writers will be on strike. Labor tensions now set to paralyze Hollywood.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 LA is a union town.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , the union representing actors, voting to hit the picket lines after negotiations with the organization that represents studios and streamers broke down early this morning. Actor Fran Drescher, best known for her role in "The Nanny," now the president of \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , saying they were given no choice.\par \par \uc2 FRAN DRESCHER (ACTOR & SAG-AFTRA PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 You share the wealth, because you cannot exist without us.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAG-AFTRA UNION\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The more than 160,000 \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2  members demanding better pay, regulations for artificial intelligence, and increased residuals, which for many members provides access to crucial health care.\par \par \uc2 MATT DAMON (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 26,000 bucks a year is what you have to make to get your health insurance, and there are a lot of people who, residual payments are what carry them across that threshold.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 ALLIANCE OF MOTION PICTURE AND TELEVISION PRODUCERS\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Association of Studios and Streamers said they offered the actors historic pay and residual increases and promises on protecting actors' digital likenesses from AI. But the union says that offer was not enough.\par \par \uc2 FRAN DRESCHER (ACTOR & SAG-AFTRA PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 They came back with so little that I began to feel like we were duped.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What's your biggest concern right now?\par \par \uc2 FRAN DRESCHER (ACTOR & SAG-AFTRA PRESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 Well, I feel, you know, a big weight and responsibility that we had to strike. I hope that the opposition will come back to the table.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Bob Iger\uc2 , the CEO \uc2 Disney\uc2 , the parent company of ABC News, today speaking on the side of the studios, saying the union's expectations are not realistic and could impact thousands.\par \par \uc2 BOB IGER (CHIEF EXECUTIVE OFFICER OF \uc2 DISNEY\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 There's huge collateral damage in the industry to people who are support services. I could go on and on. It will affect the economy of, you know, different regions even because of the sheer size of the business. It's a shame. It is really a shame.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, the strike official begins at midnight. And it not only prohibits actors from working, but also from promoting their films at festivals and premieres. And just to give you a sense how rare it is for both the actors and writers guild to strike simultaneously, that last happened in 1960, and the president of the Actors Guild was Ronald Reagan. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That puts it into perspective, 60 years ago. Matt Gutman tonight. Thank you, Matt.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230717ej7d00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THOUSANDS OF HOTEL WORKERS STRIKE MYRTLE BEACH PLANE CRASH\b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 July 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY WEEKEND MASS SHOOTINGS\par \par \uc2 SHOOTINGS, BALTIMORE, SCOTT, DEAD, INJURED, CHICAGO, WICHITA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY WEEKEND MASS SHOOTINGS\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, CHAOS, THUNDERSTORMS, TURBULENCE, BASKONYALI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JULY FOURTH TRAVEL CHAOS\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, RESCUES, TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS DANGEROUS STORM AND HEAT ALERTS\par \par \uc2 THUNDERSTORMS, RAIN, HEAT, HOLIDAY\par \par \uc2 ATTACKS, EXPLOSIVES, BUSINESSES, SUSPECTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECTS SOUGHT IN EXPLOSIVE ATTACKS\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, RULINGS, GOP, DEMOCRATS, POLL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP SUPREME COURT VICTORY LAP\par \par \uc2 FRANCE, RIOTERS, NAHEL, SHOOTING, PROTESTS, MAYOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIOTERS TARGET MAYOR'S HOME\par \par \uc2 BURNS, SPIES, MUTINY, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, COUNTEROFFENSIVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CIA DIRECTOR WEIGHS IN ON MUTINY\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, HOTEL, PLANE, CRASH, KILLED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS OF HOTEL WORKERS STRIKE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next tonight, thousands of union hotel workers going on strike in Southern California, walking off their jobs in the middle of a busy holiday weekend.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The workers are demanding higher wages and better benefits. The strike affecting several major hotels, from the Intercontinental to the Ritz Carlton. Hotel officials say they will remain open, making plans for management and nonunion staff to fill in.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MYRTLE BEACH PLANE CRASH\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) At least one person was killed, another injured after a small plane crashed at a resort near Myrtle Beach, South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Black smoke was visible from a distance. One witness says the plane flew right over his head and then crashed into the ground, causing a loud explosion and a fireball. The \uc2 FAA\uc2  says it will investigate.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, the woman who came face-to-face with a bear, and what she did to save herself and her dog.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020230705ej720000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD CLIFFHANGER ACTORS FACE MIDNIGHT DEADLINE TO STRIKE; MAY JOIN WRITERS\b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STUDENT LOANS, BIDEN, MOYA, HALEY, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 LGBTQ RIGHTS, SMITH, FREE SPEECH, WEISER, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURTS LIMITS LGBTQ PROTECTIONS\par \par \uc2 TRACK, HEAT, WEATHER, STORMS, ZAVADSKY, WILDFIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DANGEROUS AIR & SCORCHING HEAT\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, FLIGHTS, GAS PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD HOLIDAY TRAVEL CRUNCH\par \par \uc2 PARIS, PROTESTS, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRACKDOWN ON VIOLENT PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, WEST, LENO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD CLIFFHANGER\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back here at home, to the Hollywood cliffhanger. The actors' union is set to strike at midnight unless they reach a deal with the studios. But with just hours until that deadline, reports that more than 300 members, including Meryl Streep, Jennifer Lawrence, Ben Stiller, and Neil Patrick Harris, are urging their union to stand strong. ABC's Zohreen Shah is in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTORS FACE MIDNIGHT DEADLINE TO STRIKE; MAY JOIN WRITERS\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Hollywood bracing for a second strike, this time from some of its biggest movie and TV stars as the deadline nears for contract talks. "Rolling Stone" reporting that a letter signed by A-list act Jennifer Lawrence and Meryl Streep, along with hundreds of others, warned their guild, \uc2 SAG-AFTRA\uc2 , that they are prepared to strike if it comes to that. Adding, "If we settle for a less than transformative deal, the future of our union and our craft will be undermined." \uc2 SAG\uc2 's contract due to expire in mere hours at midnight local time. Tonight, actors tell us streaming has led to shrinking residuals and shorter seasons meaning less money.\par \par \uc2 RANDY WEST (\uc2 SAG\uc2  MEMBER FOR 42 YEARS)\par \par \uc2 It's a matter of keeping up with the technology. We need to recognize the current trends.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It comes nearly two months after thousands of film and TV writers hit the picket lines, shuttering many productions. Comedian Jay Leno hoping for a deal, but supports actors joining the writers in strike.\par \par \uc2 JAY LENO (COMEDIAN)\par \par \uc2 It would probably move things along. When you're making less money now than you were 15 years ago, well, that can't be right.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And with both groups striking at the same time, that hasn't happened in six decades. With no writers, no actors, that could have a seismic impact on entertainment and what all of us watch. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Zohreen Shah, thank you. When we come back, the images coming in, a large fire breaking out on a major studio lot. Smoke and flames through the roof. And the insect invasion here in New York.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230705ej6u00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW DATA ON REMOTE WORK & PRODUCTIVITY THOSE WORKING FROM HOME PUT IN FEWER HOURS\b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST CHAOS\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, CHAOS, FLIGHTS, STORMS, STAFFING, TSA\par \par \uc2 MIDWEST, SMOKE, WILDFIRES, AIR QUALITY\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE, INDEX, TEMPERATURES, SOUTH, FIRE DEPT\par \par \uc2 HEAT WAVE, TEMPERATURES, RECORD, DOME\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, OPINIONS, LANDMARK, CASES, JUSTICES\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, REBELLION, PRIGOZHIN, PUTIN, BELARUS, UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 WHITE POWDER, LAWMAKERS, INVESTIGATION, MATTIVI\par \par \uc2 MALLETT, NFL, DROWNING, RIP CURRENTS, FORD, DUSEK\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, RELIEF, FUNDS, FRAUD, TASK FORCE\par \par \uc2 SOCCER, WOMEN, ESPYS, 