Month with some workers in some states saying that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is barring them from putting up pride decorations.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Workers at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 ' flagship store in Seattle kicking off that week-long walkout with employees in at least 28 other states set to join in the days to come. Now, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , they are vehemently denying the union's claim, saying that they haven't pulled any Pride merchandise from the stores, let alone changed corporate policy surrounding Pride Month celebrations. They add, though, it has been and will continue to be at the forefront of supporting the LGBTQIA2+ community. Now, Starbucks Workers United, that is the union. They have been working to unionize stores across the country, accusing \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  of making employees feel unwelcome in the workplace amid those contract negotiations.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The company, on the other hand, calling the strike a tactic to deflect from said negotiations across 200 stores. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Thank you so much, Morgan. Appreciate you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 4 MINUTES, ALOPECIA TREATMENT APPROVED\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And coming up here in our "Morning Menu," a big development overnight. It's a big story. The hair-loss drug now approved for alopecia patients as young as 12.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 7 MINUTES, A.I. "KIDNAPPING" SCAMS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Plus, more of our "GMA" investigation into how artificial intelligence is being used to pull off so-called kidnapping scams.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 12 MINUTES, DEALS & STEALS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Looking forward to that. And also, this morning, soak up the savings with "Deals & Steals." There's Tory. We'll be right back here on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230712ej6o000bq\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEEN SUMMER JOB SEARCH EMPLOYERS WILLING TO PAY MORE FOR POSITIONS IN HIGH DEMAND\b0\par\par\uc2 801 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS MORNING: THE HEAT IS ON!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PICKING UP THE PIECES\par \par \uc2 HEAT, STORM, TEXAS, FLORIDA, CONE, FEINSTEIN\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, TEXAS, PANHANDLE, PERRYTON, KERBL\par \par \uc2 SUMMER, TRAVEL, JUNETEENTH, HOLIDAY, TSA\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, WAR, BELARUS, NUCLEAR, TACTICAL\par \par \uc2 CHINA, BEIJING, BLINKEN, CONFLICT\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CAMPAIGN, 2024\par \par \uc2 MINNEAPOLIS, EXCESSIVE FORCE, POLICE, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 SYNAGOGUE, PITTSBURGH, SHOOTER, DEATH PENALTY\par \par \uc2 DELTA, AMERICAN AIRLINES, INCIDENT, AIRPORT, \uc2 FAA\par \par \uc2 CHARLES, MONARCH, JOBSON, TROOPING THE COLOUR\par \par \uc2 MORANT, \uc2 NBA\uc2 , SUSPENDED, GUN, MCNUTT, SMITH\par \par \uc2 SHARK, AMPUTATED, LEG, BOAT, BAHAMAS, ERNST, SKOMAL, REED\par \par \uc2 GRAMMYS, AI, MUSIC, PARMAR\par \par \uc2 TEENS, JOBS, HUTCHINSON, JOHNSON, BUNKER\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And welcome back to "Gma," and the new trends for teenagers looking to make some summer cash and build up their work experience this summer. The key experts say is knowing who's hiring and where.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's that time of year for teens to get to work...\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 No running on my watch.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...and the summer jobs market is hot.\par \par \uc2 CORY HUTCHINSON (GENERAL MANAGER FUNTOWN SPLASHTOWN USA)\par \par \uc2 Demand is high everywhere.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Cory Hutchinson runs a water and amusement park in Maine and relies on teens all summer long.\par \par \uc2 CORY HUTCHINSON (GENERAL MANAGER FUNTOWN SPLASHTOWN USA)\par \par \uc2 Teen workers are a huge part of our team. They've always been very critical to our operation.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Demand in the US especially high for lifeguards amid a shortage forcing thousands of pools to close or reduce hours. Even as the overall economy slows, teen hires are expected to spike from camp workers and instructors in sports and the arts, to retail and restaurant jobs. And businesses are expected to pay teen workers even more than they did last year, an average of nearly $15 an hour, a nine percent increase. Construction offering one of the highest wages at nearly $18 an hour. 18-year-old Jack Johnson has worked for Hutchinson for three years and says he's pleased with the bump.\par \par \uc2 JACK JOHNSON (RIDES LEAD FUNTOWN SPLASHTOWN USA)\par \par \uc2 Definitely a nice, welcome surprise. I was very happy to see that. It definitely makes me want to work even more.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Western states will see some of the highest paychecks due to higher minimum wages where on average teens can earn over $1,000 per month. And according to cooljobs.com, Los Angeles, Tucson, Arizona, and Las Vegas are among the top ten cities with the best-paying summer jobs.\par \par \uc2 NICK BUNKER\uc2  (DIRECTOR OF NORTH AMERICAN ECONOMIC RESEARCH INDEED)\par \par \uc2 If you're a, you know, teenage job seeker out there right there, there's many opportunities and you should take advantage of them, and quickly because they're going to fade just like summer will.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And beyond teenagers, according to Indeed, other in-demand summer jobs include summer law associates, summer school teachers and bank tellers. My oldest daughter is getting closer and closer to that work age, so...\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...what are we doing this summer? I know what you're doing, kid...\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...get to work.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was one of your favorite summer jobs?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, I was making business cards at a print shop.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, wow.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. I was pretty good.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was making custard at Ollie's Frozen Custard.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, wow. I like that too.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ooh, that's a good one.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep, I worked at a gym, soccer camps, the whole thing.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was going to say, what, you didn't have to work?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, of course, the Olive Garden. Bona festa. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRUTAL HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Coming up on "Gma" in our second hour, the brutal heat scorching the south for the holiday weekend with Americans on the move in the air and on the roads.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PARENTING ALERT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And a "Gma" parenting alert from the Academy of Pediatrics about a popular kind of product that may be in your baby's nursery right now.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS AND STEALS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And then it's "Deals & Steals." Look at all that stuff for your home. We'll be right back on "Gma."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230707ej6h0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LABOR DISPUTE THREATENING WEST COAST PORTS OPERATORS ACCUSING DOCKWORKERS OF SHUTTING DOWN TERMINALS\b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SONIC BOOM SCARE\par \par \uc2 F-16 JETS, CESSNA, SONIC BOOM, AIR SPACE, PILOT, \uc2 FAA\par \par \uc2 SONIC BOOM, F-16S, SCRAMBLE, HYPOXIA\par \par \uc2 US, CHINA, TENSIONS, WARSHIP, DESTROYER, SULLIVAN\par \par \uc2 WHITE HOUSE, PRIMARY, GOP, DESANTIS, PENCE, SCOTT\par \par \uc2 DERAILMENT, INDIA, INJURED, SIGNAL\par \par \uc2 PORTS, DOCKWORKERS, SHIPPING, DISPUTE\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just heart wrenching for the families of those victims. James, our thanks to you. Now to the dispute that's threatening traffic at some of the biggest ports the West Coast. Operators are accusing dock workers of effectively shutting down terminals from Southern California to Seattle. Our chief national correspondent Matt Gutman has more from Los Angeles. Good morning, Matt.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LABOR DISPUTE THREATENING WEST COAST PORTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PORT OPERATORS ACCUSING DOCKWORKERS OF EFFECTIVELY SHUTTING DOWN TERMINALS\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Linsey. 40% of the all the cargo coming into the US goes into West Coast ports. The \uc2 Port of Los Angeles\uc2  here handled 10 million containers in 2022. But negotiations between Longshore Workers Union on the one hand, and shipping operators on the other, have languished over the past year. And since the weekend, the shipping operators have seen labor disruptions that they say have effectively shut down or are severely impacting some of the terminals at these major ports.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Basically what they're saying is that the longshore workers have not shown up for work. The biggest disruptions we saw in Oakland. Long lines of trucks there. But also in Tacoma, Washington and in Seattle. And the Longshore Workers Union is saying they are still negotiating, what they want they say is a greater share of the record profits that the shipping operators have seen over the past couple of years. But if these disruptions continue, that could significantly impact the supply chain. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230628ej650002z\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STOCKS SOAR AFTER JOBS REPORT MARKETS RALLY AFTER STRONG EMPLOYMENT NUMBERS\b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 June 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BUILDING, COLLAPSE, ALSTON, COLLIER, SHAFFER\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, TROPICAL STORM ARLENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, PENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENT MISSING\par \par \uc2 BURNS, CHINA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECRET VISIT TO CHINA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DEBT CEILING, DEBT DEAL, SCHUMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN ADDRESS TO THE NATION\par \par \uc2 STOCKS, JOBS, ECONOMY, EMPLOYMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STOCKS SOAR AFTER JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, of course, the White House considers that debt deal a major victory, and they also welcomed the news on the economy today. The major news on American jobs.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 339,000 JOBS ADDED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNEMPLOYMENT: 3.7%\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Employers adding 339,000 jobs last month. That's nearly double what analysts had predicted. Unemployment ticking up slightly to 3.7%.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOW JONES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 10,762.76, UP, 701.19, 2.12%\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Dow, today, soaring more than 700 points on the jobs news and on Congress clinching that debt ceiling deal.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's bring in our chief business correspondent tonight. And, Rebecca, I know you've been tracking these numbers and what this could all mean in the effort to tame inflation in the US.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, that's right, David. And this is a jobs report that doesn't make the Fed's job ahead any easier or clearer in its fight against inflation.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MARKETS RALLY AFTER STRONG EMPLOYMENT NUMBERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOBS ADDED\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We've now seen 14 straight months of job creation ahead of expectations. And while wages are starting to cool, they are now essentially keeping up with inflation. But economists would like to see that inflation continued to go lower. The Fed's job ahead in ten days is to make a new decision about interest rates.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And they will have to balance whether or not the rate hikes they've already done so far have taken their full effect, or more rate hikes are necessary. And, David, whether they can do that without causing a recession. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rebecca Jarvis here with us on a Friday as well. Thank you, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230606ej6200007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PILOTS ON THE PICKET LINE LABOR UNREST AT AIRLINES AND EFFECTS ON SUMMER TRAVEL\b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADO, TREVI\u209\'00\'D1O, VASQUEZ, VILLARREAL\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, CRISIS, PIERRE, VILLA, NICHOLS, URE\u209\'00\'D1A\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REALITY CHECK ON BORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL CHALLENGE TO COURT RULING ON PROGRAM TO EASE OVERCROWDING\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, DESANTIS, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN POWERHOUSES DUEL IN IOWA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESANTIS WOOS VOTERS, TRUMP CANCELS RALLY DUE TO TORNADO THREAT\par \par \uc2 ELECTION 2024, DESANTIS, IMMIGRATION, CRISIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNDECLARED RON DESANTIS HITS IOWA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOOS VOTERS AS HE WORKS TO GAIN GROUND ON TRUMP\par \par \uc2 WAR, EUROVISION, GERMANY, ZELENSKYY, POPE FRANCIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORTS OF A RUSSIAN STRIKE IN UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ATTACK LEAVES BUILDINGS IN FLAMES AS EUROVISION CONTESTS GETS UNDERWAY\par \par \uc2 BANGLADESH, MYANMAR, CYCLONE MOCHA, EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 TURKEY, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TURKISH VOTERS GO TO POLL IN CRUCIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OUTCOME COULD AFFECT NATO AND SUPPORT FOR UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, PAY HIKE, PILOTS, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PILOTS ON THE PICKET LINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LABOR UNREST AT AIRLINES AND EFFECTS ON SUMMER TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back at home now to the simmering labor unrest at some US airlines. Pilots taking to picket lines in several airports just as the busy summer travel season approaches. ABC's Elwyn Lopez joins us live from Atlanta with more. Elwyn, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 ELWYN LOPEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Janai, good morning. Summer travel about to kick into high gear. This as pilots for one of the major airlines are picketing for higher pay.\par \par \uc2 ELWYN LOPEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) United pilots have been flying without a raise for more than four years, that since before the pandemic. And now, they are marching with signs such as this one, depicting, "We delivered during difficult times." This after pilots unions for both Southwest and \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  voted to authorize a strike. As for Delta, the airline already greenlit a 34%-increase in pay for its pilots. Now, the likelihood to see a walkout is slim. That's because the federal law makes it quite difficult. The last time we saw a US carrier strike was more than a decade ago.\par \par \uc2 ELWYN LOPEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And in separate statements, both United and \uc2 Southwest Airlines\uc2  have reassured passengers that there will be no impact to their scheduled operations and they are continuing negotiations. Gio?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Elwyn Lopez, thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230613ej5e0005u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICA STRONG FORMER GARBAGE TRUCK WORKER SET TO GRADUATE FROM HARVARD LAW\b0\par\par\uc2 635 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 VERDICT, PROUD BOYS, GARLAND, TRUMP, CAPITOL RIOT\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, PATTERSON, ST. PIERRE, WALENSKY, JANSEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECT CHARGED IN MASS SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 CHOKEHOLD, NEELY, VAZQUEZ, ADAMS, HOCHUL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHOKEHOLD DEATH RULED A HOMICIDE\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, KIRBY, DRONE, ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIA BLAMES U.S. FOR KREMLIN ATTACK\par \par \uc2 THOMAS, CROW, DURBIN, TILLIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE THOMAS CONTROVERSY\par \par \uc2 SHEERAN, VERDICT, NEIS, COPYRIGHT INFRINGEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHEERAN WINS COPYRIGHT BATTLE\par \par \uc2 MARCUS GARVEY ACADEMY, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILD DEATH CLOSES SCHOOL\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 STATON, EDUCATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: #AMERICASTRONG\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, tonight here, "America Strong." He was the young, proud garbageman who shared with us his dream years ago. Well, clearly, he did not give up.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We have followed the extraordinary story of a proud young garbageman who dreamed of Harvard Law. Years later, he's now about to graduate, but not without paying it forward. We first introduce you to Rehan Staton from Bowie, Maryland three years ago. His single father raising him. And here's what Rehan first told us.\par \par \uc2 REHAN STATON (FORMER SANITATION WORKER / HARVARD LAW SCHOOL STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 Times are really tough. I mean, food insecurity, housing insecurity. We didn't have heat in the winter.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He was struggling.\par \par \uc2 REHAN STATON (FORMER SANITATION WORKER / HARVARD LAW SCHOOL STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 From high (inaudible), it was a low to 2.0 and I got denied by every single college I applied to. So, I just opted to go work for the local trash company.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Waking up at 4:00 AM to go to work, telling us the garbage men he worked with encouraged them to keep fighting for his dreams.\par \par \uc2 REHAN STATON (FORMER SANITATION WORKER / HARVARD LAW SCHOOL STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 They saw something in me. They uplifted me.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Rehan going back to school, getting his grades up at the University of Maryland.\par \par \uc2 REHAN STATON (FORMER SANITATION WORKER / HARVARD LAW SCHOOL STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 Go to work, clean my dumpsters, get off, go to school. Then after school, I'd go back to finish a shift and that was pretty much my day.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The next dream, Harvard Law.\par \par \uc2 REHAN STATON (FORMER SANITATION WORKER / HARVARD LAW SCHOOL STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 All right, ready?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And this was the moment he learned.\par \par \uc2 REHAN STATON (FORMER SANITATION WORKER / HARVARD LAW SCHOOL STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 All right, I am clicking it. Congratulations. Let's go. I got into Harvard. And really, it was probably just the greatest moment in my life.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And tonight, nearly three years later.\par \par \uc2 REHAN STATON (FORMER SANITATION WORKER / HARVARD LAW SCHOOL STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 Hi, David. Rehan here again.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He remembered to keep us updated, about to graduate in just weeks.\par \par \uc2 REHAN STATON (FORMER SANITATION WORKER / HARVARD LAW SCHOOL STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 The last time I talked to you, it was 2020. I just got accepted into Harvard Law School. And even to this day, I can't believe that happened.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And determined to keep his vow of paying it forward, raising an astonishing $70,000 with help from his old trash company, raising the money for janitors and support staff at Harvard, including Breon Merchant who was worked in the cafeteria for 16 years.\par \par \uc2 REHAN STATON (FORMER SANITATION WORKER / HARVARD LAW SCHOOL STUDENT)\par \par \uc2 Visibility matters. Quality-of-life matters. The fact that people know that they're being appreciated for the work they do, that matters. And that's always really important to me.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Important to all of us. We're cheering you on, Rehan, and all of the sanitation workers hard at work everyday. Paying in forward. Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230508ej540000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD WRITERS ON STRIKE FIRST LATE NIGHT SHOWS GO OFF THE AIR AS WALKOUT BEGINS\b0\par\par\uc2 584 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAUGHT\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTING, CAPTURED, OROPESA, CAPERS, PAUL\par \par \uc2 TROOPS, BORDER, BIDEN, COVID, MEXICO\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SCHOOL, TEEN, ARREST, SERBIA, INJURED\par \par \uc2 SECURITY, PALACE, ARREST, CORONATION, EXPLOSION\par \par \uc2 FOX, CARLSON, FIRING, "NYT", TEXT, DOMINION\par \par \uc2 FED, MARKETS, INTEREST RATE, HIKE, JOBS\par \par \uc2 WRITERS, STRIKE, WALKOUT, LATE SHOWS, STENTZ\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you, Robin. Now to the latest on the Hollywood writers' strike. Overnight the biggest late night shows airing reruns. Our chief national correspondent Matt Gutman is in LA with more. Good morning, Matt.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD WRITERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST LATE NIGHT SHOWS GO OFF THE AIR AS WALKOUT BEGINS\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Michael. That's right. Those late show writers were not in their writing rooms. They were out here in the streets picketing outside every major streamer and studio in Los Angeles and New York. And what they're basically demanding is a more equitable share of the profits from the media companies.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning in Hollywood, the placards are up.\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Writers got to get their pay.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the writers' pencils are down. And the late shows.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "\uc2 JIMMY KIMMEL\uc2  LIVE"\par \par \uc2 JIMMY KIMMEL\uc2  ("\uc2 JIMMY KIMMEL\uc2  LIVE")\par \par \uc2 Thank you for watching. Thank you for joining us.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "THE LATE SHOW WITH STEPHEN COLBERT"\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN COLBERT ("THE LATE SHOW WITH STEPHEN COLBERT")\par \par \uc2 I'm your host Stephen Colbert.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "THE TONIGHT SHOW WITH JIMMY FALLON"\par \par \uc2 JIMMY FALLON ("THE TONIGHT SHOW WITH JIMMY FALLON")\par \par \uc2 Welcome, everybody.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Reruns only. The writers' strike taking hold midnight yesterday. Hours later the writers taking to the streets. From New York to LA.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There are about 11,500 writers in the Writers Guild. 98% of them voted for this strike, that's why it's expected to see thousands of them here on the picket lines day after day until this ends.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Writers on average now getting paid 23% less than 15 years ago when adjusted for inflation.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How big an issue is the compensation issue at this point, making a living wage?\par \par \uc2 WRITER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 That's the biggest one.\par \par \uc2 WRITER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 That's the biggest one.\par \par \uc2 WRITER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It's the biggest one, yeah.\par \par \uc2 WRITER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Script payments, residuals, being paid a fair wage for the work we do.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The strike means any scripted projects, from film to TV, now on hold, including "Abbott Elementary," whose writers were originally set to meet this week for next season. The goal of this latest strike is securing a new three year contract addressing issues including pay in an age of streaming.\par \par \uc2 ZACK STENTZ (WORKING SCREENWRITER)\par \par \uc2 Strikes hurt a lot of people, not just writers. But the other members of the crew who get sidelined by production getting shut down.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now the unity we saw outside here the streets among writers and the support from the public was impressive. But in talking to veteran writers and organizers, they're telling me that after a number of weeks, the pressure to get writers and everybody else involved in that production ecosystem back to work begins to mount. Still, the writers say they have to stick it out because for them this is existential. Guys.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230524ej5300030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RESUME REMODEL DOES YOUR RESUME PASS THE SIX SECONDS TEST?\b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAUGHT\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, SHOOTING, CAPTURED, OROPESA, CAPERS, PAUL\par \par \uc2 TROOPS, BORDER, BIDEN, COVID, MEXICO\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SCHOOL, TEEN, ARREST, SERBIA, INJURED\par \par \uc2 SECURITY, PALACE, ARREST, CORONATION, EXPLOSION\par \par \uc2 FOX, CARLSON, FIRING, "NYT", TEXT, DOMINION\par \par \uc2 FED, MARKETS, INTEREST RATE, HIKE, JOBS\par \par \uc2 WRITERS, STRIKE, WALKOUT, LATE SHOWS, STENTZ\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , LAKERS, WARRIORS, \uc2 KNICKS\uc2 , HEAT, EMBIID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "GUARDIANS OF THE GALAXY"\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, SATTERFIELD, LIES, INSURANCE\par \par \uc2 STABBINGS, \uc2 UC DAVIS\uc2 , DEAD, PYTEL, NAJM\par \par \uc2 CAR THEFTS, AIRTAGS, CHELL, MADDREY, KIAS, HYUNDAIS\par \par \uc2 CORONATION, REHEARSALS, MILITARY, KING CHARLES\par \par \uc2 REYNOLDS, MCELHENNY, WREXHAM, SOCCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN STORM\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, ARRESTS, SHOOTING, TEXAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS MASS SHOOTING SUSPECT CAPTURED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARRESTED BY AUTHORITIES IN NEARBY TOWN\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, TRUMP, WITNESSES, CIVIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WITNESSES BACK ACCUSER IN TRUMP CIVIL TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT WILL NOT TAKE THE STAND\par \par \uc2 ALHEIMER'S, DRUG, TRIAL, SIDE EFFECTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRELIMINARY DATA ON NEW ALZHEIMER'S DRUG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 ELI LILLY\uc2 : TREATMENT SLOWS COGNITIVE DECLINE\par \par \uc2 RESUME, SIX SECONDS, REFRESH, EMPLOYMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RESUME REMODEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOES YOUR RESUME PASS THE SIX SECONDS TEST?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back with our "GMA" cover story. And if you're looking for a job, according to a story in "The Wall Street Journal," you could have just six seconds, six seconds, to make an impression on future employers with your resume. Rebecca Jarvis is back to help us. Hey there, Rebecca, let's I want to get right to it. have a mockup resume we're going to show folks. So, to start, should job seekers include a bio paragraph at the top of the resume?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, so, Robin, in the fateful words of Eminem, you get one shot, one opportunity. Same thing is true with this resume. You've got your six seconds to impress. And one of the most important things you can do when you look at this mockup resume, you no longer need that explanation paragraph. You just want to turn that idea at the top of your resume into a quick statement about who you are. So in this case, the mockup resume says sales manager with decades of experience, eager for an opportunity. That's a lot of verbiage to convey the idea you can convey in one single statement, which is you are a senior software sales manager. That's where you want to go with this instead of all those words to convey the same thing, Robin.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE TINY TWEAKS THAT CAN MAKE A BIG DIFFERENCE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, because that's quite a difference. I'm just getting hives talking about the resume because bringing back some memories here. But what if you have a variety, a variety of work experience? Should people be altering for each job they apply for?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, Robin, I just want to address the hives thing because that can, this is a stressful experience for everybody. But there are 9.5 million job openings right now. So if you're looking, it's a good time to hunt. Now, on that idea of experience, the younger you are, the less this is as important. But as you get farther out in your career, you want to make sure the experience you're putting down is totally relevant to the job you're seeking. So in the case of that mockup resume, if you're seeking the senior sales manager job, and you had experience working at an ice cream shop for a summer years ago, not necessarily the information you want to include there.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You want to include all of the relevant things. But like I said, if you're just coming out of college, and you've got a mixture of experience, and you want to convey who you are to that employer, it's something you might still include. But again, farther down in your career, strike it out, keep to the specifics on what you're good for and why you're going for this particular job.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is correct. Always good, good insight and advice there, Rebecca. We thank you. Okay, get off the street now. Get off the street. All right.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230524ej530003e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOLLYWOOD WRITERS GO ON STRIKE UNION & MEDIA COMPANIES FAIL TO AGREE ON NEW CONTRACT TERMS\b0\par\par\uc2 609 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 DUST STORM, TRAVEL, DEVORE, STARRICK, THOMAS\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMS ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DANGEROUS WIND TAKES AIM AT SOUTHEAST, SPRING SNOW THREAT FOR NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, BIDEN, CONGRESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEBT LIMIT SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TREASURY SECRETARY WARS U.S. COULD DEFAULT BY JUNE 1ST\par \par \uc2 WRITERS GUILD, PROTEST, PATTEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLLYWOOD WRITERS GO ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION & MEDIA COMPANIES FAIL TO AGREE ON NEW CONTRACT TERMS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to breaking news overnight. Hollywood writers going on strike, bringing many productions to an immediate stop, including some of the biggest shows on TV. Our chief national correspondent Matt Gutman is in Los Angeles with more.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the Hollywood juggernaut grinding to a halt. The Writers Guild telling its members to prepare to start picketing this afternoon after the union and the association of media companies failed to agree to new contract terms. The first to feel the effects of this strike, late night comedy shows like ABC's "Jimmy Kimmel Live."\par \par \uc2 JIMMY KIMMEL\uc2  (HOST "JIMMY KIMMEL LIVE")\par \par \uc2 Guillermo speaks better Hebrew than George Santos.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And "Saturday Night Live."\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 So, are you officially leaving?\par \par \uc2 PETE DAVIDSON (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, man. Lorne accidentally gifted me a sock, so I'm free.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Pete Davidson is set to host this Saturday. Now, he may not. The writers say streaming's lack of a seasonal calendar has hurt their pay and AI could transform the media landscape for the worse.\par \par \uc2 DOMINIC PATTEN (SENIOR EDITOR "DEADLINE")\par \par \uc2 Writers now are no longer paid as much as they used to be. They're paid for shorter series and they're not seeing any of the residual that you used to see back in the old days.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With blockbuster franchise movies like "Guardians of the Galaxy: Volume 3" out in theaters this Friday...\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "GUARDIANS OF THE GALAXY: VOLUME 3"\par \par \uc2 ZOE SALDANA ("GUARDIANS OF THE GALAXY: VOLUME 3")\par \par \uc2 Was that who you were in love with? It sounds more like her.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS PRATT ("GUARDIANS OF THE GALAXY: VOLUME 3")\par \par \uc2 Her? That's ridiculous.\par \par \uc2 KAREN GILLAN ("GUARDIANS OF THE GALAXY: VOLUME 3")\par \par \uc2 Do not pull me into this. Knock it off.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS PRATT ("GUARDIANS OF THE GALAXY: VOLUME 3")\par \par \uc2 What?\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) What happens beyond that isn't clear. The last writers' strike back in 2007 lasted 100 days, costing California's economy an estimated $2.1 billion. But the impact of this new strike could go far beyond Hollywood and New York. Take Georgia, for instance, where movie and TV production pumped more than $4 billion into the local economy last year.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM TV SERIES, "STRANGER THINGS"\par \par \uc2 PRODUCTION CREW MEMBER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Georgia is a leader in the world. We're top three typically production city. We're going to feel it more than most other markets and feel it, you know, just as much as New York or LA would.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, the Writers Guild has described this as an existential moment. And it's worth noting that the Alliance of Media Companies in those negotiations last night said that they offered generous increases in compensation for writers and, ultimately, they are fully committed to reaching a mutually beneficial deal. But if the last strike is any indication, it could be a while. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, so many people affected by this. I hope they can end this soon. Thank you so much, Matt.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230522ej520005p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WRITERS STRIKE FIRST STRIKE IN 15 YEARS\b0\par\par\uc2 2,057 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 May 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 WRITER, STRIKE, HOLLYWOOD, PATTEN, COLVIN\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening. We begin tonight with Hollywood grinding to a standstill as writers pick nationwide put their pencils down and pick up their protest signs for the first time in 15 years. They're demanding a new deal from the production studios, one that accounts for today's streaming reality and tomorrow's AI. So how long could strike go on? And at what cost? ABC's Matt Gutman is in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WRITERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 No content.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) From Los Angeles to New York City, today thousands of writers leaving behind the writers room for the picket line\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WRITER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I was here in '07. I will be here today. I will be here tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \u8230\'20\'26as the first strike to hit Hollywood in 15 years is now officially underway. Spotted among the New York crowd, Jimmy Fallon's sidekick Steve Higgins and "SNL" star Aidy Bryant. And in Los Angeles actor Rob Lowe.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How long are you willing seriously to picket out here and not to work?\par \par \uc2 LOLA SCARPITTA (MEMBER OF WRITERS GUILD OF AMERICA)\par \par \uc2 As long as it takes.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ten days.\par \par \uc2 LOLA SCARPITTA (MEMBER OF WRITERS GUILD OF AMERICA)\par \par \uc2 As long as it takes.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WRITER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We're not gonna give in.\par \par \uc2 COLLEEN WERTHMANN (MEMBER OF WRITERS GUILD OF AMERICA)\par \par \uc2 We wanna make people happy and we also wanna be able to afford, like, diapers for our babies or, you know, to go out to eat. And it's corporations' job to be cheap and be profitable. But it's our job to push back and go, no, no, no, no, no.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Latenight talk shows, the first to feel the effect. Already showing reruns tonight. And if the strike lasts long enough, your favorite scripted series could also be hit.\par \par \uc2 DOMINIC PATTEN (SENIOR EDITOR OF "DEADLINE")\par \par \uc2 We might be looking at months and months and months. The reality is, most writers start working on shows that are gonna appear on the networks in September, October now. If their pen is down, fingers off keyboards, that eventually, within a couple of weeks, you're gonna see that schedule getting really jammed up.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXT OF STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After weeks of negotiations, the Writers Guild Of America, which represents more than 11,000 writers, and the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2 , which represents the studios and production companies, were unable to reach a deal. The WGA releasing a statement, writing in part, "The company's behavior has created a gig economy inside a union workforce, and their immovable stance in this negotiation has betrayed a commitment to further devaluing the profession of writing."\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And at the center of the fight, streaming and the ripple effects it's had on the industry.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How big of an issue is the compensation issue at this point? Making a living wage?\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WRITER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 That's the biggest one.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WRITER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It's the biggest one.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WRITER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It's the biggest one, yeah.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WRITER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Script payments, residuals, being paid a fair wage for the work we do. It's, it's, not, we're not trying to get rich. We wanna make a living doing what we love.\par \par \uc2 DOMINIC PATTEN (SENIOR EDITOR OF "DEADLINE")\par \par \uc2 If you wanna look at the main points that the Writers Guild had bringing into these negotiations, it was money. Very simply money, transparency and time. A little while ago we used to talk about network shows, 23 episodes, season after season. Now, we're talking about streaming. Six episodes that can take months and months to write. So a lot less compensation over, over on average.\par \par \uc2 ALEX COLVIN (DEAN OF INDUSTRIAL & LABOR RELATIONS SCHOOL AT CORNELL UNIV.)\par \par \uc2 Traditionally, replaying of shows on television would be something that would generate residuals for the writers and was an important part of their income. And it really comes out of that bread-and-butter question of, you know, what is their income gonna be?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXT OF STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On the other side of the fight are studios and streaming services that have seen a drop in stock prices, prompting a number of layoffs in recent months, including at \uc2 Disney\uc2 , ABC's parent company. The \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  says it "presented a comprehensive package proposal to the Guild last night, which included generous increases in compensation for writers, as well as improvements in streaming residuals" and that "member companies remain united in their" stance " to reach a deal that is mutually beneficial to writers and the health and longevity of the industry."\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WRITERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 United we'll never be defeated.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But this strike could go far beyond writers rooms. It's estimated to put as many as 20,000 workers out of a job as various productions shut down.\par \par \uc2 DOMINIC PATTEN (SENIOR EDITOR OF "DEADLINE")\par \par \uc2 There's gonna be no craft services table, 'cause there's gonna be no production, because there's a strike. Those vendors, who are a multi-billion dollar industry here in Los Angeles County, they're no longer gonna have work. You are certainly gonna see this hit Los Angeles County pretty hard because Hollywood is one of the biggest industries around here. And if Hollywood's not working, everybody else isn't working that much either.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is not the first time Hollywood writers put pencils down.\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF 2007 NEWS REPORT\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Hollywood writer strike that began today. The first industrywide walkout by TV and movie writers in almost 20 years.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In 2007, the Guild said writers weren't getting their fair share for what was distributed on the internet.\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF WGA PRESS CONFERENCE\par \par \uc2 GUILD SPOKESPERSON (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Although the industry's pie is continually growing, our share continues to shrink.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Writers were then joined on the picket line by some of TV's biggest stars. The strike lasted 100 days, leaving the latenight hosts like \uc2 David Letterman\uc2  with plenty of time to grow a beard. And Conan O'Brien, plenty of airtime to fill. Dozens of scripted series like "Grey's Anatomy" and "Gossip Girl" ultimately shortened their seasons, while reality TV got its breakout moment with networks debuting shows like "Big Brother" and "Celebrity Apprentice."\par \par \uc2 CLIP OF TV SHOW "CELEBRITY APPRENTICE"\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  ("CELEBRITY APPRENTICE")\par \par \uc2 Tiffany, you're fired.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ESTIMATE $2 BILLION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 30,000 JOBS\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The strike ended up costing the California economy an estimated $2 billion and affected more than 30,000 jobs. Among the concessions writers ultimately won were that streaming shows would have to hire Guild writers when their budgets were big enough. Sasha Stewart was on the picket lines in New York today. She's been part of the WGA since 2014.\par \par \uc2 SASHA STEWART (COUNCIL MEMBER OF WRITERS GUILD OF AMERICA)\par \par \uc2 We have minimums, thanks to the union. We have health insurance thanks to union. All of that is thanks to union workers who struck in the past and earn those for us. And now I'm a part of it.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 She started her career as an intern on "The Colbert Report." Later, writing for "The Nightly Show with Larry Wilmore."\par \par \uc2 SASHA STEWART (COUNCIL MEMBER OF WRITERS GUILD OF AMERICA)\par \par \uc2 When I got my start as a writer, I was so excited. And then as the years went on, I started to see longer and longer gaps in employment. It was harder to get jobs and it was harder to have jobs that would last for long enough in order to qualify for health insurance. So I've really seen my life as a writer go from something where I felt like it was very stable and secure to feeling very unstable and insecure.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WRITERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Corporate greed has got to go.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And back in 2019, Stewart saw the power of her union firsthand.\par \par \uc2 SASHA STEWART (COUNCIL MEMBER OF WRITERS GUILD OF AMERICA)\par \par \uc2 I was diagnosed with cancer. It was scary. It was painful. And it was a very difficult treatment and recovery. I would get these bills from the hospital for $50,000 for a round of chemo. And then thanks to my health insurance, it would be $100.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She's now in remission and wants to ensure she can continue her career as a writer.\par \par \uc2 SASHA STEWART (COUNCIL MEMBER OF WRITERS GUILD OF AMERICA)\par \par \uc2 The overall picture is that the WGA just wants and we just want for writers to be able to make a living writing. I know it sounds simple, but that's all we are asking for. We're not asking for anything radical or revolutionary.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And like 2007, changing technology is once again a big concern for the entrance of AI into the scene. In short, writers don't want robots doing their jobs.\par \par \uc2 DOMINIC PATTEN (SENIOR EDITOR OF "DEADLINE")\par \par \uc2 They were completely in separate places because clearly the studios are looking at AI. If they're looking at, at bringing the writers down tomorrow, like what they called as a gig economy or day players, AI could play a huge role in that for the studios and they clearly want to keep as much control as possible. For the writers, they're being smart about this one. They know that AI will have a huge effect on their industry. And they wanna put some guardrails in place.\par \par \uc2 ALEX COLVIN (DEAN OF INDUSTRIAL & LABOR RELATIONS SCHOOL AT CORNELL UNIV.)\par \par \uc2 This could set a framework for the next 15 years. Is an AI tool gonna be writing a whole screen play in 15 years' time? Maybe. They are concerned about the job security aspect. Are they going to retain the rights to work?\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And now, the labor movement has new momentum, not just in Hollywood. From \uc2 Home Depot\uc2  to \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , American workers are seeking out better pay, benefits, and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 DOMINIC PATTEN (SENIOR EDITOR OF "DEADLINE")\par \par \uc2 I've been covering Hollywood labor relations for about a decade. I have never seen the atmosphere and the tone the way it is here right now in Hollywood. Usually there's at least one or two writers I will talk to, who are a little bit more conservative. And they'll say, look, I think the studios might have a point. Everyone I've spoken to has said the time for action is now.\par \par \uc2 ALEX COLVIN (DEAN OF INDUSTRIAL & LABOR RELATIONS SCHOOL AT CORNELL UNIV.)\par \par \uc2 This strike definitely fits this pattern we're seeing of increased labor conflict post-pandemic. We have seen year over year increases in strike numbers. I think it also fits a pattern we're seeing of greater union labor activity in the creative arts and media industries in general. The media industry has, has really been disrupted in recent years by some big changes. That's producing a lot of conflict. And, and I think this is a manifestation of that.\par \par \uc2 STRIKING WRITER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 What do we want?\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Back on the picket line, writers don't know how long they'll be out of work. But they do know they're determined to put up a fight.\par \par \uc2 COLLEEN WERTHMANN (MEMBER OF WRITERS GUILD OF AMERICA)\par \par \uc2 Is it gonna be hard? Is it gonna suck? Yeah, sure. But, like, what doesn't? Like, if you wanna fight for something, you gotta just buckle in and then you'll get it.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Matt.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "A SMALL LIGHT"\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Up next, a powerful new drama about the woman who helped make sure Anne Frank's diary was shared with the world. Why sharing her story is so important today.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020230504ej5200002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ISRAEL STRIKES BACK AFTER ROCKET ATTACKS ISRAEL TARGETS GAZA STRIP AFTER ROCKETS FIRED FROM LEBANON\b0\par\par\uc2 470 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GUN REFORM, PEARSON, EXPULSION, JONES, SEXTON, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 AFGHANISTAN, REPORT, WITHDRAWAL, BIDEN, KIRBY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WH REVIEW OF CHAOTIC AFGHAN EXIT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE STORMS SWEEP EAST\par \par \uc2 THOMAS, \uc2 PROPUBLICA\uc2 , CROW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE THOMAS UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, ISRAEL, PALESTINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL STRIKES BACK AFTER ROCKET ATTACKS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Overseas now, a new round of violent clashes in the Middle East. Palestinian worshipers barricading themselves inside al-Aqsa Mosque in Jerusalem, one of Islam's holiest sites. Israeli police forces removed them. And now dozens of rockets have been fired on Israel from inside Lebanon, and Israel is striking back. ABC's Matt Gutman is in Israel for us.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL TARGETS GAZA STRIP AFTER ROCKETS FIRED FROM LEBANON\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Israeli airstrikes lighting up parts of the Gaza Strip after Palestinian militant groups fired a barrage of rockets into Israel from Lebanon this afternoon. Dozens of rockets streaked across the sky to Israel's north, sirens wailing. Regional tensions at a boiling point since Israeli forces stormed the al-Aqsa Mosque multiple times this week during Ramadan. This the largest bombardment Israel has faced from Lebanon since 2006. Israeli military saying its iron dome defense system intercepted 25 rockets but that at least five landed inside Israel. A thick column of smoke rising after one rocket slammed into a bank. At least two people injured.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And this week, night after night, those clashes at the al-Aqsa Mosque in Jerusalem, one of Islam's holiest sites. On Wednesday, Palestinian worshipers attempting to barricade themselves inside the mosque, pelting police with rocks and chairs. And earlier this week, when Israeli police stormed the mosque, they were blasted with fireworks and beating barricaded demonstrators with their weapons. The video sending shock waves throughout the Muslim world.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Linsey, Israel tonight specifically signaling out \uc2 Hamas\uc2  for all of today's attacks. And just minutes ago, the Israeli air force said that it had targeted \uc2 Hamas\uc2  tunnels and weapons factories in the Gaza Strip. And in anticipation of possible Palestinian retaliation, major Israeli cities tonight opening up bomb shelters. Linsey?\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Matt, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PENSION PROTESTS TURN VIOLENT\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And in France, a new round of protests in the months' long resistance, to President Macro's planned to raise the retirement age from 62 to 64.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hundreds of thousands marching through the streets, some setting fires and vandalizing stores, including a Paris restaurant patronized by President Macron himself. Officials say fewer workers participated in today's strike, but the trade unions are calling for more protests next Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230407ej4600006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STRIKE SHUTS LOS ANGELES SCHOOL FOR SECOND DAY SERVICE WORKERS' UNION CALLS FOR HIGHER WAGES\b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD BREAKING STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, SNOW, HOPPIN, HIGHWAYS\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, HOWELL, INVESTIGATIONS, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 FED, INTEREST RATES, BANKING, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, VIDEO, 911, DEATH, OUKO, INDICTED\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, LAUSD, WAGES, STUDENTS, PARENTS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Pierre Thomas with those new developments, thank you. In Los Angeles this morning, more than 400,000 students will be staying home again. A strike shutting down school for a second day. Kayna Whitworth has the latest.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRIKE SHUTS LOS ANGELES SCHOOL FOR SECOND DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARENTS REACT AS SERVICE WORKERS' UNION CALLS FOR HIGHER WAGES\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning the city of angels preparing itself for day two of a massive strike that is shutting down the second largest school district in the country.\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Fight for your wages.\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Education.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) More than 60,000 school service workers, including teachers, aides, bus drivers and cafeteria workers, hitting the picket lines after their contract negotiations stalled. Teachers supporting them in the three day strike.\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 SEIU\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 STRIKERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 UTLA\par \par \uc2 DEANNA ESABALIDIS (INSTRUCTIONAL AID)\par \par \uc2 We can't afford to pay our rent.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The service workers' union, without a contract since 2020, is calling for higher wages, and claiming the superintendent reportedly called their planned strike a circus. With more than 420,000 students in the district out of class, some parents concerned about the impact on their kids.\par \par \uc2 PARENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I feel that they're probably being left behind.\par \par \uc2 JANELLE ALLEN (TEACHER)\par \par \uc2 I know parents are frustrated by the strike, but I want parents to know our working conditions are our children's learning conditions. And we want what's best for our children.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The LA School Superintendent saying, they're "Ready to return to negotiations" and defending the district's offer of a 23% pay increase over five years. But the union says that's not enough. Many service workers living below the poverty line. The median income just $25,000 a year.\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY JACKSON (CAPTAIN OF SECURITY)\par \par \uc2 I'm one of those people that's working $25,000 a year trying to make it, and it's really hard. I live check to check.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Community volunteers steeping up to help, recreation centers providing three days' worth of school lunches for LAUSD families to pick up. \uc2 LA Rams\uc2  Super Bowl Champ Aaron Donald, among those pitching in to pack meals for students.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now some parents also spoke out at a school board meeting yesterday, expressing concern that this strike is actually hurting the students. One parent going so far as to say that the fight in the district should be about education, not power. Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230424ej3m00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LOS ANGELES SCHOOL WORKERS GO ON STRIKE 65,000 WORKERS TO WALK OFF HE JOB FOR THREE DAYS\b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON TRUMP\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, INDICTMENT, COHEN, COSTELLO, DESANTIS, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 FIRST REPUBLIC BANK\uc2 , FALLOUT, RATES, AMAZON, LAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, HOSPITAL, MURDER, WAPO, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 LA, SCHOOL, WORKERS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the strike in the nation's second largest school district. About 65,000 staff members are walking out of schools in Los Angeles this morning, rallying against what they call unfair work practices. Kayna Whitworth joins us with that. Good morning, Kayna.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES SCHOOL WORKERS GO ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 65,000 WORKERS TO WALK OFF THE JOB FOR THREE DAYS OVER 'UNFAIR PRACTICES'\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning. So, the \uc2 LAUSD\uc2  superintendent says today will be a difficult day. We're talking about more than a half a million students at a thousand different schools that will be out of class today. And you can see here behind me, they have already gathered on this cold, rainy morning. We're outside of the district bus depot, and it's service workers like this, the bus workers, the custodians, the cafeteria workers that are asking for a pay increase and better working conditions.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCHOOL WORKER UNION DEMANDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 30% PAY INCREASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INCREASED STAFFING TO IMPROVE LEARNING AND SAFETY\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And they will be joined in force by the union teachers who say negotiations with the district broke down. They also claim that the district broke confidentiality rules.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But the district superintendent says he not only offered a pay increase that does fall short of their demands, but says that he made himself available all day on Monday to discuss this and that he was never approached. Now, he says he will be available again today. He certainly hopes to resolve this. But, Whit, in the meantime, they will have food and supervised sites available for families that need it. But again, Whit, they do expect this strike to last at least three days.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, hundreds of thousands students caught in the middle of it. All right, Kayna. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230421ej3l00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STRIKE CLOSES LA SCHOOLS SCHOOL SERVICE WORKERS FIGHT FOR PAY INCREASE\b0\par\par\uc2 588 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP, EVIDENCE, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, HOWELL, DANIELS\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, MURDER, POLICE CUSTODY, VIDEO, OUKO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIDEO FROM POLICE CUSTODY DEATH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR STORM CORSSING U.S.\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, LAUSD, SERVICE WORKERS, CARVALHO, ARIAS, JACKSON\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Meantime, also in Los Angeles, a massive strike shutting down the nation's second largest school district. More than 30,000 staff members including school aides, bus drivers, cafeteria workers and custodians all walking off the job.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Members picketing in that rain today. Teachers also walking out in support.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The union which has been without a contract since 2020 saying its 30,000 members are barely making minimum wage as costs in southern California soar. ABC's Kayna Whitworth tonight in California.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, streets in downtown Los Angeles packed with protesters\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (inaudible)\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 (inaudible)\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...as \uc2 Los Angeles Unified School District\uc2  service workers strike for better wages and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It looks like this for blocks as teachers have joined the service workers in solidarity. They're out here supporting the custodians, the bus drivers, the cafeteria workers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSES CANCELED FOR 420,000 STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 420,000 STUDENTS OUT OF CLASS\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nearly half a million students across a thousand different schools likely out of class for days, leaving some parents scrambling.\par \par \uc2 PARENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 It's a shuffle, yeah. It becomes kind of juggling and that's, that's the last minute, or just the shorter notice, I think, this time is harder.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The school district setting up food distribution and child supervision sites.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "...READY TO RETURN TO NEGOTIATIONS..."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DISTRICT'S OFFER ADDRESSES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "...THE NEEDS AND CONCERNS FROM THE UNION, WHILE ALSO REMAINING FISCALLY RESPONSIBLE..."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 ALBERTO M. CARVALHO\uc2 , LOS ANGELES UNIFIED SUPERINTENDENT\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And late today, the superintendent saying they're ready to return to negotiations, defending the district's offer as addressing the needs and concerns from the union, while also remaining fiscally responsibility.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES SCHOOL WORKER UNION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REJECTED 23% RAISE OVER 5 YEARS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMANDS 30% RAISE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEDIAN INCOME: $25,000 PER YEAR\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the union says the district offer of a 23% pay increase over five years simply isn't enough. They want 30%. Many service workers living below the poverty line. The median income just $25,000 a year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCHOOL SERVICE WORKERS FIGHT FOR PAY INCREASE\par \par \uc2 ANTHONY JACKSON (UNION WORKER)\par \par \uc2 I'm one of the people that, that working 25,000 a year, trying to make it and it's really hard. I live check to check.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The union leader telling me this strike was a last resort.\par \par \uc2 MAX ARIAS (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR \uc2 SEIU\uc2  LOCAL 99)\par \par \uc2 We're not seeking to strike. This is a sacrifice. Half of our members are parents of a student in LAUSD.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And David, this strike will likely last for two more days. The superintendent says he's ready to negotiate, but the union leader's telling me they don't want to settle and they also say - it's highly possible that there is an open ended strike coming down the line. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kayna Whitworth in Los Angeles tonight. Thank you, Kayna.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230323ej3l00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FIERY PROTESTS AND LABOR STRIKES IN FRANCE CITIZENS FIGHT AGAINST NEW LAW TO RAISE RETIREMENT AGE\b0\par\par\uc2 440 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BITTER WIND CHILLS AND FREEZE WARNINGS: ARCTIC BLAST\par \par \uc2 ARCTIC, NORTHEAST, FREEZE\par \par \uc2 TURKEY, \uc2 NATO\uc2 , FINLAND, PARLIAMENT, PUTIN, UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 XI, PUTIN, CHINA, RUSSIA, UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 TIKTOK, BYTEDANCE, BIDEN, JEAN-PIERRE, TSARYNNY\par \par \uc2 SVB, BIDEN, BANKS, BANKRUPTCY, MCBRIDE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 , BAN\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, LABOR, STRIKES, FRANCE, RETIREMENT AGE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, now to the violent protests in France. Demonstrators clashing with police as a labor strike leaves trash piling up on the streets of Paris. ABC's Ines de la Cuetara is in Paris with the policy change that is sparking outrage, and this has been going on for a few months. Ines, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Janai. And it's not the Paris you typically think of, but this is what Paris looks like right now, mounds and mounds of trash piling up as garbage collectors go on strike to protest pension reforms. They've been on strike for days, more than 10,000 tons of trash piling up across the city, and some workers now are being forced to go back to work to start cleaning up. We're also seeing massive protests breaking out around the country. Millions have been taking to the streets since mid-January to protest reforms. And here in Paris overnight, we did see protesters setting fires right in the heart of the city and even clashing with police officers.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This comes as French President Macron tries to reform pensions. He's trying to raise the minimum retirement age from 62 to 64. He argues he doesn't have a choice, that people are living longer, and that the government will go in the red should the system stay as is. Demonstrators, though, are arguing that there are other ways to finance pensions, and they're also frustrated with the way Macron is going about it here. Macron is using a procedure similar to executive action in the US to try and get this through, and many demonstrators say that is anti-Democratic.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, we are expecting these strikes and protests to continue over the next few weeks. The Macron government is hoping the law will go into effect by this summer. And on Monday, lawmakers will be holding a vote of no confidence in Macron's government, though that is not expected to pass. Guys.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Something to watch closely. Ines, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230418ej3i00031\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW ARRESTS IN INMATE DEATH THREE HOSPITAL WORKERS CHARGED WITH MURDER\b0\par\par\uc2 407 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, DRONE, RYDER\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWERFUL CROSS-COUNTRY STORM\par \par \uc2 BANKS, YELLEN, RESCUE PLAN, ONGWESO, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $30 BILLION BANK RESCUE PLAN\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, OUKO, ARREST, EXCESSIVE FORCE, BASKERVILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW ARRESTS IN INMATE DEATH\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, the emotional mother before the cameras after seeing the video of her son dying in custody, authorities say, at the hands of police and workers at a mental health facility. Seven deputies already charged. And tonight, three hospital workers now also charged in the murder. Here's Pierre Thomas.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THREE HOSPITAL WORKERS CHARGED WITH MURDER\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the family of Irvo Otieno furious, saying, a video yet to be released, shows he was intentionally and cruelly abused before he died in the custody of Virginia deputies. Today, we hear from the mother who saw that video.\par \par \uc2 CAROLINE OUKO (MOTHER OF IRVO OTIENO)\par \par \uc2 My son was treated like a dog, worse than a dog. I saw it with my own eyes on the video. My son was tortured.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And tonight, three members of the staff at the Central State Psychiatric Hospital, where Otieno was being admitted on March 6th, now accused of second-degree murder, just two days after seven deputies were charged for allegedly killing Otieno. Prosecutors say the video shows those seven deputies and staff holding Otieno face down on the ground for 12 minutes with Otieno in handcuffs and leg irons.\par \par \uc2 ANN C BASKERVILL (DINWIDDIE COUNTY COMMONWEALTH'S ATTORNEY)\par \par \uc2 He died of asphyxia. He suffocated as a result of that pressure.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And allegations of a cover-up intensifying. Deputies accused of washing handcuffs used to keep Otieno under control. And those deputies allegedly failed to call state police for three-and-a-half hours as his body lay in the hospital. And the prosecutor says, when hospital staff called 911, they suggested it was a cardiac arrest.\par \par \uc2 ANN C BASKERVILL (DINWIDDIE COUNTY COMMONWEALTH'S ATTORNEY)\par \par \uc2 The hospital ought to know better, but it was the, it was central state that made that 911 call.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, tonight, sources tell us there's no final decision on whether that apparently disturbing and graphic video will ever be released. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Pierre Thomas with us again. Thank you, Pierre.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230317ej3g00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DRAMATIC RISE IN EMPLOYMENT SCAMS HOW CRIMINALS ARE TRICKING JOB SEEKERS OUT OF MONEY\b0\par\par\uc2 1,105 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 AIR SCARE, TORRES, ARREST, UNITED\par \par \uc2 STORM, YANEZ, SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRACING FOR EVEN MORE SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UP TO FIVE MORE FEET TAKING AIM AT CALIFORNIA MOUNTAINS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOWED IN FOR DAYS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOME TRAPPED CALIFORNIA RESIDENTS RUNNING LOW ON SUPPLIES\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, SNOW, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "ATMOSPHERIC RIVER" TAKES AIM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVEN MORE SNOW SET TO SLAM HARD-HIT WEST COAST\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, DETENTION, TITLE 42\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DETENTION FOR MIGRANT FAMILIES?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: BIDEN ADMINISTRATION CONSIDERS RESTARTING BORDER POLICY\par \par \uc2 DOMESTIC TERRORISM, ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TERROR CHARGES IN "COP CITY" ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOZENS ARRESTED AFTER CHAOTIC CLASHES WITH ATLANTA POLICE\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, WAR, UKRAINE, PRIGOZHIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLOODY BATTLE FOR KEY CITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINIANS VOW NOT TO RETREAT AS RUSSIAN TROOPS ENCIRCLE BAKHMUT\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, ELECTION, DRISKELL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA GOV DESANTIS TAKES CENTER STAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SET TO PRESS CULTURAL ISSUES IN MAJOR SPEECH AHEAD OF POSSIBLE 2024 RUN\par \par \uc2 MARCH MADNESS, FURMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 43 YEARS IN THE MAKING!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FURMAN HEADING TO FIRST NCAA TOURNAMENT SINCE 1980\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 KIDNAPPING, MEXICO, JEAN-PIERRE, GRANT, PRICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH FOR AMERICANS KIDNAPPED IN MEXICO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FOUR PEOPLE ABDUCTED IN BROAD DAYLIGHT AFTER CROSSING THE BORDER\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYMENT, SCAMS, MCGOVERN, HEIM, FISHER, OWENS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRAMATIC RISE IN EMPLOYMENT SCAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW CRIMINAL ARE TRICKING JOB SEEKERS OUT OF MONEY\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to a new warning about employment scams. According to the Better Business Bureau's risk report, there has been a dramatic rise in criminals trying to trick job seekers into sending them money. Becky Worley is here with those details for us. Good morning, Becky.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, good morning. We've recently seen an increase in layoffs in the tech sector. People switching jobs for work-from-home opportunities and they have sparked rapid rise in employment scams. \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  saying they've removed more than 190,000 fake accounts in a six-month period in 2022. And it's a stark warning to job seekers, slow down and protect yourself.\par \par \uc2 RECORDED VOICE MESSAGE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hello, this is a courtesy invitation to work with Amazon from home.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Experts saying, this is not a real request.\par \par \uc2 RECORDED VOICE MESSAGE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 You make up to $400 in a day.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But one in an arsenal of more sophisticated methods that scammers are using to steal thousands of dollars from job seekers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 2022 BBB SCAM TRACKER RISK REPORT\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a new report from the Better Business Bureau, employment scams listed as the second riskiest of all the scams they track saying, the frequency at which they're being reported in the agency scam tracker increasing 23% from 2021 to 2022.\par \par \uc2 MELANIE MCGOVERN (SPOKESPERSON BETTER BUSINESS BUREAU)\par \par \uc2 A lot of workers don't want to go back to an office, so they're searching online for a purely remote position. Unfortunately, scammers know this, so they're setting up fake websites and they're luring people in with that.\par \par \uc2 CALLIE HEIM (VICTIM OF JOB APPLICATION SCAM)\par \par \uc2 They said they liked my resume and my application and they wanted to move the process along.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For Callie Heim from West Palm Beach, Florida, she said she applied for a tech position through the jobsite \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2 , but the people who posted it were suspected scammers not affiliated with the actual tech company or \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2 . They offered her this job and sent her a check to purchase her own office equipment, but then asked a lot of questions.\par \par \uc2 CALLIE HEIM (VICTIM OF JOB APPLICATION SCAM)\par \par \uc2 I gave them my bank account information, so my routing number, my account number, my checking account, like I checked off, (inaudible) checking and I gave them the front and back of my driver's license.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For Callie, her boyfriend raised concerns and then she hit the pause button.\par \par \uc2 CALLIE HEIM (VICTIM OF JOB APPLICATION SCAM)\par \par \uc2 I didn't lose any money, but it doesn't make it any less awful.\par \par \uc2 CATHERINE FISHER (CAREER EXPERT LINKEDIN)\par \par \uc2 If a company is asking you to pay for something during the interview process, that is a huge red flag.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But for Miranda Owens of Kansas City...\par \par \uc2 MIRANDA OWENS (VICTIM OF JOB APPLICATION SCAM)\par \par \uc2 I felt like my trust had been completely shattered, my trust in all of these online platforms.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The person that offered her a job sent her a check, then saying they made a mistake and she needed to return the money. The original check bounced and Miranda was out nearly $5,000.\par \par \uc2 MIRANDA OWENS (VICTIM OF JOB APPLICATION SCAM)\par \par \uc2 I just started bawling.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE RED FLAGS TO WATCH OUT FOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOB SCAM WARNING SIGNS\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, let's hit all the red flags you need to watch out for. If the person is asking you for personal information, beyond what you've provided in previous application and if they want financial information, those are a no go. If you're asked to spend money during the interview process, or if they only text with you. And this is the big one, for any scam regardless of job or anything, if they, someone sends you money and then they ask you to reimburse them, that is a hug red flag. Guys, it's so hard for these job seekers, but you just have to start with skepticism.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. And, Becky, I found another thing, a friend of mine almost fell for this, but then she went to the actual website of the company and they weren't posting the job. That was something that was a red flag for her.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Due diligence, so smart.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Preying on people being desperate for a job.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Becky, thank you as always.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:13, "PREMIUMIZATION" ON THE RISE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And coming up, Becky is going to be back and we're going to tell you how some companies are trying to upsell you with something called premiumization.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7:42, WEIGHTWATCHERS' BIG MOVE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And next, the big move from WeightWatchers. Could it be a game changer for your health? Stay there to find out.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230331ej3700036\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE FUTURE OF REMOTE JOBS EMPLOYEES BEING CALLED BACK TO THE OFFICE AS MORE SEEK STAY AT HOME WORK\b0\par\par\uc2 735 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 February 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US TRACKING CHINESE SPY BALLOON: EYES ON THE SKIES\par \par \uc2 BLINKEN, TRIP, CHINA, BALLOON, RYDER, GALLAGHER, METZL\par \par \uc2 CHINESE, BALLOON, DECISION, US, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 ARCTIC, RECORD, AMERICANS, DANGEROUS, BREEZY\par \par \uc2 JANUARY, JOBS, UNEMPLOYMENT\par \par \uc2 AID, US, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, WAR, ROCKETS, AMMUNITION\par \par \uc2 MEMPHIS, NICHOLS, OFFICERS, HEMPHILL\par \par \uc2 DALLAS, ZOO, MONKEYS, THEFT, CHARGES, EDELL\par \par \uc2 KELCE, SUPER BOWL, CHIEFS, EAGLES\par \par \uc2 NHL, ALL-STARS, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, FINANCIAL, MURDER, ARGUMENTS, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 VERMONT, MIDDLE SCHOOL, GRANDFATHER, DISABITO\par \par \uc2 DNA, MURDER, COLD CASE, POLICE, VADURRO, GARRETT\par \par \uc2 HOUSING, MARKET, RATES, BUYERS, SELLERS, PENNISI, FRATANTONI\par \par \uc2 BASKETBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ESPIONAGE, CHINA, SPY BALLOON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECRETARY OF STATE BLINKEN POSTPONES CHINA TRIP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLANNED VISIT DELAYED AS SUSPECTED SURVEILLANCE BALLOON MOVES ACROSS U.S.\par \par \uc2 WIND CHILL, HYPOTHERMIA, ACCIDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD SETTING ARCTIC BLAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS OF AMERICANS FACING DANGEROUS WIND CHILLS\par \par \uc2 REMOTE WORK, KIMBROUGH, MCINTYRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE FUTURE OF REMOTE JOBS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EMPLOYEES BEING CALLED BACK TO THE OFFICE AS MORE SEEK STAY AT HOME WORK\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Turning now to the future of remote work as more and more employers mandate workers return to the office. ABC's Alexis Christoforous has that story for us.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) More employers rolling back their pandemic-era work policies, confident they can attract employees without the promise of working from home.\par \par \uc2 KARIN KIMBROUGH (CHIEF ECONOMIST LINKEDIN)\par \par \uc2 We're seeing employers not feel as compelled to have to offer that flexibility. They don't have to compete as hard for talent.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At the start of the pandemic, one in five jobs were remote. Now, more companies are calling workers back to the office, including \uc2 Google\uc2 , \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 , TikTok and ABC's parent company, \uc2 Disney\uc2 . In December, remote jobs made up a little over 13% of all postings advertised on the professional social networking platform \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2 , down from nearly 21% in March. Still, demand for remote work is high, attracting more than half of all job applications on the site. Lauren McIntyre is one of those applicants. She has been looking for remote work as a personal assistant since late last year.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MCINTYRE (REMOTE WORK CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 It definitely is a bit more scarce right now looking for remote work. I would say that a lot of the options are at best hybrid.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She says working from home allows her to care for her 15-month-old daughter.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN MCINTYRE (REMOTE WORK CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We did the math. And if I were to put my daughter in day care, it would cancel out whatever income I'd be getting for that day.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Remote work all but drying up in industries like education, transportation and leisure and hospitality. Still, experts say remote jobs are here to stay.\par \par \uc2 KARIN KIMBROUGH (CHIEF ECONOMIST LINKEDIN)\par \par \uc2 You can't put the genie back in the bottle. There will always be the option for employers to offer remote for the talent they really want to retain.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And if you're looking for remote work, experts say be sure to let any potential employer know you're a self-starter and good communicator to ease their concerns about you being productive. And be prepared to take a pay cut in exchange for all the cost savings you'll enjoy while working from home. Guys?\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thanks, Alexis.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 3 MINUTES, "YOU PEOPLE" CRITIQUES\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up in our "GMA Morning Menu," the rom-com "You People" is sizzling over on streaming but, this morning, why some critics are taking aim at the movie's portrayal of race and religion.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 6 MINUTES, BLACK HISTORY IN THE MAKING\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Plus, celebrating black history in the making. And a football first, breaking down next Sunday's Super Bowl duel between Patrick Mahomes and Jalen Hurts.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN NEXT HALF HOUR, "THE SMALLEST SPOT OF A DOT"\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And in our next half hour, our friend Linsey Davis. She has a brand-new children's book, and she will be here live to tell us all about it. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230222ej240003e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ROBIN'S EPIC NEW ZEALAND JOURNEY ROBIN'S LEAP OF FAITH IN NEW ZEALAND\b0\par\par\uc2 555 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 February 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CHINA, SPYING, BIDEN, RYDER, BLINKEN, BALLOON\par \par \uc2 WIND CHILLS, WU, MONETTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "ONCE-IN-A-GENERATION" ARCTIC BLAST\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 CRASH, MAMMONE, SMITH, WOODROOF, BICYCLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY ASSAULT ARREST\par \par \uc2 AIR SCARE, \uc2 UNITED AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNITED JETS CLIP WINGS\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, EMPLOYMENT, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 517,000 NEW JOBS ADDED\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, TRIAL, GREER, GRIFFIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MURDAUGH DOUBLE MURDER TRIAL\par \par \uc2 NICHOLS, HEMPHILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEMPHIS OFFICER HEMPHILL FIRED\par \par \uc2 DALLAS ZOO, CENTRAL PARK ZOO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 NEW ZEALAND, FEAR, BUNGEE JUMP\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We saw Robin Roberts taking those deep breaths, and then her leap of faith in New Zealand, where they say live more, fear less.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) To live more and fear less.\par \par \uc2 TOURIST (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Yes. Ah. That was amazing.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That's the motto for brave souls from around the world who visit the home of bungee.\par \par \uc2 TOURIST (MALE)\par \par \uc2 That was incredible. Just goes to show that fear is just in your mind, you can overcome anything.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Invented in 1988 here in New Zealand.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Have you done anything like this before?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I have not.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, when in the birthplace of bungee, you've got to take a leap. For me, that's the Sky Jump in Auckland, at the tallest building in the Southern Hemisphere.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Are you ready?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) I'm ready.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 You're excited.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm ready to live more, and fear less.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 You're excited. I love to hear it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) My heart beat heavy as we head up the lift.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 How are you with heights?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm good with heights, not at jumping off of heights, but I'm good with heights.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Venturing 53 stories up.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm going to be at the bottom to catch you.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The safety briefing.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm going to check your shoes now. Lift them up for me please. Looking good. I'm going to double check your harness now.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Then it's go-time.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, this is real. Oh, my gosh. Oh, my gosh. This is happening.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Robin, I'm going do a countdown very shortly, okay?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Let go with both hands and big jump forward.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Get ready now. Here she comes in three, two, one, go.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Conquering this incredible leap of faith at 52 miles per hour.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, my god. Oh, my God. I'm doing it. It's happening.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Mind blown and elated with my feet firmly planted back on the ground. Oh, my gosh.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 High five, Robin Roberts.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, my gosh. Oh, my gosh. That was living more and fearing less.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Safe flight home, Robin, on a plane.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230206ej230000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NURSES STRIKE OVER TENTATIVE DEAL TO END WALKOUT WITH TWO NYC HOSPITALS\b0\par\par\uc2 392 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 January 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 FAA\uc2 , TRAVEL, DELAYS, CANCELLATION, MONGELLO, BUTTIGIEG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMAND FOR ANSWERS AFTER AIR TRAVEL MELTDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FAA\uc2  SAYS MAINTENANCE MISTAKE LED TO SYSTEM FAILURE & FLIGHT CHAOS\par \par \uc2 FLOODING, STORM, RECOVERY\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STORM ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEST COAST BRACING FOR ANOTHER ROUND OF RAIN & SNOW\par \par \uc2 KOHBERGER, TRIAL, INVESTIGATION, MURDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO MURDERS SUSPECT DUE IN COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH WARRANT SEALED AS PROSECUTORS RELEASE COULD JEOPARDIZE INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, RUSSIA, UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW REPORT EXPECTED TO SHOW MORE RELIEF FROM RISING PRICES\par \par \uc2 NURSES, STRIKE, HOCHUL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NURSES STRIKE OVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENTATIVE DEAL TO END WALKOUT WITH TWO NYC HOSPITALS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to go to the nurses strike at two major hospitals here in New York ending overnight. A tentative deal has been reached. And our Whit Johnson is at Montefiore Hospital in the Bronx with more. Good morning, Whit.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Michael, good morning to you. Just moments ago, New York's Governor \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  calling this a sigh of relief.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) About 7,000 nurses back on the job this morning after three days on the picket lines. Those tentative agreements reached overnight effectively ending the strike at two major hospitals.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENTATIVE AGREEMENT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One of those hospitals, Montefiore, announcing the deal includes 19% pay raises, benefits that match or exceed peer institutions and an increase of 170 nursing positions. \uc2 Mount Sinai\uc2  says their package is similar to agreements reached at other hospitals across the city and went on to thank staffers for their unwavering dedication to world-class patient care. Now, one of the key sticking points until the end was the nurse-to-patient ratio and the union says that they want a historic victory, concrete enforceable safe staffing in both deals with specific language and even financial penalties if the hospitals don't comply.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This comes at a critical time as well with winter settling in and the number of COVID patients again on the rise. Also, other respiratory viruses have had a big impact on hospital staffing. Robin?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thankfully, it has been resolved. Whit, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230201ej1c00031\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NURSES STRIKE ENTERS THIRD DAY HOSPITALS DIVERTING AMBULANCES AND POSTPONING ELECTIVE SURGERIES\b0\par\par\uc2 858 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 January 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROUNDED?\par \par \uc2 FAA\uc2 , OUTAGE, COMPUTER, FLIGHTS, GROUNDED, DELAYED\par \par \uc2 STORMS, DELUGE, RAIN, FLOODING, SNOW, NEWSOM\par \par \uc2 STORMS, CYCLONES, RAIN, WIND, SNOW\par \par \uc2 PARIS, STABBING, TRAIN, POLICE, SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DOCUMENTS, NATIONAL ARCHIVES, DOJ\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, ATTACKS, GAINS, UKRAINE, TROOPS, TRAINING\par \par \uc2 WALSHE, MISSING, ARREST, EVIDENCE, FLEURY, RIVLIN\par \par \uc2 NURSES, STRIKE, SURGERIES, STAFFING\par \par \uc2 AMTRAK, TRAPPED, PASSENGERS, DETOURED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORM ALERTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM GOLDEN GLOBES AWARDS\par \par \uc2 MURDERS, MOGEN, KOHBERGER, DNA, AFFIDAVIT, GONCALVES\par \par \uc2 GOLDEN GLOBES, RETURN, CONTROVERSY, WINNERS\par \par \uc2 DOGS, BUS, MO MOUNTAIN MUTTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ICE COVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS: GROUNDED?\par \par \uc2 FAA\uc2 , COMPUTER, SYSTEM, OUTAGE, FAILURE, GROUND STOP\par \par \uc2 STORM, DELUGE, EVACUATED, CYCLONES, CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 NURSES, STRIKE, HOSPITALS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to more on the nurses strike entering day three, 7,000 walking off the job at hospitals in New York City. Let's go back to Andrew Dymburt at \uc2 Mount Sinai Hospital\uc2  with more and how the medical centers are reacting. Good morning there, Andrew.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. You can hear the demonstrations going on behind me. We are in day three of one of the largest nursing strikes in decades. Thousands of nurses walking off the job and onto the picket line. We're talking about 7,000 nurses from two different hospitals. Mount Sanai Main here in Manhattan and Montefiore in the Bronx. And even though it's just two hospitals, they account for nearly 16 percent of all hospital beds in New York City. Their chief demand, these nurses say, is more staffing. They say they had to strike because of chronic understaffing leaving them caring for too many patients and they want help.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the meantime, hospitals are diverting ambulances and postponing elective surgeries due to this strike. Now, there are other health facilities in New York City that recently accepted a tentative new contract for nurses, which is said to include 19 percent pay raises over three years, but nurses at the two hospitals we mentioned are still holding out over those staffing issues.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Some on the picket line say they've been so overworked and overwhelmed. One telling our local WABC station that he's seeing ten patients at a time, which is double what he normally sees. Another saying that she's been working 14-hour shifts. Now, negotiations have been ongoing between these hospitals and the \uc2 New York State Nurses Association\uc2 . Both sides are said to be closing in on an agreement, but as of this morning still no deal. Guys.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, hoping they'll find a deal soon because nurses, they work so incredibly hard.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They sure do.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:11 GWEN STEFANI UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up here on "Gma" Morning Menu, Gwen Stefani taking some criticism. The Grammy winner facing new accusations of cultural appropriation.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:14 MEAL TIME AND WEIGHT LOSS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also this morning, why the time you eat may be important when it comes to losing weight. Doctor Ashton is here with more.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:16 TRY BEFORE YOU BUY\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And two ABC speedsters. No, not Michael and George. We're talking about Linsey Davis and Will Reeve. They check out running shoes as they try before you buy a new pair. Go, Linsey. Go, Will.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:30 GMA GIVES BACK!\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And it's "Gma" gives back. Ginger gearing up to surprise one deserving man who's inspired by his own experience to support hurricane victims. Ginger, how is it going?\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, we are being very quiet and this crowd is being wonderful with me because right around this corner is a man named Carlos that you are about to meet. Oh, my goodness, he needs to be celebrated, so "Gma" is about to give back big. He thinks he's about to do an interview with (inaudible) New York, but uh-uh, we brought "Gma" to him. Stick around because you're going to see the big reveal.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "Gma." And welcome back to Lara. And, Lara, I see you're making a little bit of a fashion statement this morning.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I sure am. This is not the pair of boots I was looking for for Christmas, however, it's what I got.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 How are you feeling?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I feel great. I'm so happy to be back. It was surgery that I knew was coming and all is well, so.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Don't mind the singular shoe look.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And you're going to see it for a while.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes, you will see it for a long while.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230201ej1b0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ON STRIKE OVER 7,000 NYC NURSES WALK OFF JOB OVER WAGES & UNDERSTAFFING\b0\par\par\uc2 1,926 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 January 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 NURSES, STRIKE, HAGANS, MCGOWAN, COLLINS, BURGER\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks for joining us. Tonight, thousands of nurses still refusing to be on the job in New York, striking, they say, over staff shortages that have sent many to the breaking point. Nurses now, like so many others in the workforce, demanding change. Some warning that the ripple effect could impact patient safety across the country.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 To the country, what do we say?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 This is a health care emergency.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Nurses, united, we'll never be defeated.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Braving the cold to demand increased staffing and better wages at two major New York City hospitals. It's the largest nursing strike here in decades.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 This was really the last resort. We tried, since September, to reach an agreement, and, unfortunately, we're here.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 In general, striking is scary. We lose our benefits. We lose our pay for however long this lasts, not just these three days. It can go on for weeks.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) These nurses taking to the picket line after last-minute negotiations collapsed between their hospitals and the \uc2 New York State Nurses Association\uc2 , or \uc2 NYSNA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NANCY HAGANS (PRESIDENT \uc2 NEW YORK STATE NURSES ASSOCIATION\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Nurses are walking away from the bed because of the abuse, mentally and physically. We can't take it anymore. We can't take it anymore.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 We can't take it anymore.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) More than 7,000 nurses still reeling from the pandemic and burdened by burnout finally at their breaking point. Carol McGowan is one of them. She's a neurosurgical ICU nurse who's worked at \uc2 Mount Sinai Hospital\uc2  in Manhattan for 30 years.\par \par \uc2 CAROL MCGOWAN (NEUROSURGICAL ICU NURSE)\par \par \uc2 I've done nothing else for the rest of my life. This is my passion. This is what I love doing.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Like most mornings, she's headed to Mount Sinai. But today, instead of going inside the hospital, she'll be standing outside, along with most of her fellow nurses, calling for change for the third straight day.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 You have to sign in.\par \par \uc2 CAROL MCGOWAN (NEUROSURGICAL ICU NURSE)\par \par \uc2 It's exhilarating being out on Madison Avenue with all your colleagues dressed in red. But it's also very, very sad, because we shouldn't be on Madison Avenue. We should be in the building, doing the job that we were trained to do, that we love to do.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Carol is a 45-year veteran nurse who came to New York from Scotland three decades ago.\par \par \uc2 CAROL MCGOWAN (NEUROSURGICAL ICU NURSE)\par \par \uc2 They had a short of nurses in New York City, so recruits came out all across the world to recruit nurses to come to hospitals. Go full-circle to 2023, and we're now at an even bigger staff shortage crisis than we were then.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 We're nurses, united. We'll never be defeated.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The irony isn't lost on her that she's the one demanding hospitals fill that staffing gap amid a surge in demand for health care.\par \par \uc2 CAROL MCGOWAN (NEUROSURGICAL ICU NURSE)\par \par \uc2 We have had enough of telling management time and time again that this is unsafe. When you're 500 nurses short in an institution, those 500 places that are not filled, somebody's suffering from that. And it's the nurses, it's the patients, it's the community that we serve.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A recent New York state analysis predicted that a better nurse-to-patient ratio would result in shorter hospital stays and fewer readmissions. Over two years, it would save an estimated 4,300 lives and $720 million. These strikes are the latest example of the tension that exists between hospitals and their medical staff, not just in New York, but across the country.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you think there will be a ripple effect across the country?\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE COLLINS PHD (DEAN COLLEGE OF NURSING AND HEALTH LOYOLA UNIV)\par \par \uc2 There are some nurses who feel very strongly about unionization and the need that, if you nee to, to strike. And there are other nurses who feel that they could never do that. I think it will have ripple effect. We'll have to see how it plays out.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH BURGER (PRESIDENT NATIONAL NURSES UNITED)\par \par \uc2 I don't have a crystal ball, but until this staffing crisis is solved, we're going to see more strikes, larger strikes, because it seems that that is the only way that we've been able to deal with this issue.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) These nurse strikes have also become a global movement, similar demonstrations popping up in countries like Turkey and Lebanon. And in Great Britain, nurses and ambulance workers went on strike for the first time in UK history.\par \par \uc2 NURSE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I just feel it's something that we have to do, because we have to have a voice. But nobody's listening to us.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In New York, \uc2 Mount Sinai Hospital\uc2  responding to this week's strikes.\par \par \uc2 FRANCES CARTWRIGHT PHD (CHIEF NURSING OFFICER & SR VP MOUNT SINAI HOSP)\par \par \uc2 It has not been a very fair thing that our \uc2 NYSNA\uc2  executive team have asked our nurses to make this decision, whether to come to work or to be outside, striking.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a statement, Mount Sinai called the strike reckless and said the nurses' union refuses to accept the exact same 19.1% increased wage offer agreed to by eight other hospitals.\par \par \uc2 FRANCES CARTWRIGHT PHD (CHIEF NURSING OFFICER & SR VP MOUNT SINAI HOSP)\par \par \uc2 We had submitted to them a very robust staffing enforcement proposal, and we were waiting to get a counter on that. And we did not receive it at the time that they left negotiations.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Mount Sinai\uc2  has also blamed their vacancies on the national workforce shortage and said that they've hired 4,000 new nurses over the last three years. Just a few miles north of Mount Sinai, hundreds of nurses at \uc2 Montefiore Medical Center\uc2  also advocating for what they call safe staffing.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It's not fair to the patients, because we cannot take care of them how we want to take care of them. This is not what we went to nursing school for.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 They promise, oh, yeah, we're going to have staffing for you. We're going to have the ratios for you. And you know what? They don't.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Montefiore said today that it's offered proposals to address staffing concerns, including expanding the number of registered nurses on staff, establishing average nurse-to-patient ratios, and introducing new ways to increase recruitment and retention.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 What do we want?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Safe staffing.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 When do we want it?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Now.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But they say union leadership still hasn't agreed to the concessions. In the interim, both Montefiore and Mount Sinai have relied on physicians, residents, and non-striking nurses to help take care of patients. These protests come as the profession faces national nurse shortages, according to the \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What do you think is causing it?\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE COLLINS PHD (DEAN COLLEGE OF NURSING AND HEALTH LOYOLA UNIV)\par \par \uc2 One is that the average age of the practicing RN is in the early 50s. We knew this before the pandemic, that the next 10 years, a significant number of registered nurses are going to retire, and then we don't have enough nursing faculty. There are significant numbers of students who are qualified turned away from nursing programs every year because we don't have the faculty to teach them.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The crisis exacerbated by nurses who want to leave the profession. A survey done last year by the \uc2 American Association of Critical Care Nurses\uc2  found that around 67% of nurses plan to leave their job in the next three years. But union leaders say no such shortage exists.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH BURGER (PRESIDENT NATIONAL NURSES UNITED)\par \par \uc2 The industry wants to say that there are not enough trained nurses, that they can't get those nurses. There are plenty of nurses to go around. What there is a shortage of is nurses that are willing to put themselves and their patients and their license on the line to help the hospital industry continue this staffing crisis.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE COLLINS PHD (DEAN COLLEGE OF NURSING AND HEALTH LOYOLA UNIV)\par \par \uc2 According to all the national data that we have from national nursing agencies and workforce experts, there is a shortage, and it's only projected to get worse before 2030, especially in the South and the West.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nurses on the picket lines in New York...\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Shut it down.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...following the lead of their fellow health care workers in Minnesota. This past September, nearly 15,000 nurses at more than a dozen different hospitals went on strike, the largest ever among private sector nurses.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUBESCH (VICE PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOCIATION)\par \par \uc2 All right. We've been standing strong.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUBESCH (VICE PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOCIATION)\par \par \uc2 It's nurses who are continually striving to give the absolute best, world-class care they can to their patients. So, we care deeply about the care we give, but it's incredibly distressing to not be able to meet the standards that we hold for ourselves.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nurses there were set to strike again in December, but came to a deal that included historic pay increases and a say in staffing.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUBESCH (VICE PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOCIATION)\par \par \uc2 People are feeling hurt and people are feeling like this was a good deal. I would just point out that the feeling amongst our nurses here in Minnesota is that this isn't the endpoint. This is just the end of the first phase.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In New York, 65-year-old Carol, who plans to retire later this year, considers this strike her last stand.\par \par \uc2 CAROL MCGOWAN (NEUROSURGICAL ICU NURSE)\par \par \uc2 I want this profession to be safer for the new nurses coming up, for the next generation of nurses.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nurses like Allie Seznick (PH).\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Being able to stand out here in solidarity with them is what the union's about. You know, it's unity. It's coming out in strong numbers to support each other and make a difference.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The nurses out here say they're eager and ready to get back to their patients, hoping to come to an agreement with the hospitals soon.\par \par \uc2 CAROL MCGOWAN (NEUROSURGICAL ICU NURSE)\par \par \uc2 I would love to get back to work today, but it looks like tomorrow, yeah. Take care of your nurses, because we take care of you when you're sick. Let's get back to work.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT ON NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "PROPERTY BROTHERS"\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And when we come back, you know them from the popular show. What the Property Brothers have to say about the housing market and their legendary sibling rivalry.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020230113ej1b00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NURSES STRIKE ENTERS SECOND DAY OVER 7,000 NYC NURSES WALK OFF JOB OVER WAGES & UNDERSTAFFING\b0\par\par\uc2 576 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 January 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, FLOODING, EVACUATION, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN FACING QUESTIONS OVER CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPT LAUNCHES REVIEW AFTER MATERIAL FOUND AT FORMER OFFICE\par \par \uc2 SANTOS, MCCARTHY, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL, PROTESTS, ELECTION, BOLSONARO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHAOS IN BRAZIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 1,500 RIOTERS DETAINED AFTER STORMING GOVERNMENT BUILDINGS\par \par \uc2 NURSING PROTESTS, RUSSO, HAGANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NURSES STRIKE ENTERS SECOND DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OVER 7,000 NYC NURSES WALK OFF JOB OVER WAGES & UNDERSTAFFING\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to day two of the hospital strike that sent over 7,000 nurses to picket lines. They're demanding better staffing that they say will improve patient safety. Eva Pilgrim is at \uc2 Mount Sinai Hospital\uc2  with more. Good morning, Eva.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. The nurses back out here on the picket line. One of the hospitals has come to the bargaining table with the nurses. But here, there have been no talks for the last 24 hours. The nurses say they're prepared to fight.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 And to our patients, we say...\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 This is a health care emergency.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, 7,000 nurses at two New York City hospitals walking off the job for a second day over wages, working conditions and what they call a crisis of understaffing.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What's the sticking point?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The sticking point is staffing. It's really hurtful for us to see what's happening to the patients.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Nurses united, we'll never be defeated.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The two major hospitals now moving vulnerable patients like NICU babies and bringing in travel nurses. COVID has made previous nursing shortages even worse. The union wants improved staffing standards with more nurses hired and fewer patients assigned per nurse. Bianca Russo says her neonatal ICU is overextended.\par \par \uc2 BIANCA RUSSO (NURSE NEONATAL INTENSIVE CARE UNIT MOUNT SINAI HOSPITAL)\par \par \uc2 Sometimes we get up to three, four babies for one nurse. And they're not well babies, they're sick babies. And having one nurse to four babies is absolutely unacceptable, and we cannot do it anymore.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The union chief says nursing in the city can be bleak.\par \par \uc2 NANCY HAGANS (PRESIDENT \uc2 NEW YORK STATE NURSES ASSOCIATION\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 The nurse is not able to take a break. The nurse is not able to finish her task. And the nurse is not able to deliver the proper care that that nurse needs to deliver to their patient. You could, there could be delay in medication, there could be delay in vital signs. It's really not safe for the patients.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hospital officials say the union refused to more than 19% compounded wage increase and warned the strike will spark fear and uncertainty across our community. Another hospital calls the union reckless and claims the move sadly is forcing nurses to leave their patients' bedsides.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, if patient ratio is being the sticking point, it raises the question, what are safe nurse to patient numbers? For the most part, that's determined by the hospitals. Only one state, California, legally defines it. And those numbers vary by ICUs and NICUs, having lower ratios to general care unit, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Eva Pilgrim, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230131ej1a00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NURSES STRIKE ENTERS SECOND DAY OVER 7,000 NURSES WALK OFF JOB OVER WAGES\b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 January 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, FLOODING, EVACUATION, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN FACING QUESTIONS OVER CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPT LAUNCHES REVIEW AFTER MATERIAL FOUND AT FORMER OFFICE\par \par \uc2 SANTOS, MCCARTHY, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL, PROTESTS, ELECTION, BOLSONARO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHAOS IN BRAZIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 1,500 RIOTERS DETAINED AFTER STORMING GOVERNMENT BUILDINGS\par \par \uc2 NURSING PROTESTS, RUSSO, HAGANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NURSES STRIKE ENTERS SECOND DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OVER 7,000 NYC NURSES WALK OFF JOB OVER WAGES & UNDERSTAFFING\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, ZWERNER, PROBE, DREW, SAMPLE-RUSK, GARCIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOT VIRGINIA TEACHER HAILED AS HERO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE SAY SHE "SAVED LIVES" AFTER 6-YEAR-OLD OPENED FIRE IN CLASSROOM\par \par \uc2 HAMLIN, RECOVERY, KNIGHT, PRITTS, MCDERMOTT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "ANT-MAN AND THE WASP: QUANTUMANIA"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, SEARCH, WALSHE, MINER, BELAND\par \par \uc2 PRINCE HARRY, "SPARE", KYRIACOU, ADEBAYO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROYAL FAMILY FALLOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW REACTION TO PRINCE HARRY'S HEADLINE-MAKING INTERVIEW & MEMOIR\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE FOOTBALL, BOWERS, BENSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BULLDOGS GO BACK-TO-BACK!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGIA PUMMELS TCU TO REPEAT AS NATIONAL CHAMPIONS\par \par \uc2 CYCLONES, WEATHER, CALIFORNIA, STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVACUATIONS & RESCUES AS CYCLONES SLAM WEST\par \par \uc2 NURSES, STRIKE, NEW YORK CITY, STAFFING, WAGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NURSES STRIKE ENTERS SECOND DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OVER 7,000 NURSES WALK OFF JOB OVER WAGES\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to the 7,000 nurses on strike for a second day. We're going to go back to Eva Pilgrim at \uc2 Mount Sinai Hospital\uc2  with their demands, including better staffing that they say will improve patient safety. Good morning, Eva.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. Those 7,000 nurses at two New York City hospitals walking off the job for a second day over wages, working conditions and what they call a crisis of understaffing. Now, those two major hospitals now moving vulnerable patients like NICU babies, and they're bringing in travel nurses. The sticking point in this negotiation is staffing. COVID has made previous nursing shortages even worse. The union wants improved staffing standards with more nurses hired and fewer patients assigned per nurse. The hospital officials say the union refused a 19.1 percent compounded wage increase and warn the strike will spark fear and uncertainty across our community. Now, one of the hospitals has been back at the bargaining table with the nurses. Here, there have been no talks in the last 24 hours. The nurses tell us they're prepared to fight. Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, they are, and hopefully they'll come to some sort of resolution soon. Cecilia.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230131ej1a0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW YORK CITY NURSES GO ON STRIKE 7,000+ NURSES AT TWO HOSPITALS WALK OFF THE JOB\b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 January 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETAKING CONTROL\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL, ELECTION, BOLSONARO, DA SILVA, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 CA, RAIN, STORMS, WINDS, FLOODS, EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RELENTLESS RAIN BATTERING CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EVACUATIONS ORDERED AS NEW ROUND OF STORMS TAKE AIM\par \par \uc2 CA, FLOODING, RAIN, SNOW, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, SPEAKER, BALLOTS, GAETZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE GETS TO WORK AFTER SPEAKER FIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEVIN MCCARTHY ELECTED ON 15TH VOTE FOLLOWING WEEK OF DRAMA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, MEXICO, SUMMIT, IMMIGRATION, BORDER, ABBOTT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN ON THE BORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAKES FIRST VISIT TO U.S. MEXICO BORDER SINCE TAKING OFFICE\par \par \uc2 TX, RESTAURANT, ROBBER, PATRON, WILLKENS, SHOOKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS RESTAURANT SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE SEARCH FOR CUSTOMER ACCUSED OF KILLING ARMED ROBBERY SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 NURSES, STRIKE, HOSPITALS, UNION, PATIENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW YORK CITY NURSES GO ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 7,000 NURSES AT TWO HOSPITALS WALK OFF THE JOB\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What a scene. Okay, John, thanks very much. Here in New York, thousands of nurses are on strike this morning after negotiations fell through last night. Eva Pilgrim is at \uc2 Mount Sinai Hospital\uc2  with the latest. Good morning, Eva.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW YORK CITY NURSE STRIKE\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) (Inaudible) that we are seeing across the country. About 7,000 nurses at four locations in New York City going on strike as of 6:00 this morning. The nurses union and hospitals negotiated through the weekend and all through the night. But we are told it fell apart about 1:00 am. The sticking point in these negotiations, staffing shortages, nurse-to-patient ratios that started back in COVID and have continued to now.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And this isn't just a problem here. We are seeing nursing shortages at hospitals from coast to coast. In Minnesota, some 15,000 nurses went on strike for three days back in September. They avoided a second strike in December. Here in New York, hospitals affected already making moves to care for patients moved the most vulnerable, like NICU babies, to other hospitals and even postponing some surgeries.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the nursing union making a point this morning in a tweet to say that if you need to have care, to still go get it, and even inviting people to join them on the picket line after. Guys?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Eva, thank you. Hopefully a resolution can be reached soon.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230130ej1900030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POSSIBLE NURSES' STRIKE IN NEW YORK CITY 10,000 COULD HIT PICKET LINES OVER WORKING CONDITIONS & PAY\b0\par\par\uc2 656 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 January 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 STORMS, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEVASTATING FLOODING IN CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ATMOSPHERIC RIVER SLAMMING STATE, MORE THAN 500,000 WITHOUT POWER\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, BIDEN, ABBOTT, GARCIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRISIS ON THE BORDER AS MIGRANT SURGE CONTINUES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN VISITING EL PASO TODAY BEFORE MEXICO SUMMIT\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, IMMIGRATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN VISITING U.S.-MEXICO BORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EL PASO VISIT FOLLOWS ANNOUNCEMENT OF NEW MIGRANT POLICY\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, GLOVER, DREW, GLASS, TEACHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIRGINIA CLASSROOM SHOOTING INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS: TEACHER SHOT BY 6-YEAR-OLD IN STABLE CONDITION\par \par \uc2 IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OUTRAGE FOLLOWING IRAN EXECUTIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEHRAN REGIME FACES BACKLASH OVER ANTI-GOVERNMENT KILLINGS\par \par \uc2 NURSES, PROTESTS, WEISS, KOSHY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE NURSES' STRIKE IN NEW YORK CITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 10,000 COULD HIT PICKET LINES OVER WORKING CONDITIONS & PAY\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Turning back here to home now, and a potential nurses' strike that could hit the nation's biggest city. Tomorrow, upwards of 10,000 nurses may walk out over working conditions and pay conditions here in New York City. ABC's Phil Lipof joins us live. And, Phil, this comes as COVID hospitalizations climb in some parts of the country.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Janai. Nurses at five New York City hospitals have ratified contracts avoiding a strike. But not every hospitals here is at that point just yet. In fact, negotiates went past midnight and under 24 hours from the strike deadline.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, a potential nursing strike looming in the nation's largest city. Nearly 10,000 New York City nurses set to walk off the job Monday at 6:00 AM if no deal is reached.\par \par \uc2 ALLISON WEISS (NURSE)\par \par \uc2 I just hope that by Monday morning we can come to an agreement to have safe care for all of their patients, their families and the nursing community.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The strike would affect several hospitals. The main sticking point, staffing shortages through COVID and now.\par \par \uc2 ALLISON WEISS (NURSE)\par \par \uc2 I need to stick by my co-workers who have been here in the last three-plus years who, where it has been a nightmare for them to care for their patients.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How does it make your job more difficult when you're understaffed?\par \par \uc2 SHOBA KOSHY (NURSE)\par \par \uc2 The staffing ratios are just insane. The issue is that we don't have enough nurses. We would obviously like to be staffed the way we need to, so we can properly care for our patients.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is not just a New York City problem. Across the country, there is a shortage of nurses. In Minnesota, 15,000 nurses went on strike for three days in September, then averted another strike in December. Here in New York City, Mount Sinai, which operates three of the four hospitals facing possible strikes, already moving some of their most vulnerable patients, including babies from the NICU, to other hospitals. In a statement, Mount Sinai blames the nursing union, saying in part, "The union is jeopardizing patients' care and it's forcing valuable Mount Sinai nurses to sacrifice their dedication to patient care." All of this as hospitalizations in the northeast are rising, especially among the elderly as doctors and nurses battle the flu, respiratory illnesses, and now a new subvariant of Omicron.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Office of Emergency Management tells us they are setting up a command center just in case there is a strike. Negotiations went past midnight last night, both sides. Neither side wants a strike to happen. We're told negotiations will start again today at noon and could go past midnight if they're making progress. Eva?\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's hope they can work a deal. Thanks, Phil.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230126ej1800030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NURSES THREATEN TO STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 164 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 January 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS, BOLSONARO, DA SILVA, OVERTHROW, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTORS STORM BRAZILIAN CAPITAL\par \par \uc2 HAMLIN, BILLS, ALLEN, TRIBUTES, HOSPITAL, FANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HAMLIN CHEERS ON TEAMMATES\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAINFALL, SNOW, FLOODING, POWER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMS FORCE EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, BORDER, MIGRANTS, SURGE, ABBOT, MAYORKAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN'S FIRST BORDER VISIT\par \par \uc2 HOUSE, MCCARTHY, TENUOUS, INVESTIGATIONS, DEMOCRATS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MCCARTHY'S TENUOUS TENURE\par \par \uc2 ROBBERY, DINER, SUSPECT, KILLED, PATRON, LOPEZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CUSTOMER KILLS ROBBERY SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 NURSES, STRIKE, PRIVATE, PAY, STAFFING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NURSES THREATEN TO STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Faith, thank you. Tonight, it's down to the wire in talks to head off a strike by about 7,000 nurses here in New York City.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The nurses at two private hospitals are threatening to walk off the job, tomorrow morning. They are seeking higher pay and staffing increases. One of the hospitals has moved infants out of intensive care units to other facilities and is postponing elective surgeries ahead of the possible strike.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020230110ej1800008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STARBUCKS BARISTA STRIKE WORKERS WANT MORE STORES TO JOIN UNION\b0\par\par\uc2 146 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 December 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FEDERAL APPEALS COURT DECISION ON TITLE 42: BORDER BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUDDENLY SUSPENDED\par \par \uc2 TITLE 42, BORDER, ABBOTT, GELERNT, SALCIDO, RIVERS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, TITLE 42, EXPIRATION, MIGRANTS, ASYLUM\par \par \uc2 JAN 6TH COMMITTEE, TRUMP, CHARGES, THOMPSON\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, MISSILES, ENERGY, HRYHORIEVA\par \par \uc2 US, PERU, TOURISTS, VEGA, MUNOZ\par \par \uc2 GRINER, WIFE, ARIZONA, EMOTIONAL, REUNION, WNBA\par \par \uc2 WALL STREET, STOCKS, LOSS, INVESTOR\par \par \uc2 STARBUCKS\uc2 , STRIKE, BARISTAS, UNION\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, it may be a little harder for you to get your \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  fix today. More than 1,000 workers at 100 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores across the country are on strike. The three-day strike, which began yesterday, is part of an effort to get more \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores to unionize. The union expects some stores to close entirely while others may keep running with management stepping in behind the counters.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230112eich00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MADE IN AMERICA CHRISTMAS EDITION\b0\par\par\uc2 747 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 December 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CAPITOL, RIOT, TRUMP, CHENEY\par \par \uc2 SNOW, STORM, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NOR'EASTER SLAMS MILLIONS\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, SNOW\par \par \uc2 CRIMO, SHOOTING, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FATHER OF SHOOTING SUSPECT CHARGED\par \par \uc2 MEDICINE SHORTAGE, HOSPITALIZATIONS, FLU, RSV, COVID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOSPITALS PUSHING LIMITS\par \par \uc2 IMMIGRATION, ABBOTT, TITLE 42\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRACING FOR NEW BORDER SURGE\par \par \uc2 TWITTER, SUSPENSIONS, MUSK, O'SULLIVAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MUSK UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 SEARCH, PLANE, CRASH, MAUI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH AFTER PLANE CRASH\par \par \uc2 GAS, PRICES, HOLIDAY, SHIPPING, DEADLINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 BEAUDOIN, THOMPSON, WASHINGTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MADE IN AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, tonight, here, our great "Made in America Christmas," your ideas pouring in. One spicy idea, it turns out, was planted some time ago.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, our great "Made in America Christmas" just nine days away, now. In Mystic, Connecticut, the company Mystic Knotwork, handmade wreaths, ornaments made of rope.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hi, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Bailey McGowan (PH) making their signature anchor bracelets.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It goes right to this loop, just like so.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The anchor holds the bracelet together, 20 workers tying more than 60,000 knots a year. Tonight, making Santas.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Not too short, now.\par \par \uc2 MATT BEAUDOIN (OWNER MYSTIC KNOTWORK)\par \par \uc2 Hi, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Owner Matt Beaudoin, his grandfather Alton starting the business in 1957.\par \par \uc2 MATT BEAUDOIN (OWNER MYSTIC KNOTWORK)\par \par \uc2 The whole town has nautical tradition, so I'm just keeping local tradition alive.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Happy holidays from Mystic Knotwork. Made in America.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Youngstown, Ohio, the company MishMoccs.\par \par \uc2 MICHELIN THOMPSON (OWNER MISHMOCCS)\par \par \uc2 Hi, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Owner Michelin Thompson.\par \par \uc2 MICHELIN THOMPSON (OWNER MISHMOCCS)\par \par \uc2 We manufacture some adorable children moccasins, right here in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 ARMY VETERAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Hi, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Retired Army veteran Michael Bricelin (VO), who served in Vietnam and the Persian Gulf.\par \par \uc2 ARMY VETERAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I do the initial step, cut the leather...\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Starting the shoes.\par \par \uc2 ARMY VETERAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 ...and viola.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The leather from California, New York and Texas.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hey, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Lisa Soriano, (PH) making the bows.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Here they are.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fifteen hundred pairs of shoes a month.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Made in America. Thank you, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And in community gardens across the country, from Oakland to Detroit, Baltimore to the Bronx, they're growing serrano peppers for the nonprofit Small Acts Peppers Hot Sauce. The gardens grow the peppers. Small Acts buys them back for the sauce, and the money goes back to the garden.\par \par \uc2 KAREN WASHINGTON (OWNER GARDEN OF HAPPINESS)\par \par \uc2 Hi, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Karen Washington at the Garden of Happiness in the Bronx.\par \par \uc2 KAREN WASHINGTON (OWNER GARDEN OF HAPPINESS)\par \par \uc2 We grow serrano peppers for the Bronx hot sauce. That money goes back into your community gardens.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The River Run Community Garden in the Bronx, too.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 These peppers are grown with love, made in America.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Thirty-three thousand pounds of peppers, 122 gardens, 42 cities.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Hi, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Farmville Community Garden in Farmville, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Hey, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Rush City Community Garden in Rush City, Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Work hard, we really enjoy it.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hey, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Munsey, Indiana, the afterschool program Motivate our Minds.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We planted the seeds. We had very good luck with the peppers.\par \par \uc2 OWNER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hey, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And just listen to this number from Susan Bowerstead (PH) at the Black Acre Conservancy in Louisville, Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 With our fertile soil and many volunteers, we were able the raise 600 pounds of peppers.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Enough to make 6,000 bottles of hot sauce.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Merry Christmas to all.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Bottling it up, just in time for Christmas, with three words in mind, tonight.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Made in America. Whoo.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Spicing up dinner this Christmas. We love it. Helping so many community gardens across the country. And, by the way, we should mention, Oprah joins us Monday. She wants in with all of you. Her "Favorite Things" meets our "Made in America," Monday night. Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020221220eicg0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CITY COUNCIL SCUFFLE POSTAL WORKER KILLED\b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 December 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST STORMS STRIKE\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, SNOWFALL, WINDS, BLIZZARD, AVALANCHE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST STORMS STRIKE\par \par \uc2 LOCKERBIE, BOMBMAKER, MASUD, DOJ, CUSTODY, BARR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ: LOCKERBIE BOMBMAKER IN CUSTODY\par \par \uc2 KEYSTONE, LEAK, TC ENERGY, GAS PRICES, DOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT MISSION TO FIX KEYSTONE LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRINER, FREED, REUNITED, KIRBY, CARSTENS, WHELAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GRINER IN "GOOD HEALTH"\par \par \uc2 JAN 6TH, CMTE, REFERRALS, SCHIFF, DOJ, CRIMINAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JANUARY 6TH CRIMINAL REFERRALS DECISION\par \par \uc2 WAHL, DEATH, WORLD SCANLAN, CUP, SOCCER, QATAR, TRIBUTES, JAMES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RENOWNED JOURNALIST DIES IN QATAR\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, STRIKES, DRONES, POWER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINE ON THE ATTACK\par \par \uc2 DELAND, MISSING, LAWS, FRANCE, COLLEGE, SURVEILLANCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN STUDENT MISSING IN FRANCE\par \par \uc2 ORION, SPLASHDOWN, MOON, \uc2 NASA\uc2 , GLOVER, HU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ORION SPACECRAFT SPLASHDOWN\par \par \uc2 LOS ANGELES, DELEON, POSTAL CARRIER, KILLED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CITY COUNCIL SCUFFLE\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, what started as a scuffle between a Los Angeles City Council member and protesters escalated into a full-blown fight.\par \par \uc2 ACTIVIST (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Wow, wow, wow.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Activists confronted controversial council member Kevin de Leon during a Christmas tree lighting event Friday night. Deleon has been under fire and called on to resign for not condemning derogatory comments made by former Council President \uc2 Nury Martinez\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The altercation spilled out into the hallway, where Deleon was shoved over a table. None of the protesters were arrested.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSTAL WORKER KILLED\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In Milwaukee, Wisconsin, a \uc2 United States Postal Service\uc2  carrier was shot and killed while on his route, delivering mail.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) His killer still on the loose, tonight. Investigators say surveillance video captured the gunfire, and a possible suspect running to an Audi SUV with tinted windows. Co-workers say he always came to work with a smile on his face.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, with viruses surging nationwide, major cities once again urging people to mask up.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020221212eicb0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ONE-ON-ONE WITH FRENCH PRESIDENT MACRON PARTNERSHIP WITH BIDEN, HELPING UKRAINE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,763 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 December 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RAIL STRIKE, SCHUMER, DURBIN, HAWLEY, KENNEDY, JEFFRIES\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, GAS PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAS PRICES PLUNGING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GASBUDDY: COULD FALL BELOW $3 PER GALLON BY CHRISTMAS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, CHINA, COVID-19, RESTRICTIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTS PREVAILING ACROSS CHINA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOME COVID RULES BEING EASED AS OFFICIALS STRUGGLE TO CRACK DOWN ON UNREST\par \par \uc2 VOLCANO, ERUPTION, MAUNA LOA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW THREAT FROM MASSIVE VOLCANO ERUPTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAVA MOVING TOWARDS KEY HIGHWAY ON HAWAII'S NIG ISLAND\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, MURDER, MOGEN, FRY, COLLEGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLLEGE MURDER MYSTERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE CHIEF SPEAKS OUT AS COMMUNITY GATHERS FOR EMOTIONAL VIGIL\par \par \uc2 STORM, RECOVERY, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 WORLD CUP, PULISIC, QATAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEAM USE GEARS UP FOR KNOCKOUT ROUND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL STAR CHRISTIAN PULISIC BE ABLE TO PLAY AGAINST THE NETHERLANDS?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BANKMAN-FRIED, FTX, FRAUD, CRYPTO-CURRENCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-ON-ONE WITH SAM BANKMAN-FRIED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER FTX CEO ON WHAT WAS BEHIND CRYPTO COMPANY'S STUNNING COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 ROYALS, BOSTON, EARTHSHOT PRIZE, FULANI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL & KATE TAKE BOSTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROYAL PAIR ATTEND CELTICS GAME, SET TO MEET WITH PRESIDENT BIDEN TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 THORSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAIL STRIKE AVERTED? FULL STEAM AHEAD\par \par \uc2 RAIL, STRIKE, SENATE, DEAL, LABOR UNION\par \par \uc2 GAS, CHRISTMAS, PRICES, GASBUDDY\par \par \uc2 WORK WEEK, FOUR DAYS\par \par \uc2 MACRON, BIDEN, UKRAINE, RUSSIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we are back with our "GMA" Cover Story. My interview with French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 . He's here on a State visit, set to meet with President Biden at the White House this morning. And President Macron has been a key partner in Ukraine's fight against Russia. Biden and Macron don't see eye to eye on everything, they have some differences, but they are in league on Ukraine. And Macron, as you'll see, has no problem speaking his mind.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What exactly do you hope to accomplish this week?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 I hope, I would say, to resynchronize in a certain way and build new ambitions for the future.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Have they been out of sync?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 I think so regarding some economic issues. Why? Because I think we're perfectly working closely together when we speak about war, when we speak about Ukraine, when we speak about geopolitics, but when you look at the situation after February this year, gas and energy prices are skyrocketing in Europe because we are buyers (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Americans think they're skyrocketing here too.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 But the situation is very different when you take oil, perhaps, but when I look at the gas prices paid by your companies and the European companies, (inaudible). But on top of that, a series of decisions, I can completely understand and I do share the perspective of the decision, (inaudible), Inflation Reduction Act are perhaps very good for the US economy. But as they were not properly coordinated with the European economies, they create just the absence of a level playing field.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're the first French President ever to have two State visits to the United States. Of course, the first one was under President Trump. He announced two weeks ago that he's going to run for president again. What would it mean for the relationship between the US and France if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  became president again?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 First, I try not to make any type of political fiction, as I am not...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Political fiction.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 I'm not a commentator, I'm a player of this party, and...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But you'll be president if he's reelected president.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 I never speculate about future outcomes of elections in my country, so I will not do so for others. I'm very much engaged and my willingness is for the two years to come to deliver maximum results with President Biden's administration.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's talk about the war in Ukraine. Is Ukraine winning the war right now?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 Ukraine is clearly having very positive counteroffensive. Saying they are winning the war is probably too early.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How about \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 ? You said you expected to speak with him again. Do you know when you're going to speak with him?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 In the coming days. I want to first to have the State visit and have an in-depth discussion with President Biden and our teams together.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you have a vision of what a successful peace looks like?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 A sustainable one.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What does that mean?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 It is two parties to decide and the rest is international community to be here to guarantee and to protect. But what I do believe is, what I do believe in is that it's, a good peace is not a peace which will be imposed for the Ukrainians by others, number one. A good peace is not a peace which will be, which will not be accepted in the (inaudible) long run by one of the two parties.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is a man who's capable of making a decision like that capable of negotiating what you call a good peace?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 This is exactly the question.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know. What's the answer?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 If I had the answer, I would be around the negotiating table with him and would be somebody in charge.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is he still rational is the question?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 I do hope. I do believe in that. My conviction and my pragmatic approach is to say, I have to engage with the existing leaders and the one in charge of the country. Because if we do believe in national sovereignty, we cannot decide to say as a precondition (inaudible) to stop negotiating. I think he made mistakes. Is it impossible to come back to the table and negotiate something? I think it's still possible.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You've talked about a crises of democracies...\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...around the world. What does that mean?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 Look, I think all the western democracies are under very strong pressure. We see the extremes (inaudible). We clearly see in our society a sort of fascination for (inaudible). The big transformation of this past 10 to 15 years, social networks. I can come from my \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account or post on my \uc2 Facebook\uc2  or \uc2 Instagram\uc2  account a very long message, I'm called (inaudible), I don't know what. Nobody knows why but I have a very convincing narrative saying crazy things about a vaccine, a pandemic, the war, and I will bring together some piece of evidence with no link, no verification. It's the beginning of a doubt. Doubt is good, but when it's based on argumentation and we start on the same ground.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right now, we're facing a situation where just in the last couple of days \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has said he's going to relax all the content moderation policies, covid misinformation back on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . He's making it worse, isn't he?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 I think this is a big issue. I think it deserves to be largely engaged. What I push very much for is exactly the opposite, more regulation. And regulation is not...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Can you do that in France on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 We did. And we are implementing it and we did it at the European level. Free speech in democracy is based on respect and public order. We can, you can demonstrate, you can have free speech, you can write what you want, but there is responsibilities and limits. The limit is that you cannot go in the streets and have (inaudible) or antisemitic speech. You cannot put at risk the life of somebody else. Violence is never legitimate in democracy. And this is, for me, what is very important to defend now. In democracy you can change your leaders, you can change the one who will represent you...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible) accept the change.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 ...and vote you, yes. And the point is as long as you have these rules, you are not entitled to be violent. You decide (inaudible). But you do not go to the streets. You can go to the city to protest, to demonstrate for your words, but you have to accept at the point of time the rule of democracy. And when in one of the biggest democracies and the oldest democracies of this world you can have leader and supporters deciding on purpose to refuse the (inaudible) because this is the one they didn't want to see. This is just the beginning of the end of the democracy.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT MACRON (FRANCE)\par \par \uc2 And I think whatever you think, whatever your side could be is just, we have to protect the model where we stand because what is the alternative of this model? Perhaps it's not perfect, I do agree. Perhaps, especially when you wrong to the minority where you lose an election, you are not happy with the outcome, I imagine that a lot of Democrats were not happy in 2016, did they invade Capitol Hill? No. So my strong belief is that we have to stick to the rules because this institution and the democratic framework is much more important than the others.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mmm.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Boy, strong words about January 6th there.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, very much so, and he just really cuts right through it. But he's very confident.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, no question about that. And he's got a big day ahead. He's got the meetings with President Biden today and, of course, the State dinner tonight.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is tonight, that's right. But right now, we are going to, thank you, George. Those were two big interviews you brought to us today. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221229eic10000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW HOPE FOR A FOUR DAY WORK WEEK? SUCCESSFUL RESULTS FROM GLOBAL PILOT PROGRAM\b0\par\par\uc2 551 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 December 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RAIL STRIKE, SCHUMER, DURBIN, HAWLEY, KENNEDY, JEFFRIES\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, GAS PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAS PRICES PLUNGING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GASBUDDY: COULD FALL BELOW $3 PER GALLON BY CHRISTMAS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, CHINA, COVID-19, RESTRICTIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTS PREVAILING ACROSS CHINA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOME COVID RULES BEING EASED AS OFFICIALS STRUGGLE TO CRACK DOWN ON UNREST\par \par \uc2 VOLCANO, ERUPTION, MAUNA LOA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW THREAT FROM MASSIVE VOLCANO ERUPTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAVA MOVING TOWARDS KEY HIGHWAY ON HAWAII'S NIG ISLAND\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, MURDER, MOGEN, FRY, COLLEGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLLEGE MURDER MYSTERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE CHIEF SPEAKS OUT AS COMMUNITY GATHERS FOR EMOTIONAL VIGIL\par \par \uc2 STORM, RECOVERY, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 WORLD CUP, PULISIC, QATAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEAM USE GEARS UP FOR KNOCKOUT ROUND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL STAR CHRISTIAN PULISIC BE ABLE TO PLAY AGAINST THE NETHERLANDS?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BANKMAN-FRIED, FTX, FRAUD, CRYPTO-CURRENCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-ON-ONE WITH SAM BANKMAN-FRIED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER FTX CEO ON WHAT WAS BEHIND CRYPTO COMPANY'S STUNNING COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 ROYALS, BOSTON, EARTHSHOT PRIZE, FULANI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL & KATE TAKE BOSTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROYAL PAIR ATTEND CELTICS GAME, SET TO MEET WITH PRESIDENT BIDEN TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 THORSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAIL STRIKE AVERTED? FULL STEAM AHEAD\par \par \uc2 RAIL, STRIKE, SENATE, DEAL, LABOR UNION\par \par \uc2 GAS, CHRISTMAS, PRICES, GASBUDDY\par \par \uc2 WORK WEEK, FOUR DAYS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, now to new hope for a four-day workweek thanks to an experiment involving 33 companies and nearly a thousand workers in a six month program to reduce the workweek to 32 hours over four days at the same pay. The results, employees and employers are both sold. Workers say they got more done and felt less stressed, and the companies actually averaged a 38 percent increase in revenue. I always love, though, how they ask the employees they survey, as if any of them are going to say, no, no, no, keep it five, add a day. Of course they're on board.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good point there.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's a good point, Whit.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:10 FRENCH PRESIDENT MACRON ONE-ON-ONE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up in our "Gma" Morning Menu, my interview with French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  on his partnership with President Biden and ending the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:18 CELEBRATING CHRISTINE MCVIE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, we celebrate the life and talent of Fleetwood Mac's Christine McVie.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:22 DEALS & STEALS!\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, Tory is back with more "Deals & Steals." Gifts and gadgets starting at just five bucks. And Lara with a very special guest this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:30 MINDY KALING LIVE!\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're right about that, very special. Actress, writer, producer, comedienne, have I forgotten anything? I don't think so. Just all around fabulous woman, Mindy Kaling in the house wearing a fabulous dress. She does so much. She has so much going on. We're going to talk all about it coming up on "Good Morning America."\par \par \uc2 MINDY KALING (MINDY'S BOOK STUDIO)\par \par \uc2 Thank you for that.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Love this woman.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA, THURSDAY, DEC 1\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221229eic10000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PRESIDENT CALLS ON CONGRESS TO AVERT RAIL STRIKE WARNS SHUTDOWN WOULD "DEVASTATE OUR ECONOMY"\b0\par\par\uc2 759 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 November 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, RAILWAY, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT CALLS ON CONGRESS TO AVERT RAIL STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN WARNS RAIL SHUTDOWN WOULD "DEVASTATE OUR ECONOMY"\par \par \uc2 CHINA, PROTESTS, ECONOMY, KIRBY, COVID-19\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING FALLOUT FROM UNPRECEDENTED CHINA UNREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FINANCIAL MARKETS TUMBLE AS COVID PROTESTS SPREAD INTO HONG KONG\par \par \uc2 PLEA, GENDRON, WHITFIELD, FLYNN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUFFALO SUPERMARKET SHOOTER PLEADS GUILTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 10 PEOPLE KILLED IN RACIALLY MOTIVATED ATTACK\par \par \uc2 VOLCANO, ERUPTION, MAUNA LOA, MAGNO, HARA, HON\par \par \uc2 WORLD CUP, ADAMS, BERHALTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WIN OR GO HOME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. TAKES ON IRAN TODAY IN MUST-WIN MATCH\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, CYBER MONDAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CYBER MONDAY SPENDING SPREE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS EXPECTED TO HAVE SET SINGLE-DAY ONLINE SHOPPING RECORD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, GONCALVES, MURDER\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, MURDER, COLLEGE\par \par \uc2 SMITH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL SMITH SPEAKS OUT ABOUT OSCARS SLAP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTOR'S FIRST LATE-NIGHT TV APPEARANCE SINCE HITTING CHRIS ROCK ON STAGE\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, DEALS, BERG, MCDANIELS\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , NEMBHARD, LAKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON ALERT: MAJOR STORM ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 STORM, SOUTH, TORNADO, SNOW\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CONGRESS, STRIKE, RAILROAD, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Robin. We're going to go to the White House now where President Biden is calling on Congress to avert a looming rail strike and impose a settlement that some union members rejected. The President is warning that a national railroad shutdown would devastate the economy. We want to go back to our chief White House correspondent, Cecilia Vega. Good morning, Cecilia.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, good morning, again. The unions and the railroads, they've got until December 9th to come to terms on this, and if they don't reach a deal, the President says this will cripple the economy. And this morning, he is not alone in sounding this dire warning. Hundreds of business groups sent this letter to Congress also urging them to intervene. They say a rail service shutdown for any period of time could cost upwards of $2 billion a day. We are not just talking about passenger travel here. A strike could threaten everything from farming and food to crucial chemicals that are needed for clean drinking water, causing also major supply chain disruptions.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN URGES LAWMAKERS TO IMPOSE SETTLEMENT REJECTED BY UNION MEMBERS\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The sticking point right now for many of these union workers is over paid sick days, but the President's involvement here really calling on Congress to act signals a major shift that could pit him against these union allies. So the big question right now, what is next? Well, Congress could force the two sides to keep talking. They could also impose a deal through legislation, George. Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  says that Congress will intervene, they'll act on this one at some point this week.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Cecilia Vega, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:10 JESSIE JAMES DECKER FIRES BACK\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up here on our "Gma" Morning Menu, Jessie James Decker calling out people commenting on her children's bodies in this picture, some saying she Photoshopped the shot.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:12 SALT AND HEART DISEASE RISK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also this morning, we're breaking down a new study on salt and your heart health. Doctor Ashton is here with what you should know about your food.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:18 "LOVE ACTUALLY" 20 YEARS LATER\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, our first look at Diane Sawyer with the stars of "Love Actually" 20 years later.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:30 GMA GIVES BACK!\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also, you know it's Giving Tuesday. Lara's sorting donations for Toys for Tots as part of the \uc2 Disney\uc2  Ultimate Toy Drive. And you can see she's joined by a very special guest. Lara.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I sure am, Robin. I am here with the one and only Mickey Mouse. He's joining us as we spread a little holiday cheer with the \uc2 Disney\uc2  Ultimate Toy Drive. We're going to tell you all about that and how you too can get involved in this wonderful cause. We're having a great time out here live in Times Square. It's all coming up on "Good Morning America." Should we sort? Let's get these kids their toys.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA, TUESDAY, NOV 29\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221227eibt0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PRESIDENT CALLS ON CONGRESS TO AVERT RAIL STRIKE BIDEN WARNS SHUTDOWN WOULD "DEVASTATE OUR ECONOMY"\b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 November 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, RAILWAY, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT CALLS ON CONGRESS TO AVERT RAIL STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN WARNS RAIL SHUTDOWN WOULD "DEVASTATE OUR ECONOMY"\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to the White House now where President Biden is calling on Congress to alert a looming rail strike and impose a settlement that some union members rejected.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The President is warning that a national rail shutdown would devastate the economy. Chief White House correspondent Cecilia Vega has the details. Good morning, Cecilia.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George, good morning to you. So, the deadline for these unions and these rail workers is now in less than two weeks. And if they don't, President Biden says we're looking at a potentially crippled economy and many industries shutting down. And this morning, he is not alone in this dire warning.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hundreds of business groups have come together to send a letter to Congress, urging them to intervene, also saying a rail service shutdown, listen to this, for any period of time could cost upwards of $2 billion per day. And we are not just talking about passenger travel here. A strike could threaten everything from farming and food to crucial chemicals for clean water, causing major supply chain disruptions.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POTENTIAL RAIL STRIKE\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 But this is not expected, the good news here, to impact holiday gifts. Those were shipped to stores months ago. But the sticking point right now for many of these rail workers is over paid sick days. The President's involvement, this is a big one, calling on Congress to act signals a major shift for him that could potentially pit him against his union allies.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN URGES LAWMAKERS TO IMPOSE SETTLEMENT REJECTED BY UNION MEMBERS\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) You know this, he is a big union backer, a staunch union backer. He's called himself the most pro-union president ever. He has been hesitant to get involved in congressional intervention in union issues in the past.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But right now, George, he says that he was reluctant to get involved in this one, but the potential to cripple, that this could cripple that this could cripple the economy was just too much. He had to get involved here, he says.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What's the outlook in Congress?\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, look, Speaker Pelosi says that Congress lawmakers do plan to intervene this week. This is what they could do. They could push the timeline back to keep these talks going. They could call in an independent arbitrator. And they could also push a deal through legislation. But the big headline here, George, this deadline is on December 9th, so this clock is ticking.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Boy, it sure is. Cecilia Vega, thanks very much. T.J.?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221227eibt00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEWS HEADLINES RAIL STRIKE CONCERNS/HOUSTON'S BOIL WATER WARNING\b0\par\par\uc2 249 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 November 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 VOLCANIC ERUPTION, MAUNA LOA, MAGNO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAUNA LOA ROARS TO LIFE\par \par \uc2 GUILTY PLEA, GENDRON, FLYNN, WHITFIELD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUFFALO GUNMAN PLEADS GUILTY\par \par \uc2 CHINA, PROTESTS, KIRBY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONWIDE CHINA PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, PLANE, CRASH, SMOUSE, GOLDSTEIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRAMATIC PLANE CRASH RESCUE\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, EDWARDS, RAILSBACK, MURDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER TROOPER KILLED IN 'CATFISH' CASE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, WEST, FUENTES, PENCE, BACKLASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP RIPPED FOR DINNER GUESTS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, RAILWAY STRIKE, WATER CRISIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAIL STRIKE CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just a short time ago, President Biden calling on Congress to help avert a potentially crippling rail strike over the holiday season set for Friday, December 9th.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The President asking lawmakers to pass legislation adopting the tentative agreement rail companies and union negotiators reached in September before it was rejected by some union members. President Biden warning, tonight, a strike would devastate the economy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSTON'S BOIL WATER WARNING\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the major water crisis in Houston, more than 2 million people under a boil water alert. And we've learned, tonight, Houston schools will be closed again tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The city's main water treatment plant suffering a temporary power outage yesterday, leaving it unable to safely pump water. Samples now being tested for possible contamination.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, Jay Leno cracking jokes about himself and that fire.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020221129eibs0005t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BLACK FRIDAY PROTESTS AMAZON WORKERS EXPECTED TO STAGE WALKOUTS\b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 November 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMS MOVING ACROSS THE COUNTRY\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TRAVEL, SNOW, RAIN\par \par \uc2 BLACK FRIDAY, SHOPPING, SALES, SURPLUS\par \par \uc2 BLACK FRIDAY, DEALS, GAMING, TVS, TOYS\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, PROTESTS, EMPLOYEES, WALKOUTS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If the sequins and glitter weren't enough, imagine the sand. We do turn now \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers planning protests around the globe on one of the biggest shopping days of the year. Amid the Black Friday frenzy, workers in dozens of countries are taking action and demanding better pay and working conditions from the retailing giant. ABC's Andrew Dymburt joins us now with more. Andrew, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLACK FRIDAY PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON WORKERS EXPECTED TO STAGE WALK OUTS, OTHER ACTION\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Janai. Thousands of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse workers from around the world are set to walk out today. It's part of a multinational protest organizers dub, make \uc2 Amazon\uc2  pay. Workers are demanding higher wages, safer working conditions and the right to join or form unions.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON FACING WORLDWIDE STRIKES AND PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTIONS PLANNED IN THE US AND DOZENS OF COUNTRIES\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Employees from some 40 countries and 18 different warehouses plan to take part in the walkout today on what is one of the busiest shopping days of the year, Black Friday. You can expect to see protests here in the US to India, Japan and France. This is the third year that Make Amazon Pay has organized a global day of action on Black Friday. Just last year workers walked off the job and rallied in the US from coast to coast, even demonstrating outside of \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 ' Manhattan penthouse.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now we reached out to \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , but have not yet heard back. But a company spokesperson tells "Fortune" magazine, it's working to address some of those worker issues. Meanwhile, it's unclear if or how this could affect your holiday orders. Again, Black Friday, big shopping day. Guys.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It certainly is. We'll be watching, Andrew, thank you. Whit.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221221eibp0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BLACK FRIDAY PROTESTS AMAZON WORKERS EXPECTED TO STAGE WALKOUTS\b0\par\par\uc2 677 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 November 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMS MOVING ACROSS THE COUNTRY\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TRAVEL, SNOW, RAIN\par \par \uc2 BLACK FRIDAY, SHOPPING, SALES, SURPLUS\par \par \uc2 BLACK FRIDAY, DEALS, GAMING, TVS, TOYS\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, PROTESTS, EMPLOYEES, WALKOUTS\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, \uc2 WALMART\uc2 , WILCZEWSKI, TYLER, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, SHOOTINGS, GUN CONTROL, RED FLAG, CLUB Q\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, MURDERS, EVIDENCE, MARTIN\par \par \uc2 WORLD CUP, USA, ENGLAND, WEAH, NILAND, FANS\par \par \uc2 THANKSGIVING, TRADITION, TEXTS, HINTON, DENCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "CHRISTMAS VACATION"\par \par \uc2 BARRY, BEST BUY, ELECTRONICS, PRICES, SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 BLOCKBUSTERS, BOX OFFICE, STREAMING, NOVAK, "AVATAR"\par \par \uc2 CHRISTMAS TREES, HARRIS, AHL, GENOVESE, DOMBROWSKI\par \par \uc2 DIGGS, FAN, BILLS, DETROIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEATHER WORRIES: HOLIDAY TRAVEL HEADACHE\par \par \uc2 STORMS, HOLIDAY, TRAVEL, DISRUPTIONS, SEVERE\par \par \uc2 TARGET, SALES, BLOWOUT\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, AMAZON, WALKOUTS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, now to some concerning news for online shoppers, protests planned in dozens of countries against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . Workers taking action to demand better pay and working conditions. Andrew Dymburt is back with more on that story. Andrew, good morning, again, to you.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Janai. Today, thousands of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers are expected to strike on what is arguably the biggest shopping day of the year, Black Friday. It is a global call to action. Part of the Make \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Pay initiative and it involves workers from the US and more than 30 other countries, including Germany, France and even India.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON FACING WORLDWIDE STRIKES AND PROTESTS: ACTIONS PLANNED IN THE US AND DOZENS OF COUNTRIES\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A union in Germany, meanwhile, expects work stoppages in at least ten fulfillment centers in that country alone today. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  employees worldwide are demanding higher pay, better working conditions, and the right to join unions. The company has faced this sort of pressure before. Earlier this year, a warehouse on New York City's Staten Island became the first ever \uc2 Amazon\uc2  fulfillment center to successfully unionize, and others are hoping to follow suit or at the very least send a message to the retail giant. As for today's planned walkouts we reached to \uc2 Amazon\uc2  for comment, but have not heard back. In the past, though, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has defended working conditions at its warehouses. Meanwhile, we don't know how this protest will affect your holiday orders, guys.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we'll (inaudible) for that. Andrew, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:38 BLACK FRIDAY DEALS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up on our "Gma" Morning Menu, Becky Worley is in our Black Friday flight deck ready to take off on the highway to the savings zone. Bear with us, folks.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:15 SWEET RECOVERY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tory Johnson also has huge "Deals & Steals" all with free shipping.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:30 BINGE THIS\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also this morning, this might be my favorite story of the day. The husband who woke up after a motorcycle accident thinking it was 1993. How his wife helped him get through it making their relationship stronger than ever. Such a good love story.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, a special holiday weekend edition of "Binge This" from J Lo to college football. What you won't want to miss and "Reasonable Doubt" star Emayatzy Corinealdi is here live. All of that coming up right here on "Gma."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "Gma." You're digging that, huh? It's not what we were listening to in the break, but (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I like that. I was like, da, da, da, it's Black Friday. Here we go, yeah.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks for joining us.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ZOE SALDANA LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE! MONDAY GMA\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) On Monday we're going back to Pandora, kicking off a week with the stars of "Avatar: The Way of Water" starting with Zoe Saldana live in Times Square. Should be a lot of fun.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Definitely looking forward to that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221221eibp0003b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RAIL STRIKE THREAT GROWS LARGEST FREIGHT RAIL UNION REJECTS LABOR DEAL\b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 November 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PROBE, SHOOTING, SANDERS, FIERRO, ALDRICH, ALLEN\par \par \uc2 RAILWAY STRIKE, ECONOMY, SUPPLY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the looming freight rail strike that could impact holiday travel plans.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAIL STRIKE THREAT GROWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LARGEST FREIGHT RAIL UNION REJECTS LABOR DEAL AS DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Another union has rejected the tenure deal and the strike could have a ripple effect across the economy, including delays in shipping Christmas gifts. Rebecca Jarvis is in Chicago tracking it all. Good morning, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. $2 billion a day in economic losses, that is the forecast of what could happen in the event of a strike, which is why the White House is calling this unacceptable, saying they are working to broker a deal but also preparing for all possible outcomes. And here's why. When you look at rail, it is a key part of our economy. The transportation of things like agricultural goods, corn, wheat, soybeans, manufacturing equipment. A strike would stall all of that and seriously hit the supply chain at a key time, right before the holidays, which would then put pressure on the trucking industry.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IMPACT OF POTENTIAL RAIL STRIKE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Truckers would have to pick up more work. There aren't enough truckers to do that to make the economy run smoothly, which is why this is so important to both the White House, as well as American consumers. There are several deadlines to be aware of here. The most important one is December 5th.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While a number of unions have accepted the terms of the agreement, there is one agreement that comes up December 5th. If there is a strike, that will impact all of them. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll keep an eye on it. Okay, Rebecca, thanks very much. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221214eibm0002v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RAILWAY STRIKE DECISION LOOMS KEY UNIONS SET TO ANNOUNCE RESULTS OF LABOR DEAL VOTES\b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 November 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, LGBTQ, ANDERSON, GRZECKA, SLAUGH\par \par \uc2 SUTHERS, SHOOTING, LGBTQ, VICTIMS, RED FLAG, SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 SNOWSTORM, BIDEN, WINDS, NATIONAL GUARD, BILLS\par \par \uc2 SNOW, TEMPERATURES, WIND CHILL, WINDS\par \par \uc2 EARTHQUAKE, RESCUERS, JAVA, TREMORS\par \par \uc2 GOP, 2024, TRUMP, SPECIAL COUNSEL, \uc2 TWITTER\par \par \uc2 IGER, \uc2 DISNEY\uc2 , CEO, ARNOLD, CHAPEK\par \par \uc2 WORLD CUP, TEAM USA, CONTROVERSY, FIFA, INFANTINO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORM TRACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MURDER, SNELL, 911, ROOMMATES, GONCALVES, LIND\par \par \uc2 MURDER, VICTIMS, ASLEEP, ROOMMATES\par \par \uc2 OWENS, SCAM, ONLINE, JOBS, MONEY\par \par \uc2 AMAS, PINK, RICHIE, SWIFT, WONDER, PUTH\par \par \uc2 JOHN, DODGERS, TOUR, RETIRING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DANGER IN THE AIR\par \par \uc2 PROBE, ALLEN, SHOOTING, ALDRICH, ANDERSON, SLAUGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT INVESTIGATION INTO DEADLY COLORADO SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 5 KILLED, 25 WOUNDED AT LGBTQ CLUB; AUTHORITIES PROBING AS POSSIBLE HARE CRIME\par \par \uc2 RAILWAY, STRIKE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And George, now the looming threat of a nationwide rail strike.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAILWAY STRIKE DECISION LOOMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEY UNIONS SET TO ANNOUNCE RESULTS OF LABOR DEAL VOTES\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Key unions are set to announce the results of a vote on a new contract. A thumb's down could lead to a walkout, which could seriously impact the economy.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our transportation correspondent Gio Benitez is tracking the latest for us. Good morning, Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning. Yeah, it's a big day today as we learn if rail workers are getting closer to a strike just as we head into the holidays.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, again, we're talking about two of the biggest unions representing engineers and conductors. And they're going to reveal today whether members accepted or rejected a new wage deal that was brokered by the White House. Now, the workers say, this is not just about money but also about working conditions. And here's why it all matters, this could affect the transport of agricultural, energy and manufacturing goods, dramatically affecting so many industries in this country.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IMPACT OF POTENTIAL RAIL STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONWIDE WALKOUT WOULD IMPACT SUPPLY CHAINS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Supply chains could be paralyzed, potentially costing the economy billions of dollars a day.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, some unions have already accepted a new deal, some have not. And if they don't reach a new deal soon, we could see a strike by December 4th which is less than two weeks away, Robin. It's a big deal.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is a huge deal. All right, Gio, thanks as always. T.J.?\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221214eibl0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RAIL STRIKE THREAT GROWS THIRD UNION REJECTS TENTATIVE LABOR DEAL\b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 November 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MIDTERM ELECTIONS, RESULT, HOBBS, LAKE, ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 PENCE, TRUMP, "SO HELP ME GOD"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP SET TO ANNOUNCE PRESIDENTIAL RUN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MOVE COMES AMID BACKLASH OVER DISAPPOINTING GOP MIDTERM PERFORMANCE\par \par \uc2 JONES, UVA, SHOOTING, LONGO, FAUMUI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR ANSWERS IN DEADLY CAMPUS SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE: STUDENT SUSPECTED OF KILLING THREE UVA FOOTBALL PLAYERS\par \par \uc2 IRAN, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN'S BRUTAL CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT ISSUES FIRST SENTENCE TIED TO RECENT PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 LAYOFFS, AMAZON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE AMAZON LAYOFFS?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: TECH GIANT EXPECTED TO CUT 10,000 WORKERS STARTING THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 RAIL STRIKE, LABOR DEAL, SUPPLY CHAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAIL STRIKE THREAT GROWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIRD UNION REJECTS TENTATIVE LABOR DEAL\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now, we're going to turn now to the rail strike that is looming and how it could impact the economy and supply chains across the country with the holidays approaching. Andrew Dymburt is tracking the very latest. Good morning, Andrew.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. Railroad workers appear to be one step closer to striking. This after a third railroad worker union has rejected a labor deal.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, back in September, a deal was tentatively reached with these unions and Biden administration. But these union workers are set to be at odds over paid time off, sick leave and working conditions. Though, the deal currently on the table, the one that was rejected, is said to offer pay raises of more than 20%. Now, up until now, a work stoppage has been avoided. But with this third union now voting against the deal, a strike is now increasingly more likely. Experts says, if workers do hit the picket line, it could have a devastating effect on the economy. Supply chains in this country could be paralyzed and could cost the US economy some $2 billion a day.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If an agreement isn't reached by November 19th, then workers may hit the picket line the very next day. This as the US enters peak holiday season. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, some pretty bad timing there. Okay, Andrew, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221208eibf0008j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA WORKERS ON STRIKE NEARLY 50,000 ACADEMIC EMPLOYEES DEMANDING HIGHER PAY\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 November 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MIDTERM ELECTIONS, RESULT, HOBBS, LAKE, ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 PENCE, TRUMP, "SO HELP ME GOD"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP SET TO ANNOUNCE PRESIDENTIAL RUN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MOVE COMES AMID BACKLASH OVER DISAPPOINTING GOP MIDTERM PERFORMANCE\par \par \uc2 JONES, UVA, SHOOTING, LONGO, FAUMUI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR ANSWERS IN DEADLY CAMPUS SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE: STUDENT SUSPECTED OF KILLING THREE UVA FOOTBALL PLAYERS\par \par \uc2 IRAN, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN'S BRUTAL CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT ISSUES FIRST SENTENCE TIED TO RECENT PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 LAYOFFS, AMAZON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE AMAZON LAYOFFS?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: TECH GIANT EXPECTED TO CUT 10,000 WORKERS STARTING THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 RAIL STRIKE, LABOR DEAL, SUPPLY CHAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAIL STRIKE THREAT GROWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIRD UNION REJECTS TENTATIVE LABOR DEAL\par \par \uc2 REFUND, AIR TRAVEL, AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIR PASSENGER PAYDAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOT: AIRLINES TO PAY $600 MILLION REFUNDS OVER FLIGHT DISRUPTIONS\par \par \uc2 ARTEMIS I, MOON, \uc2 NASA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 LENO, BURNS, RECOVERY, SWIFT\par \par \uc2 PROBE, HOMICIDE, TYGER, BETTGE, HIPPENSTIEL\par \par \uc2 THANKSGIVING, TURKEY, INFLATION, MCCONAUGHY, LEMPERT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TURKEY PRICES FLYING HIGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU CAN STILL SAVE ON YOUR THANKSGIVING DINNER\par \par \uc2 APPLEGATE, MULTIPLE SCLEROSIS, HOLLYWOOD WALK OF FAME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CONTROL OF THE HOUSE: EDGING CLOSER\par \par \uc2 HOBBS, LAKE, TRUMP, GOVERNOR\par \par \uc2 CALIFORNIA, STRIKE, PAY, DEMANDS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, George. Now to the historic strike at the University of California. Nearly 50,000 academic workers walking off the job at the system's ten campuses. Kayna Whitworth is back with that story for us. Good morning, again, Kayna.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Robin, good morning. It's hard to believe here nearly 48,000 academic workers going on strike. We're talking about researchers, grad students, tutors, and fellows. These are the people that actually do a bulk of the teaching at these universities and things have gotten so difficult, cost of living so high that according to the "LA Times" in some cases they're asking to nearly double their pay. And in addition to these significant pay increase asks, they are look for more benefits like child care subsidies, health care for dependents, longer family leave, and public transit passes. Now, these strikes have forced class cancellations, they've closed down labs, and caused other academic disruptions, of course, right before the Thanksgiving break and just before the final exams.\par \par \uc2 KAYNA WHITWORTH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Negotiations between uc and the unions, listen, they've been ongoing since the spring of 2021, but right now they appear to be deadlocked. The uc system saying to quote here, it "believes its offers are generous, responsive to union priorities, and recognize the many valuable contributions of these employees," but clearly those employees think differently. And, listen, strike activity has been increasing across the country and in other school districts as well, like we saw in Michigan. Also many employees at companies like \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and Amazon are also fighting for union representation, as well and, Michael, here in California, there is really no end in sight yet.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Kayna, thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221208eibf0008v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RAIL STRIKE THREAT RISES SECOND UNION REJECTS WHITE HOUSE BROKERED LABOR DEAL\b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, RECESSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON THE ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT WILL NEW GDP REPORT SAY ABOUT ECONOMY & RECESSION CHANCES?\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ABORTION, FETTERMAN, MIDTERM ELECTIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERSCHEL WALKER FACING NEW ABORTION ALLEGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN CLAIMS GEORGIA SENATE CANDIDATE PAID FOR HER PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SACK, INVESTIGATION, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, NUCLEAR THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUTIN DOUBLES DOWN ON "DIRTY BOMB" CLAIM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CONCERNS GROW AS RUSSIA HOLDS ANNUAL NUCLEAR DRILLS\par \par \uc2 RSV, FLU, COVID-19, MURRAY, MILLER, CHILDREN, SIGNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "PERFECT STORM" OF VIRUSES TAKING HOLD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILDREN'S HOSPITALS AROUND THE COUNTRY STRETCHED TO CAPACITY\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, ELECTIONS, "JUNK FEE", BANK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN'S "JUNK FEE" CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT UNVEILS PLAN TO REDUCE "UNLAWFUL" BANK CHARGES\par \par \uc2 RAILROAD STRIKE, THREAT, DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAIL STRIKE THREAT RISES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND UNION REJECTS WHITE HOUSE BROKERED LABOR DEAL\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to another possible rail strike. The threat rising as a second union rejects a White House-brokered labor deal. Andrew Dymburt is at Penn Station with the big picture. And what it could mean for the nation's supply chain. Good morning, Andrew.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. The threat of a rail strike now looms large once again. This after a second railroad workers union rejected a labor deal. This latest represents some thousands of rail workers. And at issue seems to be paid time off. Now, terms of a deal to avoid a shutdown were reached back in September. But with rank-and-file union members overwhelmingly now voting it down it is back to the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Big picture, this means workers could strike and hit the picket line as early as November 19th. But make no mistake about it, this would be a big blow to the Biden administration. A strike could cripple the US supply chain and further inflame inflation, and it's easy to see why.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAILROAD STRIKE - POTENTIAL IMPACT\par \par \uc2 ANDREW DYMBURT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) By some estimates, a railroad strike could cost the US economy $2 billion a day. That's because nearly a third of all US exports still move by freight train. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is a big blow. Andrew, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221118eiar00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "IMPACT X NIGHTLINE" CHILD LABOR IN MEXICO\b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JANUARY 6 COMMITTEE INVESTIGATION: DONALD TRUMP SUBPOENAED\par \par \uc2 SUBPOENA, JANUARY 6TH, TRUMP, TEXTS, RECORDS\par \par \uc2 JANUARY 6TH, SUBPOENA, TRUMP, OPTIONS\par \par \uc2 STUDENT LOAN\par \par \uc2 AUSTIN, PUTIN, RUSSIA, UKRAINE, WAR, INVASION\par \par \uc2 DEMONSTRATIONS, PROTESTS, IRAN, AMINI\par \par \uc2 VOTING, NEVADA, MIDTERMS, SENATE\par \par \uc2 ELECTIONS, BALLOTS, POLL WORKERS, HOBBS, \uc2 FBI\par \par \uc2 BURGLARIES, CALIFORNIA, HUNTINGTON BEACH\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE FOOTBALL, GEE, WIDOW, HEAD TRAUMA\par \par \uc2 PHILADELPHIA, \uc2 PHILLIES\uc2 , NLCS, SERIES, \uc2 PADRES\par \par \uc2 RSV, RESPIRATORY, CHILDREN, HOSPITALS, FAUCI\par \par \uc2 HOUSING, DEALS, SLUMP\par \par \uc2 TURKEY, SHORTAGE, PRICES, THANKSGIVING, COSGROVE\par \par \uc2 SWIFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, SUBPOENA, BANNON, CAPITOL, RIOT\par \par \uc2 RSV, BELMONT, PEACOE, FAUCI, CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALARMING SURGE IN RSV PATIENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILDREN'S HOSPITALS OVERWHELMED BY RESPIRATORY ILLNESS\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, "MIDNIGHTS"\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM TAYLOR SWIFT'S MUSIC VIDEO, "ANTI-HERO"\par \par \uc2 SHAKIRA\par \par \uc2 SHORTAGE, CHILD CARE, CANDIA, SPINA, BALLIVAN\par \par \uc2 CARMEN, LOPEZ, BREAST CANCER, KESMODEL, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THRIVING IN PINK\par \par \uc2 "IMPACT X NIGHTLINE", CHILD LABOR, MEXICO, FREY\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now, to "Impact x Nightline," the new streaming series from our colleagues here at ABC News. And this week groundbreaking reporting on child labor in Mexico and the truth about US companies are operating under what's called ethical banner. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "IMPACT X NIGHTLINE"\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The roosters are crowing, so the sun is about to come up.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We're up before sunrise, on a remote road in southern Mexico, investigating what we've been told is an open secret in this area, illegal child labor on some coffee farms. Not long after we set up...\par \par \uc2 WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking foreign language)\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Workers emerge from the farm's dormitories to begin the day's harvest.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Speaking foreign language)\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Amongst them, children.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Speaking foreign language) Well, there are kids, I think around four years old, maybe younger, carrying baskets.\par \par \uc2 JOHN CARLOS FREY (JOURNALIST)\par \par \uc2 They are going into the jungle. They are going where the coffee fields are.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the kids are supposed to be in school, right?\par \par \uc2 JOHN CARLOS FREY (JOURNALIST)\par \par \uc2 I don't think they're walking to school right now, something tells me.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Doesn't look like it. This is child labor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "IMPACT BY NIGHTLINE"\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Fascinating reporting there. "Impact x Nightline" is streaming now on \uc2 Hulu\uc2 , with new episodes streaming every Thursday.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And coming up, billions around the world already taking part in the festival of lights. "GMA" celebrates Diwali when we come back. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221107eiam0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FORMER DAY CARE WORKERS FACING CHARGES SCARING CHILDREN WITH HALLOWEEN MASKS\b0\par\par\uc2 718 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, MARTIAL LAW, ZELENSKYY, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 BLINKEN, RUSSIA, UKRAINE, GAS PRICES, CHINA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GAS PRICES\par \par \uc2 RSV, SAFETY, BRANCATO, CHILDREN, SYMPTOMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALARMING SPIKE IN CHILDREN WITH RESPIRATORY ILLNESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOME HOSPITALS OVERWHELMED WITH PEDIATRIC PATIENTS\par \par \uc2 TRUSS, RESIGNATION, ENGLAND, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 WORLD SERIES, MLB\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, EWUNETIE, SEARCH\par \par \uc2 ARREST, HALLOWEEN, CROOK, JOHNSON, HAYS, MASKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER DAY CARE WORKERS FACING CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEEN IN VIRAL VIDEO SCARING CHILDREN WITH HALLOWEEN MASKS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, to the fallout from the viral video showing day care workers wearing Halloween masks terrifying toddlers. Arrest warrants have now been issued for five workers involved in the incident. Stephanie Ramos here with the details. Good morning, Stephanie.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. This video is so hard to watch, guys. These day care workers entrusted with caring for toddlers by their parents are the very people frightening them.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the day care workers, seen in this viral video scaring the very children they're hired to take care of, now facing multiple charges for their actions.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF KEVIN CROOK (MONROE COUNTY MISSISSIPPI)\par \par \uc2 We started to looking into the case to see, you know, what facts that were out there to corroborate the video and kind of where it might lead them to pursue criminal charges.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to the Monroe County Sheriff's Office, five employees of the Little Blessings Child Care and Learning Center in Hamilton, Mississippi were charged and arrested. Sierra McCandless, Oci-Anna Kilburn, Jennifer Newman and Shyenne Shelton facing three felony counts of child abuse. And Traci Hutson hit with two misdemeanors, including a simple assault against a minor. In the video, day care workers used scary Halloween masks and appeared to intentionally scare the young children, even chasing and grabbing the toddler at one point in the two-minute video.\par \par \uc2 KATELYN JOHNSON (MOTHER OF CHILD ATTENDING DAYCARE)\par \par \uc2 I was in complete shock of what I witnessed. Whether they had a mask on or the mask off, their behavior was unacceptable. My blood pressure was raised. It broke my heart for my child. I was angry.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Speaking to ABC News overnight, Katelyn Johnson says her 2-year-old is still showing signs of trauma and hardly sleeping through the night. She sees these charges as first steps toward justice.\par \par \uc2 KATELYN JOHNSON (MOTHER OF CHILD ATTENDING DAYCARE)\par \par \uc2 I hope you're enjoying jail and I hope you realize what you've done is serious and it's not a joke and it's nothing to laugh at.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Keegan and Alyssa Hays' 2-and-a-half-year-old daughter was also in one of those classrooms. They want us to show her face to see what their daughter went through.\par \par \uc2 ALISSA HAYS (MOTHER OF CHILD ATTENDING DAYCARE)\par \par \uc2 I want them to see the terror on her face because that is what I see every night.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The owner of the center, who hasn't been charged, says that she was not aware of what was happening and that that kind of behavior is not tolerated. The workers, including the one holding the camera, were fired earlier in the month.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF KEVIN CROOK (MONROE COUNTY MISSISSIPPI)\par \par \uc2 Just the attention that's, you know, that's been given to this at this point might keep something like this from happening or people will look into what's going on, you know, in their day care facilities.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE RAMOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just heartbreaking. The five former workers who were arrested will go before a judge today for their initial appearance and have a bond set. Now, the grand jury meets next year and will decide whether there is enough evidence to indict them on felony charges. Guys?\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, that video speaks volumes. All right, Stephanie, thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7:42, TUA TAGOVAILOA SPEAKS OUT\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Coming up, Dolphins quarterback Tua Tagovailoa set to get back on the field after he suffered that terrible concussion. What he is now saying about the incident and his return.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221104eiak00033\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CAFFEINE JUNGLE CHILD LABOR DISCOVERED AT SUPPOSEDLY ETHICALLY CERTIFIED COFFEE FARMS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,864 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 TWINS, TEENS, ABUSE, ESCAPE, NEIGHBOR, DUNCAN, TERRELL\par \par \uc2 COFFEE, FARMS, \uc2 RAINFOREST ALLIANCE\uc2 , CHILD LABOR, FREY\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's just past 4:00 AM on a jungle road in southern Mexico, known as La Ruta Del Caf\u233\'00\'E9, "The Coffee Route."\par \par \uc2 DRIVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Rising into the highlands of Chiapas, this road is lined with ethically certified coffee farms, and yet we've come to investigate reports of human rights abuses on these remote mountainsides.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We've investigating a farm that has a rainforest citification where we've been told children are working in the fields.\par \par \uc2 JOHN CARLOS FREY (INDEPENDENT INVESTIGATIVE JOURANALIST)\par \par \uc2 David, I've got to tell you that if we are to expose the fact that children are picking coffee, this puts them out of business. So, we're in a little bit of danger, here.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we've arrived. This, behind me, is the farm of interest, today. Quite soon, the day will begin here, and workers will start arriving.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Walk into almost any grocery store in America, and you're likely to see them, little stamps with promos that leave big impressions.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: PUBLIC SERVICE AD BY THE \uc2 RAINFOREST ALLIANCE\par \par \uc2 CHILD ACTOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Gotta look for the frog seal when you shop. Otherwise, you could hurt farmers and the environment.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As consumers become increasingly conscious of what they buy, corporations have turned to an array of ethical certification groups, which advertise their products are bettering the world. Created to fill the gaps in government oversight, ethical certification has grown rapidly.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: YOUTUBE\par \par \uc2 VOICE OVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 You want to do something about it. You must do something about it.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One of the most widely respected names, \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2 , has racked up celebrity endorsements and partnered with iconic American businesses like \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2 , \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 McDonald's\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: MCDONALD'S AD\par \par \uc2 VOICE OVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 McCaf\u233\'00\'E9 believes in 100% Arabica beans from \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2 -certified farms.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But is there a disconnect between what's happening on the ground and what consumers might expect? We wanted to see how ethically sourced coffee was produced in the beating heart of coffee production in North America, Chiapas, the southernmost state in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The roosters are crowing, so sun is about to come up.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On this morning, we're up before sunrise, outside a \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2  certified coffee farm.\par \par \uc2 DRIVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Not long after we set up, workers emerge from the farm's dormitories to begin the day's harvest. Amongst them, children.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Speaking in foreign language). Well, there are kids, I think, around four years old, maybe younger...\par \par \uc2 JOHN CARLOS FREY (INDEPENDENT INVESTIGATIVE JOURANALIST)\par \par \uc2 And they're carrying baskets.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...carrying, carrying baskets.\par \par \uc2 JOHN CARLOS FREY (INDEPENDENT INVESTIGATIVE JOURANALIST)\par \par \uc2 They're going into the jungle. They're going where the coffee fields are.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And the kids are, at least under the \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2  charter, supposed to be in school, right?\par \par \uc2 JOHN CARLOS FREY (INDEPENDENT INVESTIGATIVE JOURANALIST)\par \par \uc2 I don't think they're walking to school, right now. Something tells me.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Doesn't look like it. This is child labor.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Before long, our presence on the public road starts to draw a lot of attention.\par \par \uc2 WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 JOHN CARLOS FREY (INDEPENDENT INVESTIGATIVE JOURANALIST)\par \par \uc2 We're spotted.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Yeah, we are.\par \par \uc2 JOHN CARLOS FREY (INDEPENDENT INVESTIGATIVE JOURANALIST)\par \par \uc2 I mean, (inaudible) who we are...\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. They're waiting right there for us to leave. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On the advice of our local producers, we quickly exit the area.\par \par \uc2 DRIVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I keep going, yeah.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) You can keep going.\par \par \uc2 DRIVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Okay, (speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But later that afternoon, we return to confirm the children we saw are actually working.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We needed to clear the area this morning, because within minutes, they are onto us.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 RAINFOREST ALLIANCE\uc2  CERTIFIED\u8482\'21\'22 2021\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN COMPLIANCE: THE FARM PROHIBITS THE HIRING OF CHILD LABOR.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At the time of our visit in 2021, the farm was certified, and its most recent audit showed that it was in compliance with most \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2  policies, including the prohibition on child labor. But when we arrive, we find children working in plain sight on the side of the road.\par \par \uc2 WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) (Speaking in foreign language) ?\par \par \uc2 CHILD WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language) ? What's your name?\par \par \uc2 WORKER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Alicia.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Alicia. (Speaking in foreign language) ?\par \par \uc2 CHILD WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Elias.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Elias. Si, Elias.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) More than a dozen of them carrying sacks, sorting coffee cherries, some apparently under the age of six, while infants sit out in the tropical heat as their parents labor for hours, nearby. One boy agrees to speak with us.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How old are you?\par \par \uc2 CHILD WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 JOHN CARLOS FREY (INDEPENDENT INVESTIGATIVE JOURANALIST)\par \par \uc2 Twelve.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's very difficult work, huh?\par \par \uc2 CHILD WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YES, IT'S A LITTLE BIT TOUGH.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language) ? Is there a school here for you?\par \par \uc2 CHILD WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There can be no question about child labor on this farm.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But days before we saw children working on the coffee farm, we saw another side of life for \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2  farmers. We met up with Fernando Bautista, a regional lead for \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2  who brought us to a different form that he said was a model for the organization.\par \par \uc2 FERNANDO BAUTISTA (REGIONAL COORDINATOR FOR \uc2 RAINFOREST ALLIANCE\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS COMMUNITY DEDICATES ITSELF EXCLUSIVELY TO COFFEE PRODUCTION. WE AT THE \uc2 RAINFOREST ALLIANCE\uc2  ARE WORKING WITH THEM AND ENCOURAGING THE USE OF SUSTAINABLE FARMING PRACTICES. THE BIGGER FARMS USE HIRED LABOR, SO WE KEEP AN EYE ON THE WORKING CONDITIONS.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We're introduced to one farmer who has nothing but high marks from \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 COFFEE FARMER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SO RAINFOREST IS THE MEANS TO DELIVER A SUSTAINABLE PRODUCT. WE GROW TREES THAT ARE NATIVE TO THE LAND, SO THAT OUR COFFEE PLANTS ARE NATIVE PLANTS, TOO.\par \par \uc2 PRODUCER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAN YOU ENTER "FAIRER" MARKETS WITH THE RAINFOREST CERTIFICATION?\par \par \uc2 COFFEE FARMER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THAT'S RIGHT.\par \par \uc2 PRODUCER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAN YOU COMMAND A BIT MORE BECAUSE THE QUALITY IS HIGHER?\par \par \uc2 COFFEE FARMER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THAT'S RIGHT. THAT'S RIGHT.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But during this visit in late 2021, another member of our team spoke with several small-scale farmers who are part of this \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2  community.\par \par \uc2 WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TO BE HONEST, WE'RE DESPERATE RIGHT NOW. WE'RE FIGHTING TO PROVIDE FOR OUR FAMILIES.\par \par \uc2 PRODUCER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OVER HERE, DO THE CHILDREN HELP THEIR PARENTS PICK THE COFFEE?\par \par \uc2 WORKER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YES. THEY HAVE TO HELP OUT. BECAUSE AFTER WE MAKE THE PAYMENTS, THERE'S ALMOST NOTHING LEFT. WE CAN BARELY MAKE ENDS MEET.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On our last day in Tapachula, we met back up with Fernando, the \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2  regional lead, to ask him about the children we saw working.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We took these pictures at one of your certified farms. We watched very young children working hard. How can it be that we come here for a week and can easily see this, right out in the open?\par \par \uc2 FERNANDO BAUTISTA (REGIONAL COORDINATOR FOR \uc2 RAINFOREST ALLIANCE\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 (Speaking in foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AS AN ORGANIZATION, I CAN TELL YOU THAT WE'RE WORKING TO ERADICATE ALL OF THAT. I THINK IT WOULD BE VERY COMPLICATED FOR US AS AN ORGANIZATION TO CONDUCT THESE INSPECTIONS. AS A STAFF MEMBER AT THE \uc2 RAINFOREST ALLIANCE\uc2 , I WOULD BE VERY INTERESTED TO SEE THAT FARM. OF COURSE WE HAVE THAT COMMITMENT TO INVESTIGATE THOSE FARMS. THE GOAL IS TO DO BETTER.\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ultimately, our team filmed evidence of child labor at three \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2 -certified farms in Chiapas last year. So, we reached out to their headquarters, located here in downtown Manhattan and requested an interview with their leadership.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "CHILD LABOR IS A GRAVE HUMAN RIGHTS ABUSE AND HAS NO PLACE IN A RESPONSIBLE BUSINESS." OUR SYSTEM DOES NOT PROMISE TO BE INFALLIBLE. WE ARE TRYING HARD TO HELP PREVENT, MONITOR AND REMEDIATE SITUATIONS AS WE ARE MADE AWARE OF THEM. WE ARE FULLY AWARE THIS OFTEN CAN BE AN UPHILL BATTLE."\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They declined, but provided information in a statement that reads, in part, "Child labor is a grave human rights abuse and has no place in a responsible business. Our system does not promise to be infallible. We are trying hard to help prevent, monitor and remediate situations as we are made aware of them. We are fully aware this often can be an uphill battle," they said. We provided \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2  with a detailed description of what we found on our trip.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "...DID NOT ACKNOWLEDGE ANY INSTANCES OF CHILD LABOR ON ANY OF THE FARMS."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "...IN VIOLATION OF \uc2 RAINFOREST ALLIANCE\uc2 'S ASSESS AND ADDRESS APPROACH TO MITIGATING CHILD LABOR."\par \par \uc2 DAVID SCOTT\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While they did not want to comment on the child labor we filmed without reviewing our footage and did not acknowledge any instances of child labor on any of the farms we identified, they did find some farms were in violation of \uc2 Rainforest Alliance\uc2 's assess and address approach to mitigating child labor, ultimately canceling the certification of three farms we visited.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to David. You can stream the full episode of "IMPACT x Nightline" on \uc2 Hulu\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC NEWS IMPACT X NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ORIGINAL SERIES THURSDAYS ONLY ON HULU\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 New episodes drop every Thursday.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "BLACK ADAM"\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up, "Black Adam," Dwayne Johnson's new superhero movie.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: A SPECIAL MESSAGE\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And later, the surprise for "Nightline" viewers, only.\par \par \uc2 TAYLOR SWIFT (RECORDING ARTIST)\par \par \uc2 Hey. This is Taylor Swift, and you're watching "Nightline."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020221021eiak0002v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RAILROAD DEAL REJECTED NEW STRIKE FEARS AFTER UNION TURNS DOWN CONTRACT\b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 October 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ZELENSKYY, RUSSIA, MISSILE ATTACK, BIDEN, G7, WAR\par \par \uc2 CYBERATTACK, RUSSIA, HACKING, AIRPORTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CYBERATTACKS TARGET U.S. AIRPORTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HACKERS DISRUPT AT LEAST 12 MAJOR AIRPORT WEBSITES\par \par \uc2 KIRBY, RUSSIA, UKRAINE, CYBERATTACK\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, IRAN\par \par \uc2 WALKER, ELECTION, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON GEORGIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TO REPUBLICANS TO RALLY FOR \uc2 HERSCHEL WALKER\uc2  AMID ABORTION SCANDAL\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, RAILROAD UNION, DEAL, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There are new fears of a freight railroad strike after one of the biggest track maintenance unions rejected a deal of the railroad last night.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAILROAD DEAL REJECTED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STRIKE FEARS AFTER UNION TURNS DOWN BIDEN-BROKERED CONTRACT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That strike could cause major economic consequences. Senior national correspondent Terry Moran is in Washington with the latest. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. The workers have spoken and they have rejected the deal brokered by the Biden administration just last month and announced by the President himself in a Rose Garden ceremony. 57% of the workers in the nation's third largest freight rail union, that's the Brotherhood of Maintenance of Way Employees Division of the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 , said no to Biden's deal.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXCERPT FROM TONY CARDWELL'S STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The president of that union declaring in a statement, "Railroaders do not feel valued." The workers are demanding better working conditions.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In particular, they want an end to what they call draconian sick leave and attendance policies, which they say often force them to choose between taking care of themselves or their loved ones or risk losing their jobs. Now, two more big unions, the engineers and conductors, are set to vote on this deal. But there's already been a November 19th deadline set for a new deal.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this morning, the White House is out with a statement saying in part, "The President remains focused on avoiding a shutdown" and, quote, "pledging to support the parties in their efforts." The stakes here are so high. If those efforts fail, the nation could see its first major rail strike in 30 years right in the middle of the holiday season, dealing a devastating blow to the supply chain and to the economy as a whole. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Terry, that would be really, really devastating. Thank you for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221031eiab00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II LYING IN STATE LINES STRETCH FOR MILES AS THOUSANDS WAIT TO PAY RESPECTS\b0\par\par\uc2 865 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BIDEN, RAILWAY STRIKE, DEAL\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, ZELENSKYY, GUTERRES, WAR\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, CHINA, XI, PUTIN\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, PENCE, GRAHAM\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, LAWSUIT, PRICE GOUGING\par \par \uc2 PATAGONIA, CLIMATE CHANGE, CHOUINARD, HERZOG, CALLAHAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GIVING BACK IN A BIG WAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILLIONAIRE PATAGONIA FOUNDER GIVES AWAY THE COMPANY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MUSIC VIDEO, "WHAT MAKES YOU BEAUTIFUL"\par \par \uc2 PAPINI, SENTENCING, JOHNSON, HOAX\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 SYED, "SERIAL", KUKUCKA, MCCLAIN\par \par \uc2 RED SOX\uc2 , \uc2 YANKEES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS: STRIKE AVERTED\par \par \uc2 RAIL STRIKE, BIDEN, DEAL\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, we're going to turn now to more from London. Queen Elizabeth lying in state at Westminster Hall, lines stretching for miles, people waiting for the chance to walk past her coffin and pay their respects. We want to go back to Amy and T.J. on the scene. Good morning, guys.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FINAL FAREWELL TO QUEEN ELIZABETH: HER MAJESTY LYING IN STATE FOR FOUR DAYS BEFORE FUNERAL\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, George. Yes, we are just outside of Westminster Hall and it is open to the public for the Queen's official lying in state. It lasts four full days until her state funeral on Monday. And people have been warned that they may have to wait as long as 30 hours to see their Queen one final time. That line is about four miles long right now and many people saying they're willing to do it. This is just a small thing, a small amount of time to do for a woman who dedicated her entire life in service to their country. So we understand that the line continues to grow and there you can see people in, queueing up. That's what they say here in London, queueing up and standing in those lines, but in good spirits. And we spoke to people last night who said their experience viewing her coffin was moving and it was beautiful. They spoke about how deeply loved their monarch was and still is here in the United Kingdom.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, as you can see, it's about four miles. They actually have a website you can check and they have been updating, letting you know how long that line actually is. It started this morning. When we got up, it was about 3.1 miles. It is, as you said, it's up to 4.2. It's very precise, but they're letting people know how long that line is, how long they might have to be in it. Now, we saw the extended royal family here at Westminster Hall after the procession down the mile from Buckingham Palace paying their respects, taking part in a prayer service. And on our way over this morning, guys, as we walked over here to Westminster, we walked across Saint James' Park and everywhere in town, you see people carrying flowers, they're going somewhere to lay those flowers out and there are a lot of memorials and things popping up. And then, one of our staffers, you all look at this flower arrangement. This is just what people have done. That's a heart and those are flowers, this just popped up in one park here, Green Park, not too far from where we are, so that's all over town right now.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and we've also been hearing the bells of Westminster tolling in Queen Elizabeth's honor and I know, Robin you mentioned this, the Queen died exactly one week ago today, so, so many remembrances in her honor today.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So many. All right, you two, thank you so much. I know you'll have so much more on "Gma3" later today.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:09 KIDS AND DIET PILLS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And coming up in our "Gma" Morning Menu, millions of teens struggle with eating disorders, now the new push by some states to ban selling over-the-counter diet pills to kids under 18.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:12 CELEBRATING HISPANIC HERITAGE MONTH\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also this morning, as we're celebrating Hispanic Heritage Month, we're looking at representation in Hollywood and the stars who are leading the fight to see more diverse spaces on the big screen.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:44 STEVE CARELL LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, Steve Carell is here live telling us all about his new series.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:18 DEALS AND STEALS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we cannot stop celebrating Tory. Her birthday was yesterday. We're not done. She has big "Deals & Steals," bargains on some of your favorite products. All that coming up.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible) and we get the presents.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's her birthday and we get the presents. You're right about that, George. Come on back, folks.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221011ei9f0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CATASTROPHIC RAIL STRIKE AVERTED PRESIDENT BIDEN ANNOUNCES TENTATIVE DEAL\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BIDEN, RAILWAY STRIKE, DEAL\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, ZELENSKYY, GUTERRES, WAR\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, CHINA, XI, PUTIN\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, PENCE, GRAHAM\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, LAWSUIT, PRICE GOUGING\par \par \uc2 PATAGONIA, CLIMATE CHANGE, CHOUINARD, HERZOG, CALLAHAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GIVING BACK IN A BIG WAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILLIONAIRE PATAGONIA FOUNDER GIVES AWAY THE COMPANY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MUSIC VIDEO, "WHAT MAKES YOU BEAUTIFUL"\par \par \uc2 PAPINI, SENTENCING, JOHNSON, HOAX\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 SYED, "SERIAL", KUKUCKA, MCCLAIN\par \par \uc2 RED SOX\uc2 , \uc2 YANKEES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS: STRIKE AVERTED\par \par \uc2 RAIL STRIKE, BIDEN, DEAL\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, first we do have a lot of news this morning, starting with that breaking news. The rail strike has possibly been averted. With the deal down to the wire, tens of thousands of workers almost set to walk off the job, President Biden announced a tentative labor agreement has been reached. Let's go back to our Transportation Correspondent Gio Benitez with the very latest. Good morning, again, Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin. Good morning, again. Yeah, this is a major win for the country because a strike would have led to chaos in the supply chain and for travelers. \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  is telling us this morning that right now they are quickly trying to restore those canceled trains, so all long distance trips and even some local routes. Now, in a statement this morning, President Biden is hailing the tentative agreement as an important win for our economy and the American people. He himself called in around 9:00 PM last night to help seal that deal. Now, as part of this agreement, the workers would get an immediate 14 percent wage increase and time off for medical leave without penalty. This is big news, of course, for the supply chain especially farmers who were desperately trying to find trucks to keep those businesses running. Now, the union members will now vote on this agreement, but for now this strike has been averted, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you so much, Gio. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221011ei9f0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CATASTROPHIC RAIL STRIKE AVERTED PRESIDENT BIDEN ANNOUNCES TENTATIVE DEAL\b0\par\par\uc2 677 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BIDEN, RAILWAY STRIKE, DEAL\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Breaking news first, the rail strike appears to have been averted. With the deal down to the wire, tens of thousands of workers almost set to walk off the job, President Biden announced a tentative railway labor agreement has been reached.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CATASTROPHIC RAIL STRIKE AVERTED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN ANNOUNCES TENTATIVE DEAL\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Our transportation correspondent Gio Benitez is standing by with what this means to get \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  back on track. Senior White House correspondent Mary Bruce starts us off. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. Well, after round-the-clock talks, the President just announcing a short while ago that the railway companies and the unions have reached a tentative deal that could prevent what would likely have been an economically and politically disastrous strike.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, the talks, I'm told, lasted 20 hours. The President himself calling in around 9:00 PM last night to stress that any shutdown would have been catastrophic for the economy. The President, in a statement this morning, is hailing the tentative agreement as an "important win for our economy and the American people." Now, talks had stalled over workers' demands for improved conditions, including scheduling sick time. But the President says that the deal reached is a win for thousands of workers, saying, they "will get better pay, improved working conditions and peace of mind around their health care costs." Describing that as all hard earned. But the President is also describing this as a victory for the railway companies, who will be able, he says, to retain and recruit more workers, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Mary, and the President had a lot at stake politically as well.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, the President had a lot at stake. He was walking a very tight rope here. Look, Biden prides himself as being a champion of labor. He often describes himself in speeches as being the most pro-union president ever. And we know he does likes that nickname, \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  Joe, for his love of the train. But with the midterms looming, just eight weeks away, and his economic recovery is essentially at stake here and on the line, the President had to find a solution and avoid this shutdown. There is no question this is a win for this White House and there's definitely a sense of a huge sigh of relief here at the White House this morning.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mary Bruce, thanks very much. Let's get more on this from our transportation correspondent Gio Benitez. Gio, the disruptions had already been starting to take place. What's this going to mean?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right, George, a strike almost certainly would have led to major standstills in this country, not just for freight but also, of course, for travelers and commuters who rely on trains.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMTRAK LONG-DISTANCE ROUTES CANCELED\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Already, as you said, \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  had canceled all long-distance trips and even some local routes, too. They were preparing for the worst. Commuter lines were also at risk. Now, that the strike has been averted, \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  telling us this morning, that it is working to quickly restore canceled trains. The unions and companies agreed to an immediate 14% wage increase and five annual $1,000 lump sum payments. This is also big news for farmers who, like so many other Americans, rely on the rail system. Many were already turning to trucks but, as you know, there's also a trucker shortage in this country.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Simply put, all of the industries that have been affected by this should feel some relief very soon as this scare is put behind us, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, what a relief. Okay, Gio, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221011ei9f00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II LYING IN STATE LINES STRETCH FOR MILES AS THOUSANDS WAIT TO PAY RESPECTS\b0\par\par\uc2 504 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BIDEN, RAILWAY STRIKE, DEAL\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, ZELENSKYY, GUTERRES, WAR\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, CHINA, XI, PUTIN\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the final farewell to Queen Elizabeth. She's lying in state at Westminster Hall with lines stretching for miles, people waiting for the chance to walk past her coffin and pay their respects. T.J. and Amy are live there in London for us. Good morning to you both.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: QUEEN ELIZABETH II LYING IN STATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LINES STRETCH FOR MILES AS THOUSANDS WAIT TO PAY LAST RESPECTS\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hey, good morning, Robin. Yes, that line now is approximately 3.8 miles long. But people are happy to wait in it to file past the Queen's coffin. It's certainly been a momentous past 24 hours. Most of them saying farewell to the only monarch in their lifetime. Many understandably are emotionally grieving not only the Queen herself, but this is an end of an era here in the United Kingdom.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And what we saw yesterday, the royal family taking part in that solemn service before the public was then allowed into the hall. \uc2 King Charles\uc2 , Queen Consort alongside of his siblings, Anne, Andrew and Edward, sons, William, Harry all there with their lives, with their wives. And all the women when they did step up, they did curtsy to the Queen.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FINAL FAREWELL TO QUEEN ELIZABETH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HER MAJESTY LYING IN STATE FOR FOUR DAYS BEFORE FUNERAL\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Meghan Markle in particular paid her respects with a deep curtsy. A lot of people took note of this because she told actually in an interview that when she first met the Queen, she had to learn really quickly how to curtsy. And she maybe did it a little too deep, and now people look at this as maybe a sweet moment there. And on this first full day that the Queen is lying in state, King Charles is actually getting his first day off as King. Of course, he's been going nonstop since his mother's death.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now, William and Kate, actually on their way to Sandringham right now to view flowers left at the Queen's estate there. Robin, we can tell you, as we walked over, flowers are popping up and little memorials, makeshift memorials all over the place here. And it's kind of a quiet London right now. People are being respectful but it seemed a little quiet.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, quiet. People walking around with flowers and some of them are still wiping tears from their faces, Robin. It's a very emotional time here in London.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm sure it is. And we'll check back with you throughout the morning. Thank you both.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221011ei9f00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RACE TO PREVENT CATASTROPHIC RAIL STRIKE COULD DISRUPT SUPPLY CHAIN & FORCE PRICES EVEN HIGHER\b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RELENTLESS RISE\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, STOCKS, PRICES, WAGES, FED, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 RAILWAYS, STRIKE, DISRUPT, SUPPLY CHAIN\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, George. We're gonna turn to that situation that could threaten the economy even more, this impending railway strike that has Washington bracing for the worst. The Labor Secretary today will meet with union and rail officials, but those two sides still remain very far apart. Our transportation correspondent Gio Benitez is live right now at Penn Station with more on this. Good morning, Gio.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE TO PREVENT CATASTROPHIC RAIL STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHUTDOWN COULD DISRUPT SUPPLY CHAIN & FORCE PRICES EVEN HIGHER\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Cecilia, good morning. Yeah, right now it is a race against the clock to avoid this major disruption to the supply chain. Tens of thousands of rail workers, they are threatening to strike as early as Friday. They're calling for better working conditions. And that threat is already causing issues, \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  canceling some trips going through Chicago. And some freight companies, they've now stopped accepting goods.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, the Consumer Brands Association wrote an urgent letter to the White House saying that this "Will hurt US consumers and imperial the availability, affordability and accessibility of everyday essential products." This happening after some of the largest freight carries reported record income last year, an industry trade group says a strike could cost the economy $2 billion a day.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, Washington is scrambling to solve this issue. We know that the President got on the phone this week with the unions and the companies hoping to avoid this strike. Whit.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221010ei9e0002v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAJOR RAIL STRIKE THREAT DISRUPTION COULD PARALYZE SUPPLY CHAIN, DAMAGE ECONOMY\b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, TRIBUTE, PROCESSION\par \par \uc2 RAIL STRIKE, WATTERS, SWONK, PELOSI, TINKHAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR RAIL STRIKE THREAT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the meantime, we do move onto the other news this Wednesday night. Here in this country, the race underway at this hour to try to avert a massive rail strike. With inflation and high prices already, what could this do to the already stretched supply chain? Frantic meetings in Washington today between the companies and unions. What workers are demanding. Here's our transportation correspondent, Gio Benitez, tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DISRUPTION COULD PARALYZE SUPPLY CHAIN, DAMAGE ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, a race against the clock to stop a supply chain crisis and travel nightmare, with 60,000 rail workers threatening to strike tomorrow at midnight. \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  now canceling its long-distance trips on 14 routes. Nearly all of its trains outside the Northeast Corridor would be impacted, with possible shutdowns of local commuter lines.\par \par \uc2 PASSENGER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I was like, oh, my God. How am I going to get to work next week?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nearly a third of the freight in this country is moved by rail, everything from oil to cars to crops. Farmers like Tom Watters are worried.\par \par \uc2 TOM WATTERS (FARMER)\par \par \uc2 There's a lot of fear. We need the government to step in and do something about this.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He needs to move wheat out of grain elevators to make room for beans and corn before they die in the fields. Americans are already facing sky-high prices, and experts warn a strike could cripple a stressed supply chain.\par \par \uc2 DIANE SWONK (CHIEF ECONOMIST \uc2 KPMG\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 It means that you could see empty shelves at your store, where goods that were supposed to get there just could not get there. If it goes on for any length of time, it starts to spin out of control fairly quickly.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Railroad companies have shed thousands of workers in recent years, with profits soaring. Washington trying to broker a deal.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE \uc2 NANCY PELOSI\uc2  (DEM-CA) (SPEAKER OF THE HOUSE)\par \par \uc2 The main area of disagreement is that there's no sick leave for the workers, and that's a problem.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Workers like Jared Tinkham.\par \par \uc2 JARED TINKHAM (RAILROAD WORKER)\par \par \uc2 Just trying to get us some sick time to be able to take care of, one, ourselves, and two, our loved ones. And that's what we're fighting for, our quality of life.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, while the President and Congress can step in at the last moment, tonight, they say, they want both sides to negotiate in good faith. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll certainly be tracking this in the next 24 hours and in the days ahead. Gio, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020220915ei9e00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WHEN WORKERS REVOLT 15,000 NURSES PAUSING WORK TO BEGIN STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,709 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, RUBESCH, COLVIN, TURNER, ANAAS, TINKHAM\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Good evening. Thank you for joining us. I'm Janai Norman. We begin tonight with workers across America picking up signs and putting their foot down. Teachers walking out of classrooms, a looming nationwide rail strike and, in Minnesota, thousands of nurses now making their demands clear. We join them on the picket line and quickly learned that this goes far beyond getting paid.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DULUTH, MN\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUBESCH (CARDIAC NURSE/VICE PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOC)\par \par \uc2 Going to head to the hospital and set up kind of our base camp, check-in tables, signs, food, all that.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Here on this quiet street in Duluth, Minnesota, just before the break of dawn, Chris Rubesch is preparing for a fight.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUBESCH (CARDIAC NURSE/VICE PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOC)\par \par \uc2 For decades, we've undervalued human service professions, in general, teachers, social workers, nurses included. And so, we need to really redouble our efforts to get people back to bedside care.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The father of one is a cardiac nurse and part of an energized effort to change Minnesota's health care system.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Shut it down.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Over the past three days, nearly 15,000 nurses at more than a dozen different hospitals throughout the state went on strike, demanding higher wages, increased staffing and better working conditions.\par \par \uc2 MARY TURNER (PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOCIATION)\par \par \uc2 Our health care and our profession are in crisis. And we must stand together for each other, our co-workers and our patients.\par \par \uc2 JEAN ROSS (CO-PRESIDENT NATIONAL NURSES UNITED)\par \par \uc2 People are finally waking up and seeing how they've been abused. This country has had a love affair with free and cheap labor for a long, long time.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This strike, the largest ever among private sector nurses, is one of the latest examples of workers staging walkouts across the country and across industries. From teachers...\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 If we continue to do things the way we're going, this whole thing is going to fall apart.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...to factory workers, to baristas...\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We're not going to stop until every \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in the United States that wants a union gets a union.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...even a looming rail strike, this week.\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER COLVIN (CORNELL UNIV SCHOOL OF INDUSTRIAL & LABOR RELATIONS)\par \par \uc2 It's been quite a while since we've seen such a widespread revolt. I think they actually suggest a strength to the labor force, an increasing amount of worker voice and willingness and demand to what they think is due to them.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Chris never expected to find himself on the picket lines.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUBESCH (CARDIAC NURSE/VICE PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOC)\par \par \uc2 I really love being able to come in at the beginning of my shift, to be able to meet a patient and working to get them to a place where they're not only physically recovered, but mentally able to understand and care for themselves. All right, we've been standing strong.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But the seven-year nursing veteran says his job has gotten harder over the years.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUBESCH (CARDIAC NURSE/VICE PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOC)\par \par \uc2 There are simply less staff to take care of our patients. We're seeing nurses whose are burned out, who don't have employers who are supporting them, and who are, in turn, leaving care, leaving the bedside.\par \par \uc2 JEAN ROSS (CO-PRESIDENT NATIONAL NURSES UNITED)\par \par \uc2 For people who don't realize what life is like inside a hospital, it's, I call it, fight, team fight every shift, every day, for enough staff, the right kind of staff, and equipment, even before the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The number of health care workers has faced a steep decline from pre-pandemic levels. Thirty-seven thousand fewer people now work in health care than in February of 2020, but a surge in demand for health care has left many nurses feeling overwhelmed.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUBESCH (CARDIAC NURSE/VICE PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOC)\par \par \uc2 I suddenly realize this cannot be the new normal. This is not the new normal for the care I want to give. I am legally and ethically responsible for what I do for those patients. If something happens, that's on me. If I don't stand up, then I am letting down those patients that I care for. Thanks for coming. Thanks for coming.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Chris works with the \uc2 Minnesota Nurses Association\uc2 . And after contract negotiations stalled at several hospitals this is summer, the union decided to strike against their employers. He says it's about more than just wages.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUBESCH (CARDIAC NURSE/VICE PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOC)\par \par \uc2 Morning shift, all right. They don't want to talk about staffing. They don't want to talk about workplace conditions. Frankly, the administrators of our hospitals aren't at the bedside. They're not giving care. They don't see how our jobs work. And that's why we need to have a voice in the process.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a statement, the hospital group Chris works for says they're disappointed the union is focusing its efforts on a strike instead of at the bargaining table, and that the union has consistently declined their requests for mediation, adding, "We cannot agree to a 27% wage increase because it's not sustainable." For Chris's young family, this hits close to home. His wife Andrea, an oncology nurse, who works just blocks away, also picketing. The two, parents two a 10-week-old son, Oscar.\par \par \uc2 ANDREA RUBESCH (ONCOLOGY NURSE)\par \par \uc2 We're fighting to protect not only our nurses, but also our community in terms of the patients that we take care of.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUBESCH (CARDIAC NURSE/VICE PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOC)\par \par \uc2 Having a child that I'm caring for, it really did make it real clear to me that this is a line that we have to, we have to draw, and we have to stand up and advocate for our patients. Looking at my, my kiddo, I knew that he's totally dependent on me. And, in the same way, we have a lot of patients who are in really vulnerable states.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MINNEAPOLIS, MN\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Whoo. That's right. (Inaudible) northwestern nurses. Woo.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Two hours down the road from Chris in Minneapolis, Kelly Anaas is also striking.\par \par \uc2 KELLY ANAAS (ICU NURSE)\par \par \uc2 We are out on the picket line for the second of a three-day strike out here advocating for safe staffing inside hospitals around the state of Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A registered ICU nurse, Kelly has been working in hospitals for 14 years.\par \par \uc2 KELLY ANAAS (ICU NURSE)\par \par \uc2 We need a say in what staffing looks like inside the hospitals and a way of protections for when we do stand up and advocate for our patients to have safe conditions and for us not to take on more than we are able to safely care for.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a statement, Kelly's employer said they're "scheduling a bargaining session next week to continue working with the \uc2 Minnesota Nurses Association\uc2  for a contract agreement that recognizes both the contributions of our nurses and our commitment to our patients and communities." This isn't the first strike Kelly has been a part of. Back in 2010, nurses across the state went on strike over staffing issues, and again in 2016 for better health care benefits.\par \par \uc2 KELLY ANAAS (ICU NURSE)\par \par \uc2 This time feels different. It just feels like an opportunity for us to really save our profession, in a lot of ways.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The issues raised here by Minnesota's nurses are emblematic of the frustrations among workers across the country.\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER COLVIN (CORNELL UNIV SCHOOL OF INDUSTRIAL & LABOR RELATIONS)\par \par \uc2 There are economic forces that are coming across the whole economy. Inflation is up, and that, as well as workers' wages.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And the pandemic changing the way people view work, from some quietly quitting their jobs to others demanding better conditions.\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER COLVIN (CORNELL UNIV SCHOOL OF INDUSTRIAL & LABOR RELATIONS)\par \par \uc2 COVID was the big shock of people working from home. A lot of job loss that, thankfully, we're starting to recover from, but also a lot of concerns about health and safety.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The result? An increase in unionization efforts at major companies like Amazon and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 . A recent poll found that public approval for labor unions is at its highest point since the mid-'60s.\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDER COLVIN (CORNELL UNIV SCHOOL OF INDUSTRIAL & LABOR RELATIONS)\par \par \uc2 We're seeing a real viral spread of organizing activity. This current generation is not willing to accept things that we've been putting up with for quite a while. And I think that's a real sea change.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And labor strikes aren't bound to go away anytime soon. Rail workers are gearing up for a massive strike this week, the first in over three decades, amid a dispute with railway companies over pay and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 JARED TINKHAM UNION MEMBER\par \par \uc2 Trying to get us some sick time to be able to take care of, one, ourselves, and two, our loved ones. That's what we're fighting for, is the quality of life.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Back in Minnesota, Chris views his participation in the strike as a form of service to his patients.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS RUBESCH (CARDIAC NURSE/VICE PRESIDENT MINNESOTA NURSES ASSOC)\par \par \uc2 We can make a difference for our patients not only through the care we give them, but through the advocacy that we are doing on their behalf.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT ON NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GLORIA ESTEFAN\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Up next, our interview with Gloria Estefan, a music legend who set the stage for a new generation of Latin superstars.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020220916ei9e00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PUBLIC OFFICIAL ACCUSED OF MURDER IN COURT CO-WORKER SPEAKS OUT\b0\par\par\uc2 968 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, VASYLENKO, ZELENSKYY\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, KIRBY\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, \uc2 KING CHARLES III\uc2 , NORTHERN IRELAND\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, TRUMP, SUBPOENAS, DOJ, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 STORM, WILDFIRE, MUDSLIDES, RESCUES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRES & FLOODING IN THE WEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RELENTLESS WAVE OF DANGEROUS CONDITIONS\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, ECONOMY, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 REID, GERMAN, TELLES, INVESTIGATION, SCOW\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to get the latest now on the killing of a Las Vegas journalist over a critical article he wrote. The co-worker of the Las Vegas official accused of the crime is speaking out. Erielle Reshef here with the exclusive interview. Good morning, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, George. The politician set to face a judge today. And overnight, in a new criminal complaint, prosecutors calling this crime willful, deliberate and premeditated.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUBLIC OFFICIAL ACCUSED OF MURDER IN COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CO-WORKER OF MAN CHARGED WITH KILLING JOURNALIST SPEAKS OUT\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, one of the suspect's colleagues is sharing what he was like in the workplace before the journalist's death.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, a Las Vegas politician now formally charged with murdering an investigative journalist as one of his former co-workers speaks out to ABC News about what she says she witnessed in the workplace before her boss was charged with the crime.\par \par \uc2 RITA REID (CO-WORKER OF ROBERT TELLES)\par \par \uc2 And I realized that, that it was true and that Jeff had been found murdered. My first thought was Robert Telles. And then I thought, no, it couldn't be.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Until his arrest last week, Rita Reid served for three years in the office alongside Clark County public administrator Robert Telles. She says, as a boss, Telles caused emotional stress and created a hostile work environment.\par \par \uc2 RITA REID (CO-WORKER OF ROBERT TELLES)\par \par \uc2 He came into my office several times in a rage. You saw stress every day in multiple employees, and it just became worse and worse.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Reid also alleges Telles had an inappropriate relationship with an employee that rocked the office dynamic because of preferential treatment he allegedly gave her. Telles has denied he created a toxic environment or had an inappropriate relationship, saying that he only turned to the colleague as a trusted friend for advice.\par \par \uc2 RITA REID (CO-WORKER OF ROBERT TELLES)\par \par \uc2 One of our staff was told during one of the complaints that he had the right to have favorites in the office if he wanted.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Reid says she became so appalled by his behavior, she ran against Telles in the Democratic primary and she and her co-workers approached longtime "Las Vegas Review-Journal" investigative reporter Jeff German with their allegations.\par \par \uc2 RITA REID (CO-WORKER OF ROBERT TELLES)\par \par \uc2 So, we decided that we would go public. We would try to talk to a journalist here in our community and see if somebody felt it was worthy of reporting.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) German wrote a series of scathing articles on Telles' alleged toxic behavior.\par \par \uc2 RITA REID (CO-WORKER OF ROBERT TELLES)\par \par \uc2 Primarily, there were things in social media where he was voicing that anger against the articles.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Telles venting on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and, in one blog post, taking aim at German's reporting, writing, "It was so ugly that you almost had to believe it was true. I can understand why you might have with the writer's skill at pushing buttons." With each article, Reid says Telles' combative response caused anxiety among the staff. He ultimately conceded the primary to Reid, but would remain in office through January.\par \par \uc2 RITA REID (CO-WORKER OF ROBERT TELLES)\par \par \uc2 I guess maybe I felt there might be an encounter one day or an altercation, a verbal altercation, but I just, I could never have imagined this.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Authorities believe Telles cased German's home, lying in wait according to a criminal complaint, then disguised in a reflective vest and large hat, fatally stabbed him as alleged retribution.\par \par \uc2 RICHARD SCOW (CHIEF DEPUTY DISTRICT ATTORNEY CLARK COUNTY NEVADA)\par \par \uc2 The victim, 69-year-old Jeff German, was stabbed seven times.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The politician taken into custody five days later after a standoff with police.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Did you do this?\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE) (CONTINUED)\par \par \uc2 Can you tell us anything?\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Investigators say they found DNA evidence linking Telles to the gruesome scene.\par \par \uc2 RICHARD SCOW (CHIEF DEPUTY DISTRICT ATTORNEY CLARK COUNTY NEVADA)\par \par \uc2 DNA recovered from the victim's hands, under his fingernails, they do identify the DNA as the defendant's.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Reid believes German's commitment to their story cost him his life.\par \par \uc2 RITA REID (CO-WORKER OF ROBERT TELLES)\par \par \uc2 His death was absolutely devastating to myself and my co-workers, the people that he advocated for. He was our hero. I mean, we can never thank him enough.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we reached out to Telles' attorney. So far, they are not commenting. Telles is due in court later this morning, as we mentioned. He is currently being held without bail and has not yet entered a plea. Clark County says, when the allegations of a hostile work environment arose a couple of months ago, it no longer had employees report to Telles and the county is now cooperating with investigators. But the bottom line here, guys, is there is a journalist who lost his life.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Horrible crime. Thank you, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221010ei9d0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SEATTLE PUBLIC SCHOOL TEACHERS TO STRIKE UNION DEMANDS HIGHER PAY AND MORE STAFFING\b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE WEST ON FIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTREME HEAT\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, RECORDS, HURRICANE, RAINFALL\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, EVACUATIONS, ACRES, HEAT\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, XI, SUMMIT, UKRAINE, RYDER, NORTH KOREA, GROSSI\par \par \uc2 STABBING, MANHUNT, SANDERSON, CANADA\par \par \uc2 BANNON, FRAUD, SURRENDER, FEDS, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 FLETCHER, MURDER, ABSTON, DAVIS, MILLER, MULROY\par \par \uc2 JUUL, SETTLEMENT, MARKETING, CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 US OPEN, GAUFF, TIAFOE, NADAL, KYRGIOS, PEGULA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTIVE TROPICS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SHARK, SNORKELING, SKIPPINGS, HAMMERSCHLAG\par \par \uc2 HOLMES, \uc2 THERANOS\uc2 , FRAUD, ROSENDORFF, KREITZBERG\par \par \uc2 APPLE, UPGRADE, STERN, ANDROID, BATTERY, PHONE\par \par \uc2 BIRD, \uc2 WNBA\uc2 , RETIREMENT, OLYMPIAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HAPPENING NOW: EXTREME HEAT AND WILDFIRE THREAT\par \par \uc2 HEAT, WILDFIRE, TEMPERATURES, BLAZES\par \par \uc2 SEATTLE, TEACHERS, PAY, STAFFING, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we go to Seattle now. Public school teachers are expected to go on strike this morning on what was supposed to be the first day of classes. Negotiations over pay, staffing and other issues are ongoing at this hour. Mona Kosar Abdi is there in Seattle for us with the latest. Good morning, Mona.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, good morning. Tens of thousands of students set to return to the halls of schools in Washington's largest school district will instead stay home as day one of a planned teacher strike begins today. The Seattle Education Association and the school board have been negotiating for months over the union's demands for, they say, to address teacher burnout. Over the weekend, educators made signs and trained picket captains in anticipation of demonstrations. The union says 95 percent of its members voted Tuesday in favor of the strike after both sides failed to cut a deal, even rejecting a tentative deal that would have allowed schools to start on time.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Teachers say the last couple of years have been challenging. They are pushing for pay increases, policies to cap employees' workloads, and the right to take personal days when needed, as well as maintaining staffing ratios for special needs and multilingual kids. Again, the strike is set to begin at 7:30 AM Pacific Standard time, but is there still is a last-minute chance that both sides can reach an agreement and avoid those teachers hitting the picket line, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And hopefully something can be worked out. Mona, thank you so much for being there for us. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020221004ei970000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEACHER DROPOUTS HUNDREDS OF TEACHERS STRIKE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,713 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 PROTEST, TEACHERS, VECCHIO, PRINGLE, ROTHROCK, CARDONA\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks for joining us. Tonight, we begin with the alarming teacher shortage across America, just as millions of Americans are sending their kids back to school. Teachers in Seattle on strike, the latest sign of the crisis. And those who do decide to stay are sometimes forced to make painful sacrifices, even taking second jobs. Here's ABC's Mona Kosar Abdi.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) From picket line to picket line, this process repeats itself, drive, walk, chant.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Children support.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hold signs, rinse and repeat.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We see a lot of faces, but who's out here?\par \par \uc2 MEESH VECCHIO (SPECIAL EDUCATION TEACHER NOVA HIGH SCHOOL)\par \par \uc2 You're largely seeing Seattle Education Association Educators, but you're also seeing a lot of community members, a lot of families, some students with families, too.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For 19 years, Meesh Vecchio has taught special education to the students of Seattle. But today, Meesh is skipping class...\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Children support.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \u8230\'20\'26and joining the cause, going on strike, fighting for equity, fair pay, and desperately needed help for the teachers of the country.\par \par \uc2 MEESH VECCHIO (SPECIAL EDUCATION TEACHER NOVA HIGH SCHOOL)\par \par \uc2 So, this is a strike, yes, but this is the work that we do. We're always out here for our students. Not just on the lines, but wherever our students need.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today was supposed to be the first day of classes for Seattle public schools, but all the students are home, because all the teachers, like Meesh, are here.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, there is a growing crisis in American education\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Around the country, so many school districts facing similar challenges.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 As school starts across our area, there's growing concern about who will be there to teach students.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Across the country, in multiple states, in dozens of school districts, they need teachers, as a nationwide shortage of educators ravages the system.\par \par \uc2 BECKY PRINGLE\uc2  (PRESIDENT NATIONAL EDUCATION ASSOCIATION)\par \par \uc2 We did a survey to find out a little bit more about the educator shortage. And we were shocked, honestly, that 55% of them said that they were planning on leaving the profession.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hundreds of thousands of public schoolteachers and other staff have left the field since the beginning of the pandemic. According to the \uc2 Bureau of Labor Statistics\uc2 , what's causing it, burnout tops the list, followed by lingering stress from the COVID pandemic, unfilled job openings leading to more work and low pay.\par \par \uc2 LOCAL OFFICIAL (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We have empty...\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The White House now taking action, meeting with leaders of recruitment companies, Indeed, Zip Recruiter, and Handshake to discuss strategies to fill these vacancies.\par \par \uc2 BECKY PRINGLE\uc2  (PRESIDENT NATIONAL EDUCATION ASSOCIATION)\par \par \uc2 What we're seeing now, which is shocking and has me calling it a five-alarm crisis, they are telling us that it is due to a lack of respect for them as professionals, a lack of professional pay, a lack of the kind of resources to meet individual needs of students.\par \par \uc2 CARA ROTHROCK (THIRD-GRADE TEACHER STATE RUN ELEMENTARY)\par \par \uc2 Teaching in 2022 is definitely a challenging time. I feel like there has never been more work that I am expected to do, and the pay has not kept up with inflation or cost of living or insurance. And so, overall, the stress and the, the burnout and threatening of burnout is really a real issue. I woke up, because I heard...\par \par \uc2 STUDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Footsteps.\par \par \uc2 CARA ROTHROCK (THIRD-GRADE TEACHER STATE RUN ELEMENTARY)\par \par \uc2 ...footsteps.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Cara Rothrock is a third-grade teacher in New Albany, Southern Indiana. The mom three has more than 20 years' experience in education, with a master's degree. It's a demanding job, and the workday is long, with a classroom full of 8-year-olds competing for her attention.\par \par \uc2 CARA ROTHROCK (THIRD-GRADE TEACHER STATE RUN ELEMENTARY)\par \par \uc2 It takes a lot of energy to keep up with a third grader. And so, I have 26 of them this year to keep up with. And so, I'm so tired. And sometimes it just wears you down to do all that. And I just would like to go home at night and be off.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But at the end of the school day, when her students go home, Cara is not even close to finishing.\par \par \uc2 CARA ROTHROCK (THIRD-GRADE TEACHER STATE RUN ELEMENTARY)\par \par \uc2 All right. Have a good day.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) There's paperwork, lesson planning, even tutoring after school, for extra money.\par \par \uc2 CARA ROTHROCK (THIRD-GRADE TEACHER STATE RUN ELEMENTARY)\par \par \uc2 You don't have to type it all out, you just go right there. I'm heading to work for the second time.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And then, several nights a week, she gets in her car and drives across town to work here, at Pauley's Freeze, a local ice cream stand.\par \par \uc2 CARA ROTHROCK (THIRD-GRADE TEACHER STATE RUN ELEMENTARY)\par \par \uc2 Let's start with the small banana split flurry.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's the same part-time job she's held since she was a teenager. And now, at the age of 44, she wonders how much longer she can keep it up.\par \par \uc2 CARA ROTHROCK (THIRD-GRADE TEACHER STATE RUN ELEMENTARY)\par \par \uc2 Every year I get older, would I have to give up a second job in order to be 50-plus and still teaching? Because I hope that I can do that, financially.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Cara is not alone. More than 1,000 miles away in Denver, Colorado, K.J. Larsen (PH) is feeling the immense pressure, as well.\par \par \uc2 FORMER TEACHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I think the kids liked me. I really connected with them.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) K.J. started teaching at a charter school straight out of college, eventually moving into Denver's public school system as a business teacher.\par \par \uc2 FORMER TEACHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I really wanted to have a positive impact on my community, because I didn't feel like, and I still don't feel like, you can change like the world at large, but you can impact your local community.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But several family members, including her parents, who were teachers themselves, warned the 23-year-old to stay away from the profession, encouraging her to find another job that was more flexible, with better pay. K.J. recently sat down with my colleague, Mireya Villarreal.\par \par \uc2 FORMER TEACHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 And I think they were like, you can't really, like, keep what you like to do. And, like, living in Colorado, like, on that salary. I was just so exhausted all the time. And I just think she was like, why would you, like, go into a career like that?\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And then you still did it?\par \par \uc2 FORMER TEACHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 And I still did it. Okay, so we're not going...\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Then, a year into her teaching career, the pandemic hit. Educators were being asked to do more with limited resources. K.J. stayed on, but she began to struggle.\par \par \uc2 FORMER TEACHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 My rent increased exponentially. That was, like, a big one, like 48%. And I could no longer afford to live in Denver. And I got nervous that I wouldn't be able to, like, support myself on my own.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) K.J. tried to take extra by taking on a waitress job and doing taxes for nonprofit groups on the side, but it wasn't enough. The pressures of teaching in the pandemic also weighed heavily on her.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How long did you last at that school?\par \par \uc2 FORMER TEACHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Only two years, and then I quit.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) K.J. is now working as an accountant, with better pay and more flexibility. Education Secretary \uc2 Miguel Cardona\uc2  is pushing, in the short-term, to use American Rescue Plan dollars as an incentive to bring back retired teachers without penalty to their retirement benefits and to create grow-your-own programs.\par \par \uc2 MIGUEL CARDONA\uc2  (SECRETARY OF EDUCATION)\par \par \uc2 The fact that we've normalized teachers working at Uber on the weekends or having to waitress on the weekends to make ends meet is unacceptable. It doesn't measure up. We have to do better with salary, working conditions, and teacher voice.\par \par \uc2 CARA ROTHROCK (THIRD-GRADE TEACHER STATE RUN ELEMENTARY)\par \par \uc2 I think the salary for teachers in our country is really shameful.\par \par \uc2 CARA ROTHROCK (THIRD-GRADE TEACHER STATE RUN ELEMENTARY)\par \par \uc2 Let's go put your stuff up.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Teaching remains in Cara's DNA. Her parents were both teachers. Educating students is very much in her blood, but she says her income has failed to keep up with inflation.\par \par \uc2 CARA ROTHROCK (THIRD-GRADE TEACHER STATE RUN ELEMENTARY)\par \par \uc2 We had a comfortable household, with a two-teacher family. It was comfortable. We were never extravagant, by any means, but we were comfortable. And now, I don't feel like that's the case.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Despite working three jobs to make ends meet, Cara is not giving up her teaching career just yet, although she wouldn't want her own children to follow in her footsteps.\par \par \uc2 CARA ROTHROCK (THIRD-GRADE TEACHER STATE RUN ELEMENTARY)\par \par \uc2 Until teaching changes, until the pay is better, the workload is less, I just can't ever recommend that someone go into this profession, into this abusive relationship, and be okay with it.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Mona.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OZZY AND SHARON\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Up next, Ozzy and Sharon. Why America's original first family of reality TV is leaving the country.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020220908ei9700002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LABOR DAY WEEKEND EXODUS PILOTS TO PICKET AT MAJOR AIRPORTS OVER FLIGHT DELAYS\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 September 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP, HEARING, PROBE, DOJ, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 LABOR DAY, FLIGHTS, TRAVEL, PROTESTS, PILOTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LABOR DAY WEEKEND EXODUS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PILOTS TO PICKET AT MAJOR AIRPORTS OVER FLIGHT DELAYS, OPERATIONAL PROBLEMS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the great holiday exodus. Millions of Americans are set to travel this Labor Day weekend. And if you plan on flying, a pilot picket line might greet you at the airport. Transportation correspondent Gio Benitez is at Kennedy Airport in New York. Good morning, Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael, good morning to you. Yeah, it all starts in just a few hours at airports across the country, including right here at JFK.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We're talking about pilots from Delta, United, American, \uc2 JetBlue\uc2  and \uc2 Spirit\uc2 . We've seen them publicly calling out their companies. Now, they're doing it again, telling management to fix those operational problems that are causing all those flight delays and cancellations.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIRLINE PILOTS PICKETING THURSDAY\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, these are off-duty pilots, so airlines insist that this won't affect operations. But you're going to see it at major airports, including here at JFK, Atlanta, Detroit, LA, Seattle and Salt Lake City. It's also one of the busiest travel days for the holiday. So, we're talking about today, tomorrow and Monday as being the busiest, Michael.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEARLY 13 MILLION EXPECTED TO FLY OVER THE HOLIDAY\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Gio, an important new website for travelers that was just announced this morning. What is that?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIRLINE CUSTOMER SERVICE "DASHBOARD" ROLLING OUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEPT OF TRANSPORTATION HELPING TRAVELERS KNOW THEIR RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right, Michael. They are calling it the airline customer service dashboard. Let's go ahead and show that to you right now because this just came out. This is what it looks like. It allows you to select any of the big US airlines, and then compare their cancellation and refund policies, so that if your flight is canceled or delayed, you know exactly what your rights are with each company.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) You could also use it before you even book that flight to see which company works for you. We've made it real easy for you to find. Go to goodmorningamerica.com right now. The link is there. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, that's as easy as it gets. Gio, thank you so much. Cecilia?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220930ei910002v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 OHIO TEACHERS ON STRIKE COLUMBUS SCHOOLS START YEAR REMOTELY\b0\par\par\uc2 592 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON EDGE\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, ZELENSKYY, RUSSIA, STRIKES, MILLS, NUCLEAR\par \par \uc2 RAIN, FLASH FLOODING, ROADS, DRIVERS, HYDROPLANING\par \par \uc2 RAINFALL, FLOODING, ALERTS, DROUGHT\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, STUDENT LOANS, DEBT, FORGIVENESS, \uc2 NAACP\par \par \uc2 PRIMARIES, NADLER, CRIST, DEMOCRATS, GOP\par \par \uc2 SEARCH, TRUMP, NATIONAL ARCHIVES, CLASSIFIED, DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 TWITTER\uc2 , ZATKO, DECEPTION, SECURITY, BOTS, MUSK\par \par \uc2 DROUGHT, RIVER BED, DINOSAURS, DISCOVERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DOGS, PARVOVIRUS, FITZGERALD, EAGLE, CALOGERO, FINN\par \par \uc2 TOUSSAINT, "HOUSE OF THE DRAGON", RACISM, KELLEY\par \par \uc2 SAVINGS, RETAILERS, SURPLUS, HERZOG, MCGARTH\par \par \uc2 FOOTBALL, O'NEILL, OVERHEAD, FLIP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOODING POTENTIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN ANNOUNCEMENT: STUDENT LOAN FORGIVENESS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, STUDENTS, LOANS, DEBT, SCHOOL\par \par \uc2 OHIO, TEACHERS, STRIKE, REMOTE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to that teacher strike in Columbus, Ohio (inaudible) as the first day of school gets under way remotely. Will Reeve has the latest for us. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. Teachers in Columbus, the largest school district in Ohio, are picketing this week, a strike against what they call dilapidated schools. The teachers are also seeking a wage increase, which the district has said it has offered, but teachers say they won't return to the classroom until conditions are improved. They want guaranteed smaller class sizes, full time art, music and PE teachers in schools and a cap on the number of class periods in a day. But their primary complaint and a major sticking point is that some classrooms throughout the district lack proper heating and cooling systems. 94 percent of the teachers union voted to strike this week after rejecting the Columbus school board's latest offer. Time is of the essence here, classes, they're scheduled to start today. With no deal struck, students will begin their school year online in pandemic-style remote learning. A federal mediator called the union and school board back to the table today. That pressure-packed meeting scheduled for this afternoon, guys.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hopefully they can work something out (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 WILL REEVE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. School's started.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:10 JLO'S JAW-DROPPING WEDDING DRESSES\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up here in our "Gma" Morning Menu, JLo revealing new pictures of her three custom gowns she wore to tie the knot with Ben Affleck.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:15 "FRIDAY NIGHT LIGHTS" COACH PASSES AWAY\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're remembering the inspiration behind "Friday Night Lights," Coach Gary Gaines.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:17 ITALY OR OLIVE GARDEN?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, the Tennessee couple whose engagement photos tricked everyone. Instead of Italy they went to Olive Garden. We have a surprise for them. And Lara is upstairs with Lori Bergamotto. Hey, Lara.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:38 SIMPLY THE BEST BEAUTY PICKS FOR FALL\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I sure am. Hey, Michael. Lori is with us and she's bringing us more of what's simply the best. This time, it's with beauty favorites, amazing replacements you won't want to miss. We'll have all of that coming up on "Good Morning America" when we come back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "Gma," and we are excited to have Ozuna to join us this Friday for our "Gma" Summer Concert Series, and we will see you all in Central Park.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Definitely looking forward to that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220921ei8o0003b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PICKING THE PERFECT HEADSHOT HOW THE RIGHT PHOTO CAN LEVEL UP YOUR RESUME\b0\par\par\uc2 1,160 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "VERGE OF NUCLEAR DISASTER"\par \par \uc2 NUCLEAR PLANT, ZELENSKYY, RUSSIA, STRIKES, \uc2 UN\par \par \uc2 MAR-A-LAGO, SEARCH, JUDGE, DOJ, AFFIDAVIT, SHULMAN\par \par \uc2 WEISSELBERG, TAX FRAUD, GUILTY, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MIGRANTS, TRAFFIC, BORDER, WHEELER, ABBOTT\par \par \uc2 HOUSING, RECESSION, REALTORS, BUYERS, SELLERS\par \par \uc2 RAIN, FLASH FLOODING, SOUTHWEST, DROUGHT, WILDFIRES\par \par \uc2 COLLISION, MIDAIR, \uc2 NTSB\uc2 , PILOTS, WITNESSES\par \par \uc2 LITTLE LEAGUE, OLIVERSON, JARVIS, BUNK BED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "GAME OF THRONES"\par \par \uc2 ARMSTRONG, MURDER, INTERROGATION, CLAYPOOL, FILLA\par \par \uc2 HANDCUFFED, CLAY, AR-15, STANDOFF, BOGGESS\par \par \uc2 WATSON, \uc2 NFL\uc2 , BROWNS, FINED, SUSPENSION, GOODELL\par \par \uc2 "HOUSE OF THE DRAGON", PREQUEL, VARY\par \par \uc2 IRON MAN, PROPOSAL, LEG CRAMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT: "VERGE OF NUCLEAR DISASTER"\par \par \uc2 NUCLEAR, ZELENSKYY, UKRAINE, PLANT, SHELLING\par \par \uc2 HOUSING, RECESSION, STALLING, SALES, AFFORDABILITY\par \par \uc2 ASHTON, CANCER, RISK, MODIFY, CONTROL\par \par \uc2 TEACHERS, LAYOFFS, RACE, DICKEY, SPIES, WEST, CARTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 HEADSHOT, RESUME, MCCASKILL, HURLEY, PATTERSON\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the meantime, though, let's turn now to look at the efforts in getting your dream job. Applicants put so much work into their resumes, but could it actually all come down to your head shot? Rebecca Jarvis is back with the latest on how to put your best face forward. Hey, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Amy. Yeah, so much recruiting is now online, so how do you stand out in that digital sea?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When applying for a job, first impressions can be everything, but before you even land that coveted interview, it's your resume and, if you have one, your head shot that recruiters might see first.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW MCCASKILL (LINKEDIN CAREER EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 Think of your head shot as like a virtual handshake. It's your opening (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Andrew McCaskill, a \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  career expert says profiles with head shots receive 21 times more profile views on the professional networking site, but not just any photo will do.\par \par \uc2 PETER HURLEY (PETER HURLEY PHOTOGRAPHY)\par \par \uc2 Head shots are really important for people's personal brand. I mean, if you go on \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  and somebody doesn't have a head shot, it's just print on paper about them, and I don't think people get the whole picture.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Photographer Peter Hurley has specialized in head shots for 20 years. He says the perfect photo is all about lookability.\par \par \uc2 PETER HURLEY (PETER HURLEY PHOTOGRAPHY)\par \par \uc2 Lookability is the image's ability to secure attention from an onlooker. I want them to stop the scroll, stop the feed, look at the \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  profile, click on it, make it bigger, let's see what this person's all about. What is that person giving, what is their essence through the image?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Meet Hunter Patterson, an aspiring sports commentator.\par \par \uc2 HUNTER PATTERSON (LIVE NEWS AND EVENTS EDITOR FOR THE ATHLETIC)\par \par \uc2 I didn't really have a head shot that I felt comfortable with until about my junior year of college.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since then, he's updated his head shot twice, cultivating an online brand and leveling up his image.\par \par \uc2 HUNTER PATTERSON (LIVE NEWS AND EVENTS EDITOR FOR THE ATHLETIC)\par \par \uc2 I wanted to be looking directly at the camera, smiling, and I think it played out pretty well.\par \par \uc2 PETER HURLEY (PETER HURLEY PHOTOGRAPHY)\par \par \uc2 There you go, right there. Hold that.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's a dynamic look that Peter Hurley says couples confidence with approachability. He calls it the squinch.\par \par \uc2 PETER HURLEY (PETER HURLEY PHOTOGRAPHY)\par \par \uc2 I define squinch as a narrowing of the distance between the lower eyelid and the pupil.\par \par \uc2 PETER HURLEY (PETER HURLEY PHOTOGRAPHY)\par \par \uc2 Keep smiling. Oh, wow, that's cool.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Other ways to make your head shot stand out, dress for the job you want, not the job you have.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW MCCASKILL (LINKEDIN CAREER EXPERT)\par \par \uc2 If you are a medical professional, you want a stethoscope. Those little things also kind of help people say, oh, I want to have a conversation with this person.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And shy away from busy backgrounds.\par \par \uc2 PETER HURLEY (PETER HURLEY PHOTOGRAPHY)\par \par \uc2 I don't want another character in your background. You don't need a supporting role back there. You only have a split second of this person viewing you.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Step over, smise, it's all about the squinch these days. It's all about the squinch these days. One concern, and this is a valid one with including photos on resumes, is that inherent bias could come into play during recruiting. Well, \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2  tells us they have tools that remove ethnicity and gender in profiles to help recruiters mitigate unfair bias, Amy.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, I have a lot of questions about squinch, but I'm going to...\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to do a whole segment on squinching in the future.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What is that exactly? All right, what are some other ways that you can get potential employers to take a look at your resume?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOOST YOUR RESUME VIEWS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, it's not just about a picture. Now video is another aspect that you can add to your resume. 80 percent of recruiters are saying that having that video really helps you stand apart, it gives you an eye toward your personality, you authenticity. One thing I would add here is don't forget about your social media profiles.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If you don't have a picture, or even if you do, that recruiter is probably going to \uc2 Google\uc2  you and check you out in addition to what you've put out there.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, in these days 100 percent. These kinds of photos, these head shots can be expensive. Is there a way to get a good one, a quality one without breaking the bank?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GETTING BETTER HEADSHOTS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You've got your phone, right? Everybody can take an excellent photo with their phone. If you're not able to do it yourself, a selfie is not always the best move here, look to a friend to really help you go through photos, try different settings, get comfortable, and make sure you're happy with it before you post it. Yes, these head shots, they can be very expensive. It's not the path you have to go through to get the job of your dreams, Amy.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rebecca. Thank you. I learned so much. Thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Squinching our way out.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Cecilia?\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to see you guys next week for a segment on squinching. Thanks, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220920ei8j0003e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LIGHTNING STRIKE SURVIVOR SPEAKS OUT 28-YEAR-OLD RECOVERING AFTER DC STRIKE THAT KILLED THREE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,418 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, TRUMP, SALTZBURG, GIULIANI, WEISSELBERG\par \par \uc2 PRIMARIES, TRUMP, CHENEY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION REDUCTION ACT, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN'S BIG VICTORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SET TO SIGN INFLATION REDUCTION ACT INTO LAW\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, FLASH FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLASH FLOOD EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE THAN 100 HOMES DAMAGED IN WEST VIRGINIA\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, UNITED KINGDOM, VACCINES\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, INVASION, EVACUATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE TOP ESCAPE THE NUCLEAR ZONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINIANS FLEEING AREA AROUND RUSSIAN-HELD PLANT\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, CAR CRASH, ADAMS, CAREY, GOYA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH SCHOOL HEROES!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGIA FOOTBALL PLAYERS SAVE WOMAN TRAPPED IN CAR AFTER CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 RODNI, SEARCH, INVESTIGATION, BROWN\par \par \uc2 LIGHTNING, STRIKE, KONTOSTATHIS, HAGGARD, BONTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIGHTNING STRIKE SURVIVOR SPEAKS OUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 28-YEAR-OLD RECOVERING AFTER DC STRIKE THAT KILLED THREE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we're going to turn now to an ABC News exclusive with the sole survivor of that deadly lightning strike near the White House. She's talking about those moments for the first time. Eva Pilgrim is here now with the latest on her recovery and the reunion with the people who saved her. Good morning, Eva.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. Amber Escudero-Kontostathis suffered second-degree burns all along the left side of her body and now relies on a walker. She says she doesn't remember much about the lightning strike, but she hasn't forgotten the care she received as she spent five days in the hospital recovering or the strangers she says saved her life.\par \par \uc2 AMBER ESCUDERO-KONTOSTATHIS (LIGHTNING STRIKE SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I don't feel good about being the only survivor, that's for sure. I'm grateful, but I just don't feel good about being the only one.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It happened right across the street from the White House, six lightning bolts seen in this footage, strike within half a second, hitting four people, including Amber Escudero-Kontostathis.\par \par \uc2 AMBER ESCUDERO-KONTOSTATHIS (LIGHTNING STRIKE SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I was just surprised to learn that I was struck at all. I didn't really fully comprehend it at first.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Amber was in Lafayette Square during fundraising work for the \uc2 International Rescue Committee\uc2 , waiting on her husband to pick up her for dinner to celebrate her 28th birthday. But as that storm rolled in, she and three strangers took shelter under a tree.\par \par \uc2 AMBER ESCUDERO-KONTOSTATHIS (LIGHTNING STRIKE SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I saw like a tree would, if it would hit by a lightning it would catch on fire and we'd run from the fire.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But there was no time, the lightning killing 29-year-old on Brooks Lambertson who was in town on business along with James and Donna Mueller who were celebrating their 56th anniversary. Amber the sole survivor.\par \par \uc2 AMBER ESCUDERO-KONTOSTATHIS (LIGHTNING STRIKE SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I don't know why I survived. I just don't think it's fair.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The last thing she remembers that day is talking to that couple.\par \par \uc2 AMBER ESCUDERO-KONTOSTATHIS (LIGHTNING STRIKE SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I remember talking to them about Wisconsin because we went there for a family reunion. And I remember asking them how their time was out here. I just hope I didn't stop them to talk to them. I hope they weren't there because of me.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One thing Amber thinks may have helped her, her shoes.\par \par \uc2 AMBER ESCUDERO-KONTOSTATHIS (LIGHTNING STRIKE SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I was wearing my platform sandal, Doc Martens that have humungous rubber soles. They definitely didn't save my life, but I definitely think that it contributed to potentially less of a burn.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, she keeps those shoes close, so close she wore them to our interview. We got the chance to be there for the reunion with the two good Samaritans Amber credits with saving her life.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REUNITED WITH GOOD SAMARITANS WHO SAVED HER\par \par \uc2 JESSEE BONTY (CERTIFIED EMERGENCY ROOM NURSE)\par \par \uc2 Hi, I'm Jesse. Can I give you a hug?\par \par \uc2 AMBER ESCUDERO-KONTOSTATHIS (LIGHTNING STRIKE SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Hi. Amber. Yes, please.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nolan Haggard and Jessee Bonty traveled from Texas and back to DC to meet Amber for the first time. The emergency room nurses immediately performed CPR alongside Secret Service agents.\par \par \uc2 NOLAN HAGGARD (CERTIFIED EMERGENCY ROOM NURSE)\par \par \uc2 I worked on all three other people and she worked on her and a couple of others because we had to move around.\par \par \uc2 JESSEE BONTY (CERTIFIED EMERGENCY ROOM NURSE)\par \par \uc2 I got your first pulse back. I got to go back on you twice. I mean, I remember holding your hand, you're like gripping it really tight and you lost your pulse again.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Amber grateful for the chance to thank them.\par \par \uc2 AMBER ESCUDERO-KONTOSTATHIS (LIGHTNING STRIKE SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 If it weren't for all of you guys, I wouldn't be here. I owe you everything. I'm so grateful for you guys.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She's learned not to take even the smallest things for granted.\par \par \uc2 AMBER ESCUDERO-KONTOSTATHIS (LIGHTNING STRIKE SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I died and came back, I think. I don't I think I had a heartbeat for some time. You don't know when your last day might be.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What she does know is she is lucky and grateful to be alive. And despite her near-death experience, she continues to help others, even though she can't go back to work yet, she's continuing to fundraise for charity online. Guys?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She is a special young woman. Eva, thank you so much. And, Ginger, so many people think they're doing the right thing by taking cover under a tree, and that can be so dangerous.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's one of the biggest misconceptions. Trees are not your friend with lightning. Amy knows this from your personal experience. We see this year after year, people go under there because it's raining and they think, or they think it's the tallest object, that it's safe. It is not, because trees do often get struck. And here's what can happen.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) I want to bring you to this. So, you see the lightning striking. If the tree gets struck, what can happen is it can conduct electricity and it doesn't go deep into the ground, it can actually spread out.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that ground current can impact everybody around. It can actually also, the charge from it can jump from tree to person. So, I don't know where she was in relationship to the tree and the other people, perhaps she was farther away, it was a less of a charge. But also, thank goodness that those nurses were right there.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is it the roots that go down and\u8230\'20\'26?\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Actually will, it can. But it's mostly the ground, it will go right along the ground. And so, anybody that is near the tree is more at risk than the biggest thing is, when you hear thunder go inside. Don't mess with lightning.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's how you stay safe.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, but as you said, that's the biggest misconception because so many people believe that's what you're supposed to do.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. Now, get away from the trees.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So important for the summer. All right, Ginger, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7:43 SAVE ON HOLIDAY TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Well, coming up, we're going to switch gears here, maybe the summer, but experts say now is the time to start thinking about your holiday travel, Rebecca she is here and you've got all the details.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, that's right, Gio. Get this, holiday travel is expected to be the most expensive it's been in five years. So, what can you do to get the best prices? And when do you feed to book by? That's next.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220912ei8g0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "QUIET QUITTING" TREND ON THE RISE EMPLOYEES AVOIDING BURNOUT BY STEPPING BACK FROM BURDENS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,015 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 August 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHAIN OF CUSTODY\par \par \uc2 MAR-A-LAGO, SEARCH, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , ALI, DOCUMENTS, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2 , DHS, THREATS, BULLETIN, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 RUSHDIE, STABBING, INJURIES, REESE, SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 GRINER, APPEAL, RUSSIA, PRISON, SWAP\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, SHELLING, POWER PLANT\par \par \uc2 TALIBAN, WITHDRAWAL, POVERTY, WOMEN, BALKHI\par \par \uc2 RAINS, FLASH FLOODING, RESCUES, MONSOON\par \par \uc2 FOWLES, RETIRE, \uc2 WNBA\uc2 , REBOUNDS, LYNX, OLYMPICS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "SPIDER MAN: NO WAY HOME"\par \par \uc2 "RUST", HUTCHINS, BALDWIN, GUTIERREZ-REED, CARMACK-ALTWIES\par \par \uc2 BEACH, UMBRELLA, PERRAULT, WIND, SCHERMERHOR\par \par \uc2 HYUNDAI, KIA, THEFTS, SPIKE, TIKTOK, USB, CONN\par \par \uc2 LITTLE LEAGUE, WORLD SERIES, NO-HITTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 POLIO, SAFETY, VACCINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLIO DETECTED IN NEW YORK CITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS URGING VACCINATIONS AFTER VIRUS FOUND IN WASTEWATER\par \par \uc2 HECHE, TRIBUTE, CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ANNE HECHE PASSES AWAY AT 53\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTRESS TAKEN OFF LIFE SUPPORT AFTER FIERY CAR CRASH\par \par \uc2 HOLLAND, MENTAL HEALTH, SIMMONS, GOMEZ, DOWD, MENDEZ\par \par \uc2 "QUIET QUITTING", WEST, FARRIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "QUIET QUITTING" TREND ON THE RISE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE EMPLOYEES AVOIDING BURNOUT BY STEPPING BACK FROM BURDENS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to quiet quitting. It's the new job trend that does not involve leaving your company. It's an unexpected spin on work/life balance we first saw in "The Wall Street Journal." And ABC's News chief business correspondent Rebecca Jarvis has the story. Hey, Rebecca, good morning.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Gio, good morning. Instead of handing in their notice, burned out employees are quietly quitting. Here's how.\par \par \uc2 PAIGE WEST (YOUTUBER)\par \par \uc2 Today, I want to talk about a trend that I've been seeing all over the internet as well as from a few of my friends, which is quiet quitting.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Quiet quitting, the new trend redefining work/life balance for young professionals everywhere.\par \par \uc2 CLAYTON FARRIS (FREELANCE WRITER)\par \par \uc2 Quiet quitting is just kind of, it's about quitting the hustle culture that goes along with work in our society. I can still be a very productive active worker and not have to focus on work 24 hours a day.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The hashtag #quietquitting seen over 3.5 million times on TikTok alone.\par \par \uc2 CLAYTON FARRIS (FREELANCE WRITER)\par \par \uc2 I just heard about this term quiet quitting, and I realize that's what I've been doing against my will.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This new form of quitting happens when workers mentally step back from the burdens of work, working the bare minimum numbers of hours and not making their job the important center of their lives.\par \par \uc2 EXPERT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 When I was quiet quitting, I didn't want to constantly feel that stress of working that job and feeling like I needed to put my 1,000% in. And so, I decided to scale that back and really just do the work that was required of me.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And with COVID blurring the lines between home and work, many now using quiet quitting as a way to set more boundaries between their professional and personal lives.\par \par \uc2 EXPERT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I was really struggling with the idea of just a 9 to 5, especially when COVID hit and I was stuck at my desk all day from 9 to 5 at a minimum, working on my computer staring at a screen. For me, that just wasn't the ideal situation.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The trend of putting limits on the job popular among those in their early 20s.\par \par \uc2 JIM HARTER (CHIEF WORKPLACE SCIENTIST GALLUP)\par \par \uc2 Being connected to a mission or purpose is a high a priority for the younger generation. That's something they want. But they're not experiencing it in their current workplaces.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, this really comes down to your priorities. If your objective is work/life balance over income and maybe even job security and you're not looking for big raises and promotions, then this could work for you. It is much easier to pull off when there are nearly two job openings for every job seeker. The risk is that the less invested employees are more likely to be laid off in a down economy. And, Gio, real talk here, I don't think if you or I have quietly quit along the way that we wouldn't be standing here right now.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, you know what, I grew up with Cuban grandparents and saw a lot of honor in work. But that also meant no vacations. So, I guess we could see a little bit of both sides here. What if you're feeling a little burnt out, though, Rebecca? There are some ways to take control here, right?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. A lot of people are feeling burnt out right now. The first question you want to ask is, how much is this coming from you or your employer? If there's a part of it that's coming from you, there's a conversation to be had with your boss, your manager.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AVOID BURNOUT\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Set time, talk to them about the fact that you're feeling burnt out, look at your schedule. Be a problem solver. How can you make sure you're fulfilling all your obligations to your company while also filling obligations to yourself? And finally, think about building community. Gio, it might not be necessary on your team. I'm so lucky it is here for me on "GMA" and all of us. But for people who don't necessarily feel it on their team, look around the company. There may be others. And when you have that community, those friends at the job, it goes by so much more quickly. Gio?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rebecca's real talk on that segment.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rebecca, thank you. Amy?\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Gio.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220909ei8f0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUMMER SURGE WARNING HEALTH CARE WORKERS STRIKE AS CASES RISE\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 May 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WHITE, BRYANT, SINGLETON, FUGITIVE\par \par \uc2 WHITE, ARREST, HUNT, KEELY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FUGITIVE COUPLE CAUGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. MARSHALS ON HOW THEY TRACKED DOWN MURDER SUSPECT & EX-ECTIONS OFFICER\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, INVASION, UKRAINE, KIRBY, BIDEN, ZELENSKYY\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, DOW JONES, S&P 500, RECESSION, STOCKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STOCKS SLIDE AS GAS PRICES SOAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL AVERAGE HITS NEW ALL-TIME RECORD\par \par \uc2 ABORTION RIGHTS, ALITO, MURKOWSKI, MCCONNELL, PSAKI\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, CASES, SURGE, SUMMER\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to new warnings about a summer surge of COVID.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUMMER SURGE WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOME HEALTH CARE WORKERS STRIKE AS CASES & HOSPITALIZATIONS RISE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As infection rise nationwide, more than doubling in the last month, some experts fear those numbers could be even higher. Kaylee Hartung is at \uc2 Cedars-Sinai Medical Center\uc2  in Los Angeles. Good morning, Kaylee.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And good morning, George. We are seeing some alarming numbers across nearly the whole country.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 10+% INCREASE IN COVID-19 CASES\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In 45 states and territories, cases have jumped more than 10% in the last week. And these are just the cases that we know about. Some experts fear because more and more people are testing at home or not testing at all, that these case numbers are under reported and that's the incoming wave that we're seeing could be even bigger than the statistics suggest. Hospital admissions are jumping up 10% nationwide.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVID-19: HOSPITAL ADMISSIONS\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And adding to the problem, thousands of health care workers in California have walked off the job. Here in \uc2 Cedars-Sinai\uc2  Los Angeles, one of the top ten hospitals in the world, union workers are demanding higher pay and safer working conditions. The hospital saying it will remain fully operational through this strike because they are bringing in supplemental workers.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we are two-and-a-half years into this pandemic, and we are nearing another grim milestone. This country is expected to surpass a million COVID deaths in the next week, guys.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Kaylee Hartung, thanks very much. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220525ei5a00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORK FROM HOME BLEAK TO OFFICE CHIC TRANSITION YOUR WARDROBE TO THE WORKPLACE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,772 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 April 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, WAR, ZELENSKYY, SANCTIONS, WEIR, KULEBA\par \par \uc2 LEND-LEASE, UKRAINE, AID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE PASSES BILL TO SPED UP AID TO UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALLOWS PRESIDENT TO MORE QUICKLY DELIVER MILITARY AID\par \par \uc2 SECRET SERVICE, ARREST, PROBE, TAHERZADEH, ALI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECRET SERVICE SCANDAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AGENTS SUSPENDED OVER ALLEGED INVOLVEMENT WITH FAKE OFFICERS\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 JACKSON, CONFIRMATION\par \par \uc2 LOCKE, WELLS, HANNEMAN, FREEMAN, ELLISON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NO CHARGES IN DEADLY POLICE RAID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMIR LOCKE'S FAMILY SPEAKS OUT AFTER PROSECUTOR'S DECISION\par \par \uc2 WOODS, MASTERS, COMEBACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, SANCTIONS, BIDEN, SONIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHO ARE PUTIN'S DAUGHTERS?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIAN LEADER'S INNER CIRCLE TARGETED BY SANCTIONS\par \par \uc2 DRAWBRIDGE, BOAT, SAFETY, PISCIOTTA\par \par \uc2 GAS, PRICES, THEFT, DE HAAN, CHRONISTER, BIG OIL\par \par \uc2 PROPOSAL, NBA, PONTY, HATCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINE'S URGENT NEW PLEA\par \par \uc2 SANCTIONS, PUTIN, DAUGHTERS, UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUNISHING PUTIN'S INNER CIRCLE'\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. TARGETS LEADER'S DAUGHTERS WITH SANCTIONS\par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADO, SOUTH, WEATHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOZENS OF REPORTED TWISTERS TOUCH DOWN IN SOUTH\par \par \uc2 CLINE, SOCIAL MEDIA, REALITY, STRUGGLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "OUTER BANKS" STAR'S SOCIAL MEDIA STRUGGLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW MADELYN CLINE IS DEALING WITH 'FILTERED REALITY"\par \par \uc2 ALCOHOL, DRINKING, WOMEN, CANCER, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN & ALCOHOL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDIES INDICATE DRINKING INCREASES CANCER RISK\par \par \uc2 FOOD, INFLATION, SAVINGS, HACKS, FRIDGE, MILLER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MONEY-SAVING FRIDGE HACKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW ONE MOM SAVES UP TO $400 A MONTH ON GROCERIES\par \par \uc2 WALSH, THE WEEKND, MEYERS\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 FASHION, WORK, OFFICE, FEINTZEI, GARCIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORK FROM HOME BLEAK TO OFFICE CHIC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO TRANSITION YOUR WARDROBE TO THE WORKPLACE\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) It is so good to be here in Times Square on this Thursday morning. Love hearing "9 to 5" by Ms. Dolly Parton, and it's the perfect song for now because we're taking a look at how to upgrade your work-from-home wardrobe to moving back to the office. A lot of us are doing that now. If you're thinking of going straight from your comfy sweat pants to a rigid suit, not so fast. A recent article in the "Wall Street Journal" points out casual wear doesn't affect our competence on the job. Great news. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nine to five, dressed in business chic, we used to dress to impress.\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM "THE DEVIL WEARS PRADA"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("THE DEVIL WEARS PRADA")\par \par \uc2 Are you wearing the...\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("THE DEVIL WEARS PRADA")\par \par \uc2 Chanel boots? Yeah, I am.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For whatever industry we worked in.\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM "EVAN ALMIGHTY"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("EVAN ALMIGHTY")\par \par \uc2 I am successful. I am powerful. I am handsome. I am happy.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) But the pandemic turned that upside down, Zooming from home forever changing what we wear to work, TikTokers prioritizing comfort as sales for athleisure wear rose by 36 percent in 2021. Research also showing that people succeed just as much even while wearing comfy clothing.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL FEINTZEI ("THE WALL STREET JOURNAL")\par \par \uc2 Instead of trying to kind of mimic that office setting or what used to be, they found that employees really feel their best when they're kind of mimicking where they are, and so in that case it was at home.\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM "WORKING GIRL"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("WORKING GIRL")\par \par \uc2 A Mr. Jack Trainer to see you, Ms. McGill.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("WORKING GIRL")\par \par \uc2 Thank you, Cynthia.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So now, as employees start going back to their offices, the question is what does workplace fashion look like today?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL FEINTZEI ("THE WALL STREET JOURNAL")\par \par \uc2 We are seeing that change, I think whether it's the way we're talking or what we're wearing, things are going to be different.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, so Melissa Garcia is here now, stylist to the stars, and she has a few simple ways to take the work-from-home look to office chic. And you can shop these looks by scanning the QR code that you should see. There it is, right there on your screen. All right, so let's first talk about this. More Americans returning to the office. What are you expecting to see look a little bit different in wardrobe?\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, so I think, listen, we all got really comfortable being comfortable these past couple years, and I'm not ready to give away all my comfy clothes. So, I think we're seeing a transition to more casual wear in the office but with elevated pieces. So we're going to show you how you can keep your casual clothes but still make them office appropriate.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm getting a sneak peek, and I love this look. Get out here. This is so cute. Talk to me about what you've done here.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 Yes. So, as we see in the monitor, there's Jenn before, in our matching sweat set. This one's from The Gap. I think it's like $55 complete. But...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I get it. It's cute. It's matching. We love those sweatsuits. They became in. But, guys, look at this, what you've done with that.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 How adorable. So we basically, we kept the sweatshirt, the hoodie, but we lost the sweatpants, and we swapped in a pair of jeans. Every woman has jeans in the closet. And then the piece that I really I love is this great, the great blazer. This is from \uc2 Abercrombie & Fitch\uc2 . It's elevated. And if you're going to be doing it over a sweatshirt, get it a little bit more oversized so it fits. And then, of course, a heel. A heel elevates any outfit. So we pulled this whole look together, perfect and office appropriate.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, home run. Great job. Looking good, girl. All right, so let's talk about this next thing. You say that a lot of these looks, like from legging collections, we all have them, that you can sneakily, subtly bring them into the office.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I mean, how many leggings do you have?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So many, and I love them all.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 So many, we have so many, so many black leggings, and we usually wear it like Lil has in this picture.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, there you go. Look at the before.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 There's a, right, a big sweatshirt, nice and comfy and cozy. But here we're elevating it. So, these leggings are actually amazing. If you want to get a new pair, they're from Commando, one of my favorite pairs of leggings.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah because they have a nice little, you know what I mean, that little, yeah.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, they suck it in in all the right places. But we gave her this great white button down, and white button downs, again, are those are the pieces that are always inherently classic and tailored, and we gave her this oversized one from \uc2 H&M\uc2 , which is great because you're still comfortable. You get coverage in the backside because you want to have coverage in the office, of course, pop the color, push up her...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I love the loafer.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 And then of course, yeah, if you don't want to do a heel, a loafer is another great sleek option. Loafers are huge this spring. So, these are from Steve Madden (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Looking good. And then all of those pieces can be mixed and matched. So use that QR code. Now, we're not leaving out the boys. I see Sam and Michael waiting anxiously to hear how they can elevate their game. Get out here. First of all, we're going to see, we're going to see the before shots.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 Yes, so there's Luigi before, wearing a T-shirt and jogger slacks, which we all know guys are loving. But how can we elevate it? So, here we have his crisp, white T-shirt from The Gap. You can always get a new one. You want it nice, crisp and white. For joggers, I would...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You should see Sam. Sam is approving wildly.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 Is it good?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thumbs up.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sam is letting me know that I can wear that tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I would love to see both of you in this look. Luigi, I love it. Is it, it's comfy, right?\par \par \uc2 LUIGI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Very comfy.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 So the pants, yes, so the joggers are from Express. And if you want to do a jogger, for work make sure it has, like, a sleeker tapered leg, not big and baggy, a nice textured feel, and a great cardigan pulls the whole look together with a nice clean pair of sneakers. Spring is a great time to do a refresh on your sneakers.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Emphasis on the clean sneaker because that was another look is that a lot of sneakers are now sold with, like, sort of a beaten-up look.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 Exactly.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Not for the office. Bottom line is we're looking at these gorgeous models. What do you say to folks as they're returning to the office about the wardrobe?\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 You do not have to throw on a full-on suit. You can definitely incorporate your cozy pieces for the office.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, mix and match.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Overdressed so...\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 We all missed the memo today.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, Sam, we love your turtleneck. And guys, as I said, you can shop all of these looks by scanning the QR code on your screen, or just head to our website, goodmorningamerica.com. Melissa, great job as always.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GARCIA (STYLIST)\par \par \uc2 So good to be here. And welcome back to the workplace, everybody.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Coming up, "Deals & Steals." Oh, my gosh, get ready to shop there, too. Small businesses, amazing products, Tory Johnson has done it again and just in time for spring. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220427ei470000p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 JOB UPGRADE AMERICANS LOOK FOR BETTER EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITIES\b0\par\par\uc2 625 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 April 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT, WILL SMITH RESIGNS\par \par \uc2 SMITH, RESIGN, ACADEMY, ROCK, PACKER, KOHN\par \par \uc2 KREMLIN, OIL DEPOT, RUSSIA, ZELENSKYY, SADOVYI, FRANCIS\par \par \uc2 UKRAINIAN, REFUGEES, ASYLUM, US, TRUMP, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 ENERGY, FUEL, COST, PUTIN, PESKOV, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 FOOD, GAS, PRICES, ZANDI\par \par \uc2 PALIN, CONGRESS, YOUNG, MCCAIN, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 CAWTHORN, BACKLASH, TRUMP, MCCARTHY, NEHLS\par \par \uc2 MASK, MANDATE, CHILDREN, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 HUSKIES, GAMECOCKS, AURIEMMA, BUECKERS, BOSTON, STALEY\par \par \uc2 ROCK, SMITH, PINKETT SMITH, MAHER, PACKER, BRIGHT\par \par \uc2 CARTER, OSCARS, SMITH, ROCK, ACADEMY, SYKES\par \par \uc2 SNOW\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, JOBS, UPGRADE, PRILUKER, FABIAS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Welcome back to "GMA" and the great upgrade. More Americans looking to cope with rising inflation and a job position that fits their lifestyle are submitting their resumes. Deirdre Bolton has more.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, millions of Americans squeezed by inflation, left without enough money to cover basics.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PAYCHECK SURVEY\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A recent survey from \uc2 Salary Finance\uc2  shows one in five Americans runs out of money before payday.\par \par \uc2 ROSS PRILUKER (SINGLE FATHER)\par \par \uc2 When you're living paycheck to paycheck, it hits you like a ton of bricks.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Ross Priluker (PH) is a single father from Pennsylvania. He's working multiple jobs to make ends meet. He's a multimedia ad producer during the day, bartender at night.\par \par \uc2 ROSS PRILUKER (SINGLE FATHER)\par \par \uc2 It's a struggle to survive every single day.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And he's not alone.\par \par \uc2 SPOKESPERSON (MALE)\par \par \uc2 These numbers are, are not good. They show a lot of people are in trouble.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MARCH JOBS REPORT\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But a recent bright spot with the March Jobs Report, 431,000 jobs were added to the US economy, the 11th straight month of an amount higher than 400,000. The unemployment rate is also down to 3.6 percent, almost back to pre-pandemic levels. For many workers, especially women who left the job market due to responsibilities at home including childcare, that means they can look for new or better jobs.\par \par \uc2 SPOKESPERSON (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Employers know there is a tight labor market. And in order to attract and retain their top talent, they're being more flexible.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Savannah Fabias (PH) felt stuck in her job at the height of the pandemic. She found a new one and, with the state of the job market, sees a chance to upgrade again.\par \par \uc2 SAVANNAH FABIAS (UPGRADING EMPLOYMENT)\par \par \uc2 I just want something that I genuinely would like to do. I don't wanna hate getting up in the morning.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For some, many opportunities may mean a nontraditional schedule or permanent work from home.\par \par \uc2 SPOKESPERSON (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Evaluate the whole package. That includes your healthcare, benefits, perks.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUGGESTIONS FOR JOB SEEKERS\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Other suggestions for job seekers, know the marketplace for your skill set and know your worth. Don't be afraid to negotiate. Think about details ahead of time including salary and hours. Cast a wide net if you can work remotely. Many are no longer limited by zip code.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) One other expert tip, have your resume up to date, be ready to go. You never know when you're gonna meet a new contact. And if your materials are ready, well, then you will be too.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gotta be prepared.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Deirdre, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE BOLTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sure.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPACE MISSION\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up here on "GMA," meeting the crew on the first private astronaut mission to the International Space Station. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220421ei420000f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEADLY STRIKE NEAR POLISH BORDER RUSSIAN MISSILES KILL DOZENS IN WESTERN UKRAINE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,381 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 March 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKE NEAR POLISH BORDER\par \par \uc2 POLAND, MISSILES, \uc2 NATO\uc2 , KIRBY, RENAUD, SULLIVAN, PODOLYAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKE NEAR POLISH BORDER\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening, everyone. Thanks so much for joining us on this Sunday. I'm Linsey Davis. Once again, we do begin with breaking news on this day 18, Russia expands its war to every part of Ukraine, striking a military training base less than 15 miles from the Polish border. Video shared on social media shows the aftermath. Smoke rising, buildings damaged after being pelted by cruise missiles. Dozens killed, and more than 100 wounded.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That base was used by the US and \uc2 NATO\uc2  to train Ukrainian soldiers. No Americans were there, at the time. But the war is now moving closer to Poland, a \uc2 NATO\uc2  ally, raising fears the alliance could soon be dragged into the fight. And as Russian ground forces inch closer to the Ukraine's capital, we've learned an American journalist, Brent Renaud, was been killed in ab ambush just outside the city. A second American spoke from his hospital bed, describing how they came under fire after passing through a checkpoint.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Leaders around the world now condemning that attack. Tonight, refugees are still streaming out of Ukraine. Nearly 2.7 million have fled their war-torn country, but some experts warn that number could double or triple in the coming weeks. The President of Ukraine visiting wounded troops at a hospital, awarding some with medals for their courage. Tonight, some small kinds of optimism for a possible ceasefire. ABC's Maggie Rulli spoke with a top adviser to President Zelenskyy, and leads us off, tonight, from Lviv.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKE NEAR POLISH BORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIAN MISSILES KILL DOZENS AT BASE IN WESTERN UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight in a major escalation, Russian forces attacking dangerously close to \uc2 NATO\uc2  forces on the Polish border. Just before dawn, Russian missiles striking a military facility near the town of Yavoriv, just about 10 miles from Poland, and an hour west of Lviv. Videos circulating on social media show the aftermath. At least 35 killed, more than 100 wounded. One volunteer fighter, we do want to use his name, telling our Ines de La Cuetara...\par \par \uc2 VOLUNTEER FIGHTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 This morning, we wake up, there's missiles flying everywhere. I didn't have time to panic. I just focused on running, as fast as I can.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That facility, previously used by the US and \uc2 NATO\uc2  to train Ukrainian troops. Our Martha Raddatz pressing Pentagon spokesman, John Kirby.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) If they strike in Poland, what happens?\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY (PENTAGON PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 Look, we take our Article Five commitment very seriously. An armed attack against one is considered an armed attack against all.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The town of Yavoriv, along a route used to supply Ukraine with Western military aid. Russian officials warning such shipments are legitimate targets. But it's also a major route refugees have been using to get out of the country. It's a road American Keith Crowe has driven many times. We meet him outside the train station, in Lviv.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what made you pick up from your life in Santa Fe to come here?\par \par \uc2 VOLUNTEER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I couldn't watch it. So, I went to the border, ran to the border, essentially, rented a car, and saw people walking over.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He says he normally crosses the border twice a day, picking up people who need a ride in Ukraine, and taking them to safety in Poland. When we meet him, he's surrounded by families.\par \par \uc2 REFUGEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking foreign language).\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This woman tells us she's grateful for the ride, as Russian attacks are getting dangerously closer.\par \par \uc2 ANDRIY MOSKALENK (DEPUTY MAYOR OF LVIV UKRAINE)\par \par \uc2 It was like new actions in the war, because we don't have any safety place in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN JOURNALIST SHOT DEAD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRENT RENAUD KILLED IN ATTACK JUST OUTSIDE OF KYIV\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's forces advance on the capital Kyiv, town on the outskirts are warzones. In Irpin, 12 miles to the northwest, Ukrainian soldiers helping to evacuate the living and the dead. Among those killed, American journalist Brent Renaud, he and fellow American journalist Juan Arredondo coming under fire at a checkpoint.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Tell me, please, what is your name?\par \par \uc2 JUAN ARREDONDO (JOURNALIST)\par \par \uc2 Juan.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Juan? Where are you from?\par \par \uc2 JUAN ARREDONDO (JOURNALIST)\par \par \uc2 The US.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Juan describing the attack from his hospital bed.\par \par \uc2 JUAN ARREDONDO (JOURNALIST)\par \par \uc2 We were, we crossed the first bridge in Irpin, we were going to film other refugees leaving. And we got into a car, somebody offered to take us to the other bridge. And we crossed a checkpoint, and they started shooting at us. So, the driver turned around, and they kept shooting. There's two of us. My friend is Brent Renaud, and he's been shot and left behind.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In recent weeks, Renaud was in the region for Times Studios. Times issuing a statement tonight, saying, "We are devastated by the loss. Our hearts are with all of Brent's loved ones. It is essential that journalists are able to safely cover this ongoing invasion and humanitarian crisis in Ukraine."\par \par \uc2 JAKE SULLIVAN (NATIONAL SECURITY ADVISER)\par \par \uc2 I will just say that this is part and parcel of what has been a brazen aggression on the part of the Russians, where they have targeting civilians, they have targeted hospitals, they have targeted places of worship, and they have targeted journalists.\par \par \uc2 REFUGEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking foreign language).\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This woman, inconsolable, describing the attack on her home.\par \par \uc2 REFUGEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking foreign language).\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKES NEAR POLISH BORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ZELENSKYY VISITS WOUNDED WARRIORS IN KYIV HOSPITAL\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Something went through the air, and then boom, she said. Until this, I didn't want to leave my town. She, like so many Ukrainians, now must flee. The white flag marking this van as civilian transport. Today, Ukrainian President Zelenskyy visiting wounded soldiers in a Kyiv hospital, negotiations between the two countries becoming more urgent. Russia still demanding Ukraine change its constitution to commit to not joining \uc2 NATO\uc2  or the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , recognize Crimea as a part of Russia, and the eastern separatist regions as independent.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STRIKE NEAR POLISH BORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOTH SIDES HINT AT PROGRESS IN NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But today, both sides hinting at progress. \uc2 Mykhailo Podolyak\uc2 , a chief adviser to President Zelenskyy who's leading negotiations with Russia, tells me he's cautiously optimistic.\par \par \uc2 MYKHAILO PODOLYAK (CHIEF ADVISER TO PRESIDENT ZELENSKYY)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking foreign language).\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But insists Ukraine will offer no concessions.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) President Biden has spoken quite a bit about the no-fly zone, saying that if America was to implement this, this no-fly, it could lead to World War III.\par \par \uc2 MYKHAILO PODOLYAK (CHIEF ADVISER TO PRESIDENT ZELENSKYY)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking foreign language).\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Forcefully, he says he believes World War III has already started. Now leaders must decide which side they're on.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Major global implications. Let's get right to Maggie Rulli, in Lviv, for us. And, Maggie, those negotiations we know are ongoing. But Russia's trying to squash resistance in occupied areas in the south. Tell us about the latest reports about another mayor being kidnapped?\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Linsey. This is a second mayor in another occupied town. You know, we still haven't heard from that mayor who was kidnapped in Melitopol. That town is now under Russian rule, they're installed a puppet administration. But, Linsey, this has not stopped the protests. We have seen people taking to the streets, despite the dangers. And now, Linsey, the big fear is that Russia seems to be targeting prominent voices within the resistance. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020220314ei3d00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 EMPLOYEE APPRECIATION CELEBRATION "GMA" BEHIND THE SCENES\b0\par\par\uc2 1,268 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 March 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF THE UNION\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, STATE OF THE UNION, UKRAINE, INFLATION, COVID\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, CIVILIANS, ZELENSKYY, POROSHENKO\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, BIDEN, UKRAINE, INFLATION, CHILDCARE, INSULIN\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, REFUGEES, IMMIGRANTS, \uc2 UN\uc2 , SHELTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "ENCANTO"\par \par \uc2 OLIGARCHS, PUTIN, MEDIA, SANCTIONS, SWEENEY, FRIED\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, OLIGARCHS, SANCTIONS, UKRAINE, CHINA\par \par \uc2 LEVIEV, LAWSUIT, "TINDER SWINDLER", OPHIR\par \par \uc2 BIG 10, PURDUE, WISCONSIN, CHUCKY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF THE UNION\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE, APPRCIATION\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, PUTIN, INFLATION, PANDEMIC, CRIME\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, CIVILIANS, RUSSIA, CONVOY\par \par \uc2 FITBIT, SMARTWATCH, RECALL, BURN\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 "JULIA", CHILD, COOLIDGE, "WHEEL OF FORTUNE"\par \par \uc2 RIHANNA, PREGNANCY, FASHION, GARCIA\par \par \uc2 "GMA", STAFF, EMPLOYEES\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good to have you here with us, Janai. Now, to all, all the dedicated staff who not only helps "GMA" get on the air every morning, but who truly make this show one big family. We have been shining the light on them all morning long and there are countless people to name. Here's a look at a few of their stories.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Here at "GMA," our team works around the clock to bring us TV magic.\par \par \uc2 KRIS (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 What I love about working at "GMA" is that every day is exciting and every day is different.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kris is often editing a piece just minutes before air.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Are you almost ready to push?\par \par \uc2 KRIS (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 I don't know, it might be a room roll, put me on the line.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So in his time off, the father of two says he lets his creativity flow, transforming his home for the holidays.\par \par \uc2 KRIS (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 People say my house is eclectic for Christmas. We started a tradition where Santa Claus doesn't just bring presents at night. He turns the whole living room into a winter wonderland.\par \par \uc2 VICTORIA (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 It's 11:00 PM and I'm about to start working on the show's opens.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Victoria also understand the demands of working on a deadline.\par \par \uc2 VICTORIA (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 This is crunch time.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Victoria taking it all in stride.\par \par \uc2 VICTORIA (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 This is what we've been working on all day.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And then to the dance floor, keeping up with her passion for choreography as a member of Dance Works New York City.\par \par \uc2 KECIA (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 My name is Kecia. I'm a stage manager at "GMA," and the show is about to begin so let's go. Whoo.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At the "GMA" studio...\par \par \uc2 KECIA (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 One minute to air.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...our Times Square team is all about the lights, camera, action.\par \par \uc2 KECIA (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 Here we go in three, two.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kecia helps keep the show on track. And backstage, she brings the joy.\par \par \uc2 KECIA (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 I love my colleagues. We, we're like family here.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And her A game as a model, even giving me pointers.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whoa.\par \par \uc2 KECIA (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 When you're on the stage and you're walking, I feel like I'm a whole different person.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nearby on set, Will always lights up for the task.\par \par \uc2 WILL (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 I'm Will. I'm a stagehand and lighting electrician here at "Good Morning America." And right now we're gonna look at the grid.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After he wraps up his day, it's off to rehearsals for his alternative rock band called Radiate.\par \par \uc2 WILL (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 I just do what I have to do so I can burn the candle on both ends because both of these things mean a lot to me.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And there's Oscar who keeps our studio crew fueled throughout the morning.\par \par \uc2 OSCAR (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 First thing I do in the morning is to brew coffee. Then I start stocking the refrigerator with waters, juices, yogurt.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Oscar bringing as much care to catering as he does building his vinyl record collection.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 1,000+ VINYL RECORDS\par \par \uc2 OSCAR (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 I own about 1,000 records in my collection now. I have it at home in the basement and I stack them in bins because it's a lot of records.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) From the Times Square studio to our home offices, "GMA" writer Emily is a standup comedian.\par \par \uc2 EMILY (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 It's like the world's most congested boy band.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She also has a sweet side hobby.\par \par \uc2 EMILY (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 I like to recreate famous paintings with icing on cakes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) From Mona Lisa to Girl With the Pearl Earring, Emily's cake paintings are a work of art. And finally, for those of us who have a need for speed, meet Sam.\par \par \uc2 SAM (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 I'm Sam. I'm a graphic artist for "GMA."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Powered by his creativity and drive, Sam's mission is to explore the world on his bike.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 9,000+ MILES, 18 COUNTRIES\par \par \uc2 SAM (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 I cycle like 9,000 miles through 18 countries. My advice is to just go try it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sam and all our wonderful colleagues, a testament to the power of teamwork, helping us soar to new heights together.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, we, we, we couldn't wait until Friday to celebrate. That's the official appreciation day. And we asked everybody to nominate. So the people that you saw, they were nominated by their fellow colleagues. And because we, there was no way that we could choose. And we could do this on and on and on. Just amazing, just amazing talent.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Amazing how much, I mean, how much creativity is embodied in this entire staff, this entire team. And what a joy to see all that great work they're doing when they're not here.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Because we know how hard they work when they are here.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How they have time to do anything else.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I want a new tradition at those cakes on our birthdays, please, please. They're so beautiful. And I hear delicious, as well.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They are. Let's, can we see the control room? I know that they're patting themselves on the back probably right about now. And - oh, Kecia, Kecia (inaudible)...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hi, Kecia.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She taught me, every hallway is a runway.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, yes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA EMPLOYEE APPRECIATION CELEBRATION, SHARE PICTURES OF YOUR CO-WORKERS & TEAMMATES! #GMAEMPLOYEEAPPRECIATION\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...runway, work it Kecia. There she goes. But the day is, is on Friday. That's the official day. And we wanna meet your work family. Can you share pictures of your co-workers and teammates and why they're a special part of your workplace? And use the #gmaemployeeappreciation. And we do have such appreciation for those that we're blessed to work with.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So great. Coming up, "Snowfall" star Damson Idris is here live.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220321ei320000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 EMPLOYEE APPRECIATION CELEBRATION MAKING TV MAGIC\b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 March 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF THE UNION\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, STATE OF THE UNION, UKRAINE, INFLATION, COVID\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, CIVILIANS, ZELENSKYY, POROSHENKO\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, BIDEN, UKRAINE, INFLATION, CHILDCARE, INSULIN\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, REFUGEES, IMMIGRANTS, \uc2 UN\uc2 , SHELTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WESTERN STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "ENCANTO"\par \par \uc2 OLIGARCHS, PUTIN, MEDIA, SANCTIONS, SWEENEY, FRIED\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, OLIGARCHS, SANCTIONS, UKRAINE, CHINA\par \par \uc2 LEVIEV, LAWSUIT, "TINDER SWINDLER", OPHIR\par \par \uc2 BIG 10, PURDUE, WISCONSIN, CHUCKY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF THE UNION\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE, APPRCIATION\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we are the "GMA" family. Meet the incredible team making TV magic every single morning.\par \par \uc2 KECIA (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 Here we go and three, two.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're kicking off National Employee Appreciation Day early, celebrating our "GMA" crew behind the scenes.\par \par \uc2 DOUG LANCE (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 I'm Doug Lance.\par \par \uc2 SUMMER (GMA EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 Hi, I'm Summer.\par \par \uc2 JAMES CARTER (EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 Hi. This is James Carter.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The power of co-worker connection and how colleagues can become family as we all say...\par \par \uc2 GMA EMPLOYEES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We certainly do say good morning, America. You're used to seeing our faces every morning. Sorry about that, but there are so many people behind the scenes who make it possible to say those three magical words, good morning, America. And this morning we are thrilled to introduce you to the rest of our "GMA" family.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is our control room. Take a look at our script coordinators. Ah, they include Courtney and Phil who make sure we have our scripts every morning. Phil just celebrated his ten-year anniversary with "GMA."\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He was 12 when he started.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He was 12 when he started, right.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible) for all of the city, the country and the world to make this possible. Like our early morning editing team (inaudible) there they are right there including (inaudible). Some of the many folks who help get us on the air each morning.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, of course, our team of producers, but we have a lot of folks who are still working from home. We haven't been able to see them in the office the way we're used to. They had to adapt during the pandemic but, yes, that's family, as well, even though they haven't been in the building for quite some time. But there they are, those smiling faces. But we'll have much more from our team coming up a little later this hour.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220321ei320000e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORKING REMOTELY IN THE "NEW NORMAL" COMPANIES' NEW STRATEGIES TO WORK PRODUCTIVELY\b0\par\par\uc2 1,026 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 February 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN THE BULLSEYE\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, FREEZING, ICY, ACCIDENTS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, ROADS, ICE, WINDS\par \par \uc2 STORM, TRAVEL, AIRPORTS, CANCELLATIONS\par \par \uc2 STORM, SNOW, ICE, FREEZE, WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 PUTIN, JINPING, UKRAINE, TROOPS, KIRBY\par \par \uc2 RAID, ISIS, BIDEN, MCKENZIE, ABDULLAH\par \par \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 , STOCKS, DROP, ZUCKERBERG, WALL STREET\par \par \uc2 OLYMPICS, OPENING, CHEN, ATHLETES, COVID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 NFL, SNYDER, EMPLOYEES, CONGRESS, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH, THRONE, JUBILEE, MURPHY\par \par \uc2 JOBSON, QUEEN ELIZABETH, JUBILEE\par \par \uc2 COVID, TESTS, POISON CONTROL, REAGENT\par \par \uc2 DELIVERYMEN, SNOW, SHOVEL\par \par \uc2 WINTER STORM, FLOODING, WEATHER, POWER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR WINTER WALLOP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: I-95 IDOR IN THE BULLSEYE FOR ICE & FLASH FREEZE\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, INVASION, KIRBY, TENSIONS\par \par \uc2 GOMEZ, THERAPY, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 COVID, MASKS, SAFETY, ALSOP, LEE, LASHER, PERKINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE GREAT MASK DEBATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DISAGREEMENTS OVER SCHOOL RULES REACHING FEVER PITCH\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, MASKS, PARENTING, SIMMONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW PARENTS CAN NAVIGATE SCHOOL RULES\par \par \uc2 HEART DISEASE, AWARENESS\par \par \uc2 LOHAN, SUPER BOWL, COMMERCIAL, ENGAGEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-ON-ONE WITH LINDSAY LOHAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNEAK PEEK AT THE ACTRESS'S NEW SUPER BOWL AD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HAMM, KINDRED STORIES, "NOBODY'S MAGIC"\par \par \uc2 HART, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEVIN HART & DWAYNE JOHNSON TOGETHER AGAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERSTARS TALK FRIENDSHIP, FAMILY & NEW MOVIE\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS, FINANCES, GENERATIONAL WEALTH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAY IT LOUD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING BLACK HISTORY MONTH\par \par \uc2 FITNESS, HEALTH, GREENE, SHREPEE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEVEL UP YOUR LIFE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INCLUSIVE FITNESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORKOUTS FOR EVERY SHAPE\par \par \uc2 REMOTE WORK, RICHARDSON, DOMENICI, GOTO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORKING REMOTELY IN THE "NEW NORMAL"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMPANIES' NEW STRATEGIES TO WORK PRODUCTIVELY\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we're back now with what could be a look at the future.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) 57% of workers say they refer working from home full time even after the pandemic is over. But not being with your colleagues face-to-face can be tough.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ginger, don't we know.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, yes. It's been almost two months since I've been back in the studio, so certainly do. And these last two years have changed our lives in so many ways. This segment is sponsored by GoTo, which understands the challenges businesses are facing and has tips on how co-workers can stay connected and still be productive.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Welcome to the life of a remote worker. Step into my office.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The employees of the \uc2 Raspberry Pi Foundation\uc2  are getting creative with the new normal of remote work.\par \par \uc2 MATT RICHARDSON (EXEC DIRECTOR - NORTH AMERICA \uc2 RASPBERRY PI FOUNDATION\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 It's time for our daily water cooler check-in where we all come in and say hello to each other. Say hi, everybody.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The foundation putting the power of computing and digital technology into the hands of young people worldwide. For executive director Matt Richardson, pivoting their own strategy was key.\par \par \uc2 MATT RICHARDSON (EXEC DIRECTOR - NORTH AMERICA \uc2 RASPBERRY PI FOUNDATION\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 It felt like when we were in an office together, there were ideas floating around. Going remote, it kind of disconnected us. We acted fast in order to be able to stay in touch with each other and continue to collaborate.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For many companies, remote work presents new challenges and new opportunities.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE DOMENICI (SPOKESPERSON & CHIEF MARKETING OFFICER GOTO)\par \par \uc2 As we realize this is the new normal, we have more and more companies coming to us to figure out how they build and use technology to set the stage for the future.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jamie Domenici, chief marketing officer for our sponsor, GoTo, which provides seamless technology experience for growing businesses and says that there are simple ways to connect even when you're working remotely. First up...\par \par \uc2 JAMIE DOMENICI (SPOKESPERSON & CHIEF MARKETING OFFICER GOTO)\par \par \uc2 It's important that you show off your personality. You're welcoming people into your home. So, I always recommend that use your space to reflect you.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE DOMENICI (SPOKESPERSON & CHIEF MARKETING OFFICER GOTO)\par \par \uc2 Next, Jamie says, encourage open communication.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE DOMENICI (SPOKESPERSON & CHIEF MARKETING OFFICER GOTO)\par \par \uc2 Communicate often and always. I like to send video emails, where you'll see me. Instead of reading it, you can see me talking my message.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Finally, use flexible IT products to easily collaborate with colleagues and customers.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE DOMENICI (SPOKESPERSON & CHIEF MARKETING OFFICER GOTO)\par \par \uc2 Technology is critical. And with GoTo, we make it easy so that your customers and your employees can stay connected no matter where they are, no matter what they're doing.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And this company understands the importance of sharing these tools.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE DOMENICI (SPOKESPERSON & CHIEF MARKETING OFFICER GOTO)\par \par \uc2 Hi.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And we were there as they presented a big surprise.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE DOMENICI (SPOKESPERSON & CHIEF MARKETING OFFICER GOTO)\par \par \uc2 So, we're excited to donate to you a year's worth of free technology, GoTo connecting and resolve.\par \par \uc2 MATT RICHARDSON (EXEC DIRECTOR - NORTH AMERICA \uc2 RASPBERRY PI FOUNDATION\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE DOMENICI (SPOKESPERSON & CHIEF MARKETING OFFICER GOTO)\par \par \uc2 We also believe so much in your mission and we love what you do that, on behalf of GoTo, we're donating $10,000 to the \uc2 Raspberry Pi Foundation\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MATT RICHARDSON (EXEC DIRECTOR - NORTH AMERICA \uc2 RASPBERRY PI FOUNDATION\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much. We use all of this to help young people get excited about technology and creating a building. That's what it's all about.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Thanks to the donation from our sponsor, GoTo, the \uc2 Raspberry Pi Foundation\uc2  will be able to help more young people and educators. Cecilia?\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Ginger, thanks so much. Everybody, we'll be right back. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Big weekend in Las Vegas for sports fans. You can watch the \uc2 NHL\uc2  all-star game tomorrow at 3:00 PM Eastern right here on ABC. And on Sunday, the NFL pro bowl at 3:00 Eastern. That simulcast on ABC and \uc2 ESPN\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Took the words right out of my mouth. Have a good weekend.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220301ei240000w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LIVING IN LEGGINGS FROM WORKING OUT TO WORKING FROM HOME\b0\par\par\uc2 992 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 January 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 NOR'EASTER, STORM, SNOW, ICE\par \par \uc2 BLIZZARD, SNOWFALL, WAVES, ICE, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, POLL, SUPREME COURT, COLLINS, DURBIN\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE RUSSIA, TROOPS, BORDER, \uc2 UN\par \par \uc2 NORTH KOREA, KIM, MISSILE, THOMAS-GREENFIELD, ABRAMS\par \par \uc2 FLUKE-EKREN, ISIS, SYRIA, PLOT, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 OLYMPIC, COVID, CASES, BUBBLE, PROTOCOLS\par \par \uc2 RAMS, BENGALS, SUPER BOWL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BRADY, RETIREMENT, REPORTS, SCHEFTER\par \par \uc2 ROAD RAGE, SHOOTING, I-95, POPPER, GERSHMAN\par \par \uc2 SPOTIFY, COVID, ROGAN, YOUNG, LOFGREN\par \par \uc2 WEDDING, SNOW, NOR'EASTER, MARRIED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS HEAVY RAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 NOR'EASTER, BLIZZARD, STORM, TRACK\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, NOMINATION, BIDEN, POLL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT FACES TOUGH NEW POLL NUMBERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS DOUBTFUL OVER ECONOMY, UKRAINE, SUPREME COURT SEARCH\par \par \uc2 BRANDY, HOUSTON, JACKSON, "LUV I LUV", NADAL\par \par \uc2 KRYST, SUICIDE, MENTAL HEALTH, WARNING SIGNS\par \par \uc2 JAYNE, EMBEZZLEMENT, FRAUD, LAWSUIT, TULLY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "REAL HOUSEWIFE'S" LEGAL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ERIKA JAYNE DISMISSED FROM FRAUD & EMBEZZLEMENT LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 LEGGINGS, PANNOZZI, WARD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIVING IN LEGGINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FROM WORKING OUT TO WORKING FROM HOME\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to our series, "Try Before You Buy." Nearly 40% of Americans have purchased athleisure clothing during the pandemic, including leggings.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 38% OF AMERICAN ADULTS PURCHASED ATHELEISUREWEAR SINCE START OF THE PANDEMIC\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To check out some of the most popular brands, Becky Worley went to the experts, two busy moms. You can shop these styles by pointing your phone's camera at the QR code on your screen right now. Good morning, Becky.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, good morning. They are indeed the foundation piece of the athleisure movement. Leggings might be the clothing item most consistently worn by modern women. But do you have to stretch your budget to get comfort and performance?\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They're the ultimate wardrobe staple, leggings. From workouts to relaxing at home to errands out, they're the versatile pant that performs for all shapes and sizes. But not all leggings are equal.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA PANNOZZI (LEGGINGS FANATIC)\par \par \uc2 I want to make sure that they don't fall down.\par \par \uc2 DOMINIQUE WARD (LEGGINGS ENTHUSIAST)\par \par \uc2 They need to have pockets.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHICH ARE THE BEST LEGGINGS FOR YOU?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW SOME POPULAR BRANDS MEASURE UP FOR TWO BUSY MOMS\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The gold standard, a premium brand that costs around $100 a pair.\par \par \uc2 DOMINIQUE WARD (LEGGINGS ENTHUSIAST)\par \par \uc2 Let's see what it is.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Meet Dominique Ward, a mom to 2-year-old twin girls and an entrepreneur that loves yoga.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA PANNOZZI (LEGGINGS FANATIC)\par \par \uc2 It's here.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Alyssa Pannozzi, a spin instructor, serious athlete and mom.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA PANNOZZI (LEGGINGS FANATIC)\par \par \uc2 Because I teach 14 classes a week, I live in leggings.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But how much of a difference is there with less expensive leggings? "GMA" sent Dominique and Alyssa a premium pair and three pairs of leggings at multiple price points to see if they work as alternative options. First up, Fabletics leggings for $59.95.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA PANNOZZI (LEGGINGS FANATIC)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Super, super comfortable. They do not pick up sweat, which is awesome. They also will be awesome for every day just going to get coffee, walking around, taking the kids to school.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Alyssa says they're versatile. And Dominique dressed them up for a dance party with her girls. Then the Old Navy leggings costing $29.99.\par \par \uc2 DOMINIQUE WARD (LEGGINGS ENTHUSIAST)\par \par \uc2 High waist. I like the fit.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Both women like the fit and the color.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA PANNOZZI (LEGGINGS FANATIC)\par \par \uc2 I'm digging the color. They're like a deep maroon. They are super comfortable. I really am enjoying that they are high-rise because when I'm teaching spin, the last thing I want is for my pants to roll over or fall down.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And finally, ColorfulKoala leggings. They're a best seller on Amazon with over 43,000 reviews giving them a 4.6 out of 5 rating. And they only cost 25 bucks.\par \par \uc2 DOMINIQUE WARD (LEGGINGS ENTHUSIAST)\par \par \uc2 They are really soft, really stretchy. It has pockets for a phone, a set of keys, cards, really easy to move in.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They both say the least expensive option delivers in both quality and comfort. And they agree this top-seller has become a top choice for them.\par \par \uc2 ALYSSA PANNOZZI (LEGGINGS FANATIC)\par \par \uc2 It is 11:00 PM and I literally am just getting home from a full day of three classes, meetings all day long. I am still wearing my ColorfulKoala leggings. Honestly, these leggings are incredible. $25, literally the most comfortable pants you might ever own. Feels like butter.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think this trial shows that price does not always equal superior performance, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So, what did Dominique and Alyssa, what did they say that they would buy in the future?\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. I mean, they had, like, pros and cons with all the pairs, including the premium ones. One mom said she'd buy the least expensive brand in the future just because they fit her lifestyle and they really fit her budget. Another still swears by the premium brand, but says she thinks she'll try some of the less expensive options because then she'll have more variety in her wardrobe. Who can have too many pairs of leggings? I'm currently wearing some in my workplace. I may workout in them later. And, yes, I did sleep in them.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And nice extension, by the way. Nice extension. Very impressive that you can do that. All right, Becky Worley, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And coming up, Josh Groban, he is back. He's going to join us live.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220219ei1v0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STILL WORKING REMOTELY? HOW YOU CAN REVAMP YOUR HOME OFFICE\b0\par\par\uc2 928 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 January 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BREYER, BIDEN, NOMINATION, PSAKI, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 BREYER, RETIREMENT, BIDEN, NOMINATION, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, SNOWSTORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRACING FOR A NOR'EASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR SNOWSTORM EXPECTED TO SLAM EAST COAST\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, NOR'EASTER\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, CRISIS, BIDEN, BLINKEN, INVASION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. RESPONDS TO RUSSIAN DEMANDS ON UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEC. OF STATE BLINKEN: "THE BALL IS IN THEIR COURT"\par \par \uc2 VACCINES, COVID-19, BA.2, HAN, STEDMAN, FAUCI, VARIANT\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, INFLATION, KRAFT HEINZ, GROCERY, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROCERY STICKER SHOCK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP MANUFACTURER SAYS IT WILL RAISE PRICES ON DOZENS OF PRODUCTS\par \par \uc2 COLLINS, TENNIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DANIELLE COLLINS HEADS TO AUSTRALIAN OPEN FINALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN STAR ADVANCES WITH STRAIGHT SET SEMIS VICTORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 PRINCE ANDREW, ASSAULT, LAWSUIT, GIUFFRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRINCE ANDREW RESPONDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DENIES SEXUAL ASSAULT ACCUSATIONS & DEMANDS TRIAL BY JURY\par \par \uc2 CRASH, SEARCH, DAVIES, TOP SECRET, JET\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUNT FOR CRASHED NAVY FIGHTER JET\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. RACING TO SALVAGE AIRCRAFT WITH TOP SECRET TECHNOLOGY\par \par \uc2 SCAM, SOCIAL MEDIA, SAFETY\par \par \uc2 SCHNEIDER, "JEOPARDY!"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMY SCHNEIDER'S EPIC STREAK SNAPPED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "JEOPARDY!" CHAMP DEFEATED AFTER 40 STRAIGHT WINS\par \par \uc2 MOORE, BASKETBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE STEPHEN BREYER RETIRING\par \par \uc2 BREYER, SUPREME COURT, RETIREMENT, NOMINEE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE STEPHEN BREYER RETIRING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SET TO STEP DOWN AFTER MORE THAN 27 YEARS ON SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 WALKING, EXERCISE, HEALTH, MORTALITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALKING FOR A LONGER LIFE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: JUST 10 MINUTES PER DAY REDUCES DEATHS\par \par \uc2 DUVERNAY, BUBLE, DION, VEGA\par \par \uc2 FIRE, TODDLER, RESCUE, SURVIVAL, DAHL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TODDLER TO THE RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 2-YEAR-OLD SAVES FAMILY FROM DEVASTATING FIRE\par \par \uc2 SCAM, FRAUD, ONLINE, SOCIAL MEDIA, ROMANCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOCIAL MEDIA SCAMS REACHING NEW HEIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE MOST COMMON ONES & HOW TO PROTECT YOURSELF\par \par \uc2 FAST FOOD, SECRET, MENU, FOOD, HACKS, FROST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FAST FOOD HACKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 MCDONALD'S\uc2  & OTHER CHAINS ROLLING OUT SECRET MENUS\par \par \uc2 NUTS, FRUIT, CRISPS, ME'EAT, SPICES, KITCHENWARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEALTHY EATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DELICIOUS DEALS FROM SMALL BUSINESSES\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 "MOONFALL", BERRY, MOVIE, ACTOR, SCI-FI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HALLE BERRY LIVE ON GMA\par \par \uc2 POMPEO, "GREY'S ANATOMY", TV, MEDICINE, DRAMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "GREY'S ANATOMY" STAR ELLEN POMPEO, LIVE!\par \par \uc2 HOME OFFICE, RENOVATION, TIPS, WORK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STILL WORKING REMOTELY?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU CAN REVAMP YOUR HOME OFFICE\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back now, and we are leveling up your home office. So many people are still working remotely, I myself am coming to you from my home right now. This segment's sponsored by \uc2 Verizon\uc2 , and they are so committed to helping you create the right work space, where you can be productive and very comfortable. And this morning, "GMA" contributor Megan Ryte has some great tips on revamping your home office.\par \par \uc2 MEGAN RYTE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Millions of Americans have pivoted to working from home for almost two years, making it more important than ever to have a space that is positive, purposeful and productive. Experts say the right equipment, decor and technology can make working from home a whole lot easier. First up, let there be light.\par \par \uc2 MEGAN RYTE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Lighting can have a big impact on productivity. You can use a desk lamp that casts off a warm glow. It signals to the mind a calm environment.\par \par \uc2 MEGAN RYTE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Then invest in the right chair. Slouching can cause stiff and achy muscles. An ergonomic chair, like this one, is designed to alleviate stress to the body by helping with proper posture, making it easier to sit comfortably for longer periods of time. Next, upgrade your technology.\par \par \uc2 BRIAN HIGGINS (VERIZON)\par \par \uc2 Nothing is more frustrating than having poor connectivity.\par \par \uc2 MEGAN RYTE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The answer, 5G home internet powered by 5G ultra-wideband. It's new tech available by our sponsor \uc2 Verizon\uc2  to millions across the country.\par \par \uc2 BRIAN HIGGINS (VERIZON)\par \par \uc2 We're going to be delivering that 5G upgrade to wireless phones and also the home. It's going to be 10 times as fast. You simply order this device, it gets delivered to your home, you plug it in, it delivers all the bandwidth that you're going to need, so more capacity for everything, whether it's work, school or gaming. It just simply makes your life that much easier.\par \par \uc2 MEGAN RYTE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Then to dress up your space, bring in some greenery. An easy change, like adding a plant to your desk, can help add in some color and purify the air.\par \par \uc2 MEGAN RYTE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And finally, add some personal touches to your space.\par \par \uc2 MEGAN RYTE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Surround yourself with touches of art and pictures to help improve creativity. Now, experts say adding little personal touches can help improve imagination and happiness.\par \par \uc2 MEGAN RYTE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) All great tips for taking your home office to the next level. For "Good Morning America," I'm Megan Ryte.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Great tip, thanks, Megan. And we will be right back.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 "GMA's" "Level Up Your life" sponsored by...\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Well, you saw it right there. That's the special, just slide it right in, airing tonight at 8:00 Eastern right here on ABC, "Truth and Lies: The Last Gangster," where you can see that new interview with the notorious mafia hitman, Sammy "The Bull" Gravano.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 This has been some 8:30 half-hour, and a reminder, you can always the ABC News app to watch "GMA," all of our reporting at ABC News. Have a great day, everyone.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Have you recovered, George?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220217ei1r0000u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PERSON OF THE WEEK HELPING AMERICAN WORKERS WITH SPECIAL NEED\b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 January 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, WINTER, STORM, SAFETY, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, MASK GUIDANCE, KECK, JHA, HOCHUL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW COVID MASK GUIDANCE\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, UKRAINE, INVASION, KIRBY, FALSE FLAG OPERATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRETEXT FOR RUSSIAN INVASION?\par \par \uc2 RHODES, ARREST, MOSELEY, CHARGES, RIOT, BRIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OATH KEEPERS LEADER IN COURT\par \par \uc2 FIRE, INVESTIGATION, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLEEING THE FLAMES\par \par \uc2 TRAIN, ROBBERY, BALDWIN, CELL PHONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRAIN CARGO THIEVES\par \par \uc2 FEDEX\uc2 , \uc2 FAA\uc2 , INFRARED LASER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 LANDIS, HOWDY HOMEMADE, JONES, CARRIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PERSON OF THE WEEK\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) It is never too cold for ice cream, especially when you meet our "Persons of the Week."\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, with the deep freeze moving in, the American workers who specialize in something frozen.\par \par \uc2 COLEMAN JONES (VICE PRESIDENT HOWDY HOMEMADE)\par \par \uc2 Hi, David Muir. Come on in.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coleman Jones first took us inside Howdy Homemade Ice Cream in Dallas, Texas more than three years ago. Thirty-four flavors.\par \par \uc2 CUSTOMER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 What's this one?\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Coffee and cookies.\par \par \uc2 CUSTOMER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Coffee and cookies, huh?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When they started, a dozen employees, all with special needs.\par \par \uc2 TOM LANDIS (FOUNDER HOWDY HOMEMADE)\par \par \uc2 It just jumped out that, hey, this is what the restaurant industry needs.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tom Landis, founder of Howdy Homemade, designing the store to give his workers a chance. Everything here is tailored made. Even the cash drawer, only bills, to help simplify transactions.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Four dollars is your change.\par \par \uc2 CHILD (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Annemarie Carrigan had trouble finding a job.\par \par \uc2 ANNEMARIE CARRIGAN (HOWDY HOMEMADE)\par \par \uc2 It makes me feel like there's not a place for me in this world.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her lesson for us all...\par \par \uc2 ANNEMARIE CARRIGAN (HOWDY HOMEMADE)\par \par \uc2 Never take no for an answer. Grab what you are passionate about and make it happen.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And that's what they've done, ever since.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hi, David Muir.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Howdy, David Muir.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Brant Urban (PH) and his favorite flavors.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Dr. Pepper chocolate chip. But little bit better is chocolate (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The new locations and new hires since we first met them. Now in Lubbock, Texas. Georgie, a new hire.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Howdy David Muir. It might be cold out there, but we might have some ice cream to warm your heart.\par \par \uc2 TOM LANDIS (FOUNDER HOWDY HOMEMADE)\par \par \uc2 Howdy, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Founder Tom back, too.\par \par \uc2 TOM LANDIS (FOUNDER HOWDY HOMEMADE)\par \par \uc2 Since y'all talked to us last time, we've had 281 franchise inquiries. We've signed 10 franchises. We're in 123 HEB grocery stores.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A grocery store chain in Texas, the workers' faces on every pint. And in North Carolina...\par \par \uc2 FAMILY (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Howdy, David Muir, from Asheville, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Brewer family opening their franchise, with the same mission.\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS OWNER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We are so excited to be opening a Howdy Homemade Ice Cream to provide jobs for adults with amazing, untapped abilities.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And tonight, we've learned soon in Indianapolis, too.\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS OWNER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Howdy, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Every new location, at least 15 new jobs. And tonight, from Indianapolis, their sales pitch, already.\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS OWNER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 It's really good ice cream. But don't take my word for that, David. Come grab a scoop.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) It's a deal. We love their mission and their ice cream. Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020220117ei1e00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUPERMARKET WORKERS ON STRIKE THOUSANDS WALK OUT OF \uc2 KROGER\uc2 -OWNED STORES\b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 January 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 INFLATION, ECONOMY, CUMMINGS, SWONK, DEESE, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INFLATION SOARS TO 40-YEAR HIGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. CONSUMER PRICES UP 7% OVER PAST YEAR\par \par \uc2 PROTEST, \uc2 KROGER\uc2 , WAGES, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMARKET WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OUT OF \uc2 KROGER\uc2 -OWNED STORES IN COLORADO\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All right, Robin, now to thousands of workers at \uc2 Kroger\uc2 -owned grocery stores in Colorado going on strike. Terry Moran is tracking the latest on the new walkout by fed-up workers. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good morning, Michael. This is another big one. This morning, more than 8,000 cashiers and store stockers and custodians and baggers and other grocery workers, they're all out on strike. At King Sooper Stores, more than 70 of them out in Colorado, they're seeking better wages and benefits and a safe for work environment at King Soopers, which is owned by \uc2 Kroger\uc2 's. These workers risked their lives during the pandemic. Many got COVID on the job as they kept stores open and food on our tables and they've seen King Soopers make record profits during this time.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXCERPT FROM UFCW - LOCAL 7 STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a statement, the union declaring, "We strike because it has become clear that this is the only way to get what is fair, just and equitable for the grocery workers."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXCERPT FROM \uc2 KROGER\uc2  STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The company in its statement responding, "We want what is right for our associates, workers, and that is more money in their paychecks while continuing to receive industry-leading health care benefits."\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) The Colorado strike is just the latest example of the new dynamic for workers across America. Successful strikes at John Deere, at \uc2 Kellogg's\uc2  and other major companies in recent months have shown that workers know that they have leverage for the first time in a long time in this tight labor market and they are willing to use it. Robin?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) They are. Terry, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220127ei1d00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NITA PROSE TALKS "THE MAID" AUTHOR OF JANUARY BOOK CLUB PICK\b0\par\par\uc2 1,447 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 January 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 INFLATION, ECONOMY, CUMMINGS, SWONK, DEESE, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INFLATION SOARS TO 40-YEAR HIGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. CONSUMER PRICES UP 7% OVER PAST YEAR\par \par \uc2 PROTEST, \uc2 KROGER\uc2 , WAGES, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMARKET WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OUT OF \uc2 KROGER\uc2 -OWNED STORES IN COLORADO\par \par \uc2 OMICRON, WADE, DELTA, SNYDER, ZHOU, WALKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ENCOURAGING NEW DATA ON OMICRON VARIANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: RISK OF DEATH 91% LOWER THAN FROM DELTA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, COVID-19, OMICRON\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, INVESTIGATION, CAPITOL RIOT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, SNOW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, APOLOGY, STRATTO, WILKIE, STARMER, LOCKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BORIS JOHNSON UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALLS FOR BRITISH PRIME MINISTER'S RESIGNATION OVER LOCKDOWN PARTY\par \par \uc2 SPECTOR, TRIBUTE, THE RONETTES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING RONNIE SPECTOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROUNDBREAKING LEAD SINGER OF "THE RONETTES" PASSES AWAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 PRINCE ANDREW, SEXUAL ASSAULT, GIUFFRE, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRINCE ANDREW IN THE CROSSHAIRS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE SAYS SEXUAL ASSAULT LAWSUIT AGAINST QUEEN'S SON CAN PROCEED\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, REED, SHOOTING, KENNEY, "RUST"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW LAWSUIT OVER FATAL FILM SET SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "RUST" ARMORER SUES COMPANY THAT PROVIDED GUNS & AMMUNITION\par \par \uc2 TIKTOK, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, PRICE, INCREASE, SPENDING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INFLATION SOARS TO 40-YEAR HIGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. CONSUMER PRICES UP 7% OVER PAST YEAR\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, GROCERY, WORKERS, \uc2 KROGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMARKET WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OUT OF \uc2 KROGER\uc2 -OWNED STORES IN CO\par \par \uc2 COVID, OMICRON, DELTA, STUDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ENCOURAGING NEW DATA ON OMICRON VARIANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: RISK OF DEATH 91% LOWER THAN FROM DELTA\par \par \uc2 SPECTOR, SAG AWARDS, COACHELLA\par \par \uc2 RED CROSS, BLOOD, LASKY, JAMISON, ANDREWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL BLOOD SHORTAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RED CROSS SOUNDS ALARM ON CRISIS\par \par \uc2 JOB, SEARCH, INTERNET, ADVICE, PARSLEY, MCCASKILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEVEL UP YOUR JOB SEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU CAN FIND A BETTER JOB RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 SLIPPERS, TOOTHBRUSH, GLASSES, PADS, SHOES, LEGGINGS\par \par \uc2 QUAID, "SCREAM", MOVIE, ACTOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JACK QUAID LIVE ON GMA\par \par \uc2 REID, FASHION, 2022, TRENDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 2022 FASHION FORECAST\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS, THRIFTING, ENTREPRENEUR, SMALL, WICKER, SCHNEIDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FROM PASSION TO PROFIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN TURNS LOVE OF THRIFTING INTO BUSINESS\par \par \uc2 PROSE, "THE MAID", BOOK, AUTHOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NITA PROSE TALKS "THE MAID"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-ON-ONE WITH AUTHOR OF JANUARY BOOK CLUB PICK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We are back now with our January "GMA" Book Club pick. It is "The Maid" by Nita Prose, an instant "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 " bestseller. Amy got a chance to sat down with the author, and Amy, people are just, they're really enjoying this book.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) They really are Robin. In fact, I'm included. I did not put this book down. I read it in two days. It was incredible, and it's also remarkable considering this is Nita's debut novel. I had so much fun talking to her about her, this is my favorite, hopeful murder mystery.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Behind the beautiful fa\u231\'00\'E7ade of the five-star Regency Grand Hotel lies a dirty secret and one that Molly the maid, at the center of Nita Prose's debut novel, unexpectedly finds herself cleaning up.\par \par \uc2 NITA PROSE ("THE MAID")\par \par \uc2 Molly stumbles across a infamous guest who is very dead, like really, really dead, in his bed. But the mystery can only be solved through a connection to the human heart.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) You have gotten rave reviews. What do you make of the reaction to "The Maid"?\par \par \uc2 NITA PROSE ("THE MAID")\par \par \uc2 I think it's interesting. This book has a sort of Agatha Christie feel about it but maybe with a little bit of the sensibility of the film, "Knives Out," and a smattering of the board game, "Clue." Is it the bartender with a knife in the kitchen or is the maid with a pillow in the bedroom? So I think that whodunit feeling is really appealing to people.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We made the announcements that you were the "GMA" Book Club pick. I got a big laugh from the anchors when I said it's a hopeful, heartwarming murder mystery.\par \par \uc2 NITA PROSE ("THE MAID")\par \par \uc2 I know.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Who would have ever thunk of that? How did you come up with that?\par \par \uc2 NITA PROSE ("THE MAID")\par \par \uc2 Well, I was on a business trip, and I came back into my hotel room, opened the door, and completely startled the room maid, who was cleaning it. And I remember her sort of jumping back into a shadowy corner, and I just looked at her, and I thought, what an intimate and invisible job it is to be a room maid. You know, she'd been cleaning my room for days, and she knew so much about me, but what did I know about her?\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) "The Maid's" premise as unique as its protagonist, Molly.\par \par \uc2 NITA PROSE ("THE MAID")\par \par \uc2 Molly is a really interesting person. She, you know, really struggles with social cues, and she's a bit of a misfit, and yet she's so diligent. She loves her job in the service industry. However, it's as though she's invisible. I really wanted the reader to step into that experience.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) There's a lot of research you've done throughout your life at led you to be able to create such a complex character.\par \par \uc2 NITA PROSE ("THE MAID")\par \par \uc2 I worked with special needs students. And when I would take them out on a field trip, sometimes they were treated so badly, it was really hard for me to watch. However, the amazing thing that happened was I got to see these students be more resilient, more capable of change, more able to bounce back than so-called normative people, and I wanted a little bit of that flavor in Molly.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) "The Maid" already set to the hit the big screen with Florence Pugh executive producing and starring as Molly.\par \par \uc2 NITA PROSE ("THE MAID")\par \par \uc2 I don't think I could be happier, and I don't think we could find a better Molly than her. I think she's going to be absolutely brilliant.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Do you see any other actors that we might know in supporting roles?\par \par \uc2 NITA PROSE ("THE MAID")\par \par \uc2 I keep seeing Stanley Tucci as Mr. Snow. There is a very officious sort of hotel manager in the book.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) With an ending you'll never see coming, Prose hopes Molly the maid leaves a lasting impression on readers.\par \par \uc2 NITA PROSE ("THE MAID")\par \par \uc2 I really hope that when you step away from this book, you have a special empathy for those who are different. There are moments in the book where we might feel really, you know, sad for Molly. But don't you worry, readers. By the time you get to the end, you will see that she is a very strong young lady.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) She is, indeed. "The Maid" is out now, and you can go to our website to find a free copy in a Free Little Library near you. And if you're in Times Square, well, you can just come by and scan the QR code in our studio window, and you can read an excerpt with that. And as always, be sure to keep reading along with us on our \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , @GMAbookclub. You guys, you've got to read it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Amy, did you, did you see this on the book jacket? Because Michael picked it out, pointed it out. "Nita Prose, longtime editor," blah, blah, blah, blah, "she lives in a house that is only moderately clean."\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) That's all of us, right?\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I love that.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) She sounds like hoot.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) She was so much fun to talk to. She really was such a personality, and we hope there are more books coming from her.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good for her. Good for her. Thanks, Amy. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 In remembering and celebrating Ronnie Spector, we've been playing this all morning long. So we thought, why not end this way, "Be My Baby."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That's right.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We were singing along earlier. It didn't go so well.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 So we're going to let Ronnie sing it.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 There you go.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Thank you guys for watching. Everybody, have a great day.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220127ei1d0000u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUPERMARKET WORKERS ON STRIKE THOUSANDS WALK OUT OF \uc2 KROGER\uc2 -OWNED STORES IN CO\b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 January 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 INFLATION, ECONOMY, CUMMINGS, SWONK, DEESE, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INFLATION SOARS TO 40-YEAR HIGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. CONSUMER PRICES UP 7% OVER PAST YEAR\par \par \uc2 PROTEST, \uc2 KROGER\uc2 , WAGES, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMARKET WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OUT OF \uc2 KROGER\uc2 -OWNED STORES IN COLORADO\par \par \uc2 OMICRON, WADE, DELTA, SNYDER, ZHOU, WALKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ENCOURAGING NEW DATA ON OMICRON VARIANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: RISK OF DEATH 91% LOWER THAN FROM DELTA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, COVID-19, OMICRON\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, INVESTIGATION, CAPITOL RIOT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, SNOW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, APOLOGY, STRATTO, WILKIE, STARMER, LOCKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BORIS JOHNSON UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALLS FOR BRITISH PRIME MINISTER'S RESIGNATION OVER LOCKDOWN PARTY\par \par \uc2 SPECTOR, TRIBUTE, THE RONETTES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING RONNIE SPECTOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROUNDBREAKING LEAD SINGER OF "THE RONETTES" PASSES AWAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 PRINCE ANDREW, SEXUAL ASSAULT, GIUFFRE, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRINCE ANDREW IN THE CROSSHAIRS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE SAYS SEXUAL ASSAULT LAWSUIT AGAINST QUEEN'S SON CAN PROCEED\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, REED, SHOOTING, KENNEY, "RUST"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW LAWSUIT OVER FATAL FILM SET SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "RUST" ARMORER SUES COMPANY THAT PROVIDED GUNS & AMMUNITION\par \par \uc2 TIKTOK, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, PRICE, INCREASE, SPENDING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INFLATION SOARS TO 40-YEAR HIGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. CONSUMER PRICES UP 7% OVER PAST YEAR\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, GROCERY, WORKERS, \uc2 KROGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMARKET WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OUT OF \uc2 KROGER\uc2 -OWNED STORES IN CO\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We do turn now to thousands of supermarket workers on strike at \uc2 Kroger\uc2 -owned grocery stores in Colorado. Let's go back to Terry Moran with more this morning. Terry, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good morning, Whit. This morning, more than 8,000 grocery workers are out on strike at more than 70 King Soopers stores in Colorado, that chain owned by \uc2 Kroger\uc2 . The workers are seeking better wages and better health care, and they're also seeking a safer work environment. During the pandemic, they kept stores open in a dangerous time. Many of them got COVID before vaccines and treatments. King Soopers, they made record profits. So now the workers want a bigger share of all that money.\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) In a statement, the union declaring, "This is the only way to get what is fair, just and equitable," and the company responding in a statement, "We want what is right for our associates, and that is more money in their paychecks and industry-leading health care benefits." This strike, coming after successful strikes at John Deere and \uc2 Kellogg's\uc2  and other major American companies, is just another sign of a new militant spirit out there. American workers are on the march. Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All right, new spirit indeed, Terry, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220127ei1d0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FROM PASSION TO PROFIT WOMAN TURNS LOVE OF THRIFTING INTO BUSINESS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,091 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 January 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 INFLATION, ECONOMY, CUMMINGS, SWONK, DEESE, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INFLATION SOARS TO 40-YEAR HIGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. CONSUMER PRICES UP 7% OVER PAST YEAR\par \par \uc2 PROTEST, \uc2 KROGER\uc2 , WAGES, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMARKET WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OUT OF \uc2 KROGER\uc2 -OWNED STORES IN COLORADO\par \par \uc2 OMICRON, WADE, DELTA, SNYDER, ZHOU, WALKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ENCOURAGING NEW DATA ON OMICRON VARIANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: RISK OF DEATH 91% LOWER THAN FROM DELTA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, COVID-19, OMICRON\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, INVESTIGATION, CAPITOL RIOT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, SNOW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, APOLOGY, STRATTO, WILKIE, STARMER, LOCKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BORIS JOHNSON UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALLS FOR BRITISH PRIME MINISTER'S RESIGNATION OVER LOCKDOWN PARTY\par \par \uc2 SPECTOR, TRIBUTE, THE RONETTES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING RONNIE SPECTOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROUNDBREAKING LEAD SINGER OF "THE RONETTES" PASSES AWAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 PRINCE ANDREW, SEXUAL ASSAULT, GIUFFRE, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRINCE ANDREW IN THE CROSSHAIRS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE SAYS SEXUAL ASSAULT LAWSUIT AGAINST QUEEN'S SON CAN PROCEED\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, REED, SHOOTING, KENNEY, "RUST"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW LAWSUIT OVER FATAL FILM SET SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "RUST" ARMORER SUES COMPANY THAT PROVIDED GUNS & AMMUNITION\par \par \uc2 TIKTOK, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, PRICE, INCREASE, SPENDING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INFLATION SOARS TO 40-YEAR HIGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. CONSUMER PRICES UP 7% OVER PAST YEAR\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, GROCERY, WORKERS, \uc2 KROGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMARKET WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OUT OF \uc2 KROGER\uc2 -OWNED STORES IN CO\par \par \uc2 COVID, OMICRON, DELTA, STUDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ENCOURAGING NEW DATA ON OMICRON VARIANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: RISK OF DEATH 91% LOWER THAN FROM DELTA\par \par \uc2 SPECTOR, SAG AWARDS, COACHELLA\par \par \uc2 RED CROSS, BLOOD, LASKY, JAMISON, ANDREWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL BLOOD SHORTAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RED CROSS SOUNDS ALARM ON CRISIS\par \par \uc2 JOB, SEARCH, INTERNET, ADVICE, PARSLEY, MCCASKILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEVEL UP YOUR JOB SEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU CAN FIND A BETTER JOB RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 SLIPPERS, TOOTHBRUSH, GLASSES, PADS, SHOES, LEGGINGS\par \par \uc2 QUAID, "SCREAM", MOVIE, ACTOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JACK QUAID LIVE ON GMA\par \par \uc2 REID, FASHION, 2022, TRENDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 2022 FASHION FORECAST\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS, THRIFTING, ENTREPRENEUR, SMALL, WICKER, SCHNEIDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FROM PASSION TO PROFIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN TURNS LOVE OF THRIFTING INTO BUSINESS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All right, we are turning now to leveling up your small business. So many people have turned their passions into their professions over the past few years, and Lara has a story of an Arizona woman who did just that. Hey, Lara, good morning.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Hey, Whit, good morning to you guys again, and, you know, we share a love of thrifting and upcycling, the woman and I that you're about to meet, in a big way. And she's made quite a business of it. This segment is sponsored by GoDaddy, which helps everyday entrepreneurs grow their businesses, and in this case it was all about turning clicks into cash.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In 2019 Sara Small took her passion for thrifting and turned it into a purpose.\par \par \uc2 SARA SMALL (WICKER GODDESS)\par \par \uc2 We restained it to match the body and touched up a few small spots.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Breathing new life into vintage pieces like these and selling them on social media.\par \par \uc2 SARA SMALL (WICKER GODDESS)\par \par \uc2 People just really related to what we were offering, and I finally felt that I was really doing what I was supposed to be doing.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TURNING FANS INTO CUSTOMERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPAND SOCIAL PRESENCE WITH ONLINE STOREFRONT\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sara's business, Wicker Goddess, offering her carefully curated collection of refurbished furniture, home goods, handmade prints and more to customers both online and here, at her boutique in Phoenix.\par \par \uc2 SARA SMALL (WICKER GODDESS)\par \par \uc2 We know that this is helping the environment, helping the Earth, and it's also giving someone something that is exciting for their space.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Over the past two years, Sara's sales have doubled, thanks in part to our sponsor GoDaddy, who helped her build her website and boost her business.\par \par \uc2 SARA SMALL (WICKER GODDESS)\par \par \uc2 It gives me two streams of revenue, which is what you're hopeful for as an entrepreneur, that you have an online site people can access, they're ordering from all over the world, and then you also have your in-person offerings.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Experts say the key to small business success is reaching customers online.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA SCHNEIDER (GODADDY)\par \par \uc2 Over the course of the past couple of years, we've seen a 60 percent increase in the number of online sellers in the US. The pandemic really created a new normal in terms of how consumers want to shop.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) There are simple ways to level up your online presence. First, turn you fans into your advocates.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA SCHNEIDER (GODADDY)\par \par \uc2 You can offer a discount to friends and family and initial customers that are coming in and using your product and loving it in order to get them to write a great review for you.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Next, stay in touch with your loyal customers.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA SCHNEIDER (GODADDY)\par \par \uc2 Send them an email with a discount, create an email newsletter that talks to them about things that you're learning and things you're doing with your brand.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Finally streamline your sales by using a tool to help track every purchase.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA SCHNEIDER (GODADDY)\par \par \uc2 GoDaddy's commerce solutions are built to help you sell anything anywhere. With the GoDaddy Smart Terminal, we really created a one-stop shop where you can connect all of your sales offline to online, that it saves you time and helps you more effectively manage your business.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) These strategies have helped Sara transform her favorite hobby into a growing, thriving brand.\par \par \uc2 SARA SMALL (WICKER GODDESS)\par \par \uc2 As an entrepreneur, we're so hard focused on our local community and making sure people know our name that we forget an entire world exists outside of that, and they really opened my eyes to that.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Wicker Goddess, she sure is. Sara started the business by selling furniture and home goods that she bought as decorations for her own wedding, and then she just kept doing it because it was so much fun. Love that story, Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That's right, pursuing her passion. All right, Lara, thank you so much. And coming up here, the author of our January Book Club pick, "The Maid," a murder mystery unlike any you've ever read before. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 "GMA" Level Up your Life is sponsored by...\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220127ei1d0000t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LEVEL UP YOUR JOB SEARCH HOW YOU CAN FIND A BETTER JOB RIGHT NOW\b0\par\par\uc2 925 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 January 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 INFLATION, ECONOMY, CUMMINGS, SWONK, DEESE, PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INFLATION SOARS TO 40-YEAR HIGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. CONSUMER PRICES UP 7% OVER PAST YEAR\par \par \uc2 PROTEST, \uc2 KROGER\uc2 , WAGES, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMARKET WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OUT OF \uc2 KROGER\uc2 -OWNED STORES IN COLORADO\par \par \uc2 OMICRON, WADE, DELTA, SNYDER, ZHOU, WALKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ENCOURAGING NEW DATA ON OMICRON VARIANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: RISK OF DEATH 91% LOWER THAN FROM DELTA\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, COVID-19, OMICRON\par \par \uc2 MCCARTHY, INVESTIGATION, CAPITOL RIOT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, SNOW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, APOLOGY, STRATTO, WILKIE, STARMER, LOCKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BORIS JOHNSON UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALLS FOR BRITISH PRIME MINISTER'S RESIGNATION OVER LOCKDOWN PARTY\par \par \uc2 SPECTOR, TRIBUTE, THE RONETTES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING RONNIE SPECTOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROUNDBREAKING LEAD SINGER OF "THE RONETTES" PASSES AWAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 PRINCE ANDREW, SEXUAL ASSAULT, GIUFFRE, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRINCE ANDREW IN THE CROSSHAIRS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE SAYS SEXUAL ASSAULT LAWSUIT AGAINST QUEEN'S SON CAN PROCEED\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, REED, SHOOTING, KENNEY, "RUST"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW LAWSUIT OVER FATAL FILM SET SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "RUST" ARMORER SUES COMPANY THAT PROVIDED GUNS & AMMUNITION\par \par \uc2 TIKTOK, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, PRICE, INCREASE, SPENDING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INFLATION SOARS TO 40-YEAR HIGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. CONSUMER PRICES UP 7% OVER PAST YEAR\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, GROCERY, WORKERS, \uc2 KROGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERMARKET WORKERS ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS WALK OUT OF \uc2 KROGER\uc2 -OWNED STORES IN CO\par \par \uc2 COVID, OMICRON, DELTA, STUDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ENCOURAGING NEW DATA ON OMICRON VARIANT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: RISK OF DEATH 91% LOWER THAN FROM DELTA\par \par \uc2 SPECTOR, SAG AWARDS, COACHELLA\par \par \uc2 RED CROSS, BLOOD, LASKY, JAMISON, ANDREWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL BLOOD SHORTAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RED CROSS SOUNDS ALARM ON CRISIS\par \par \uc2 JOB, SEARCH, INTERNET, ADVICE, PARSLEY, MCCASKILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEVEL UP YOUR JOB SEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW YOU CAN FIND A BETTER JOB RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) It is time to level up. This morning, it's all about the job hunt. According to a survey by Resume Builder, one in four American workers plans to quit their jobs this year. Rebecca Jarvis is back with expert tips on how to land the gig you really want. Good morning again, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Hi, Robin. And this is really a job seeker's market. A record 4.5 million Americans voluntarily quit their jobs in the month of November in search of something new, and there are one and a, one and a half job openings for everybody who's out of work. Here's how you can take advantage.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After four years of working in health care, Philadelphia native Sierra Parsley is ready to change her career. Her goal, find a new job in IT.\par \par \uc2 CIERRA PARSLEY (IT WORKER)\par \par \uc2 I am looking into project management. However, I have so many transferable skills that I'm looking to go anywhere.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But her search hasn't been exactly fruitful. After six months and about 20 job applications, she's only scored one phone interview.\par \par \uc2 CIERRA PARSLEY (IT WORKER)\par \par \uc2 I'm basically overwhelmed. I'm not getting any calls back.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So we enlisted the help of LinkedIn career expert Andrew McCaskill, who had the chance to review some of Cierra's most pressing questions.\par \par \uc2 CIERRA PARSLEY (IT WORKER)\par \par \uc2 I would love to know if there is anything else that I could do to get my foot in the door.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW MCCASKILL (LINKEDIN)\par \par \uc2 Cierra is doing so many of the right things. She's got a great picture on her LinkedIn profile. She's got her skills highlighted there. One of the things that I think that she should do is look at hashtag #opentowork. That alerts all recruiters that, hey, I'm looking for a new opportunity.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her next question?\par \par \uc2 CIERRA PARSLEY (IT WORKER)\par \par \uc2 What's the best way to start networking?\par \par \uc2 ANDREW MCCASKILL (LINKEDIN)\par \par \uc2 One is get a warm introduction from somebody that you already know. Secondly, be specific with the ask when you do make that connection. Busy people need specificity. Third, refresh their memory. Point out something that you've got in common.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And finally, how to get that response. Andrew says persistence is key.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW MCCASKILL (LINKEDIN)\par \par \uc2 Being first to respond, being highly responsive to a recruiter, sending a follow-up note, all of those things still really, really matter.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Those are all great tips. Now Rebecca, many, if not most, people, as you know, are networking and interviewing virtually. So how should a job hunter prepare for that type of remote meeting?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So you're going to prepare for it, Robin, much like you would if you were doing it in person. But one thing to keep in mind is test your technology, make sure it's working, and be prepared if you have to troubleshoot in the interview to do that. Practice with a friend. And finally, follow up with a note. The most important thing to consider there is obviously spelling and everything has to be on point, but don't let the perfect be the enemy of the good. Send the note either way, and send it quickly after the interview, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I cannot stress enough, and I'm glad that you and our other expert, follow up, follow up, follow up. That is so, so key. All right, Rebecca, thank you. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All right, thank you, Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220127ei1d0000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RECORD NUMBER OF AMERICANS QUITTING THEIR JOBS LABOR DEPT: MORE THAN 10 MILLION JOB OPENINGS IN NOVEMBER\b0\par\par\uc2 943 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 January 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSES CANCELED\par \par \uc2 COVID, CTU, SCHOOLS, LIGHTFOOT, DISPUTES\par \par \uc2 OMICRON, SURGE, CDC, TESTS, JHA, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 CHINA, COVID, OLYMPICS, LOCKDOWN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, SNOW, ICE, WINDS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, NAZARBAYEV, GAS PRICES, PUTIN, KAZAKHSTAN\par \par \uc2 INSURRECTION, COMMITTEE, HANNITY, TEXTS\par \par \uc2 RIOTERS, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , SEARCH, CAPITOL, BOMBS, D'ANTUONO\par \par \uc2 JOBS, QUITTING, CONSUMERS, EMPLOYERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WIND CHILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE ARCTIC AIR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HOLMES, TRIAL, GUILTY, JURY, KEW, KAATZ\par \par \uc2 DJOKOVIC, AUSTRALIAN OPEN, UNVACCINATED, TILEY\par \par \uc2 GOLDEN GLOBES, HFPA, BOYCOTT, MALKIN, DIVERSITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSES CANCELED\par \par \uc2 COVID, SCHOOLS, TEACHERS, STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 OMICRON, SURGE, TESTING, HOSPITALS\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, SNOW, ICY, TEMPS\par \par \uc2 JOBS, QUITTING, OPENINGS, INDUSTRIES, RAISE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I can't believe it's 25 years since the first one. But we have our "GMA" cover story right now. The record number of people quitting their jobs, 4.5 million in the month of November. That's according to new statistics just out from the Labor Department. That couple with the historically high number of job openings means this could be the best time ever to find a new job and ask for a raise. Rebecca Jarvis is back with us yet again. All right, Rebecca, so let's get right to it. Which industries are losing the most people right now?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD NUMBER OF AMERICANS QUITTING THEIR JOBS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LABOR DEPT: MORE THAN 10 MILLION JOB OPENINGS IN NOVEMBER\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Well, you said it at the top, Robin. This is a job seekers market but people are also burnt out, and the places that are really losing the most workers are where it's required to be in person. So industries like accommodation and food services, people who work at restaurants, health care, they've been so burnt out by the pandemic. Transportation warehousing and utilities, Robin, are the places that are shedding the jobs the fastest, people are opting out and going elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD NUMBER OF AMERICANS QUITTING THEIR JOBS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT INDUSTRIES ARE DOING THE MOST HIRING NOW?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) There are a lot of openings right now, so who's doing the most hiring right now?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah, I mean, there's also a lot of hiring taking place, and in particular if you're looking in the travel industry, if you're interested in recreation, if you're interest in software and IT services, those are jobs that can be done remotely by and large, they're hiring. Corporate services, finance and hardware and networking. Basically, Robin, if you're looking for work, a lot of places are hiring. You just have to make sure you're optimized.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And can you give folks some advice on how to get the best offer?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DREAM JOB MARKET?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NOW IS THE TIME TO LOOK FOR A NEW JOB\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah, look, when you go out and you're hunting for work, oftentimes there's going be this question, do I talk right off the bat about money? The answer is, probably no in most cases, not starting that conversation about money. If you're asked how much money would you like to make, the best answer you can give is, I'd like to make in line with what the industry is paying right now, and I think what I bring to this job is top of the line, so you can think about me as a top of the line candidate.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) But don't necessarily go out and be specific with those numbers, because you can either set yourself backwards, you set a number out there, maybe they're willing to pay you more or you can keep yourself out of the pool because you gone too high right off the bat.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DREAM JOB MARKET?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHY NOW IS A GREAT TIME TO ASK FOR A RAISE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) That is great advice right there. Also, we know that not everybody is looking for a new job. But maybe, you know, maybe they know that they deserve a raise, so can you help folks out there?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I mean, Robin, I don't know anybody who doesn't think they deserve a raise. But here's the bottom line with that. When you go and look for a raise, when you go to your boss and you ask for a raise, you want to walk in that room with facts. What have you done for the business? Talk to them about how much you love your job, the things you've accomplished in the last year. Set it up as a meeting, you can do it over Zoom, but in person if you can get in person, that's usually a better thing.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And then finally, fortunately, you often have to be prepared to leave in order to get the best offer. But you really do have to be prepared to leave if you put that on the table, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Well that is your third appearance on "Good Morning America," so you are deserving of a raise. You march in there and you say.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Love it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Okay.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I'm not quitting, but I'll take the money.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) There you go. Tell them Robin sent you. Okay, thanks, Rebecca. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220110ei150000j\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/10/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Source\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 ABC Network - All sources\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trga